    <node id="paper-0001::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">MBSE creates a system model that integrates discipline-specific engineering models/simulations and provides a cohesive, consistent source of requirements, design, analysis, and verification across development.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Generic system-level MBSE model as authoritative integrated repository.", "claim_text": "MBSE creates a system model that integrates discipline-specific engineering models/simulations and provides a cohesive, consistent source of requirements, design, analysis, and verification across development.", "evidence_source": "MBSE creates a system model that helps integrate other discipline specific engineering models and simulations. The system level model is initiated at the start of a project and evolves throughout development. It provides a cohesive and consistent source of system requirements, design, analysis, and verification.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "No metric for the broad claim.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Expected cohesion and consistency of system information; not empirically measured as a generic claim.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[0].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0001", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "This is a general MBSE rationale, not a measured effect of the RAX implementation."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0001::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">The RAX executable MBSE representation integrates SysML architecture/behavior with MATLAB analytical models and STK simulation through ModelCenter/MBSE Analyzer, enabling execution of behavior and parametric models for subsystem functions/states.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "MagicDraw SysML model, ModelCenter workflows, MBSE Analyzer bridge, CST time-stepped behavioral simulation.", "claim_text": "The RAX executable MBSE representation integrates SysML architecture/behavior with MATLAB analytical models and STK simulation through ModelCenter/MBSE Analyzer, enabling execution of behavior and parametric models for subsystem functions/states.", "evidence_source": "ModelCenter was used to integrate the analytical and simulation models. The integrated analyses were linked to the SysML model using MBSE Analyzer, a bridge between SysML tools and ModelCenter. Behavioral models were executed for a representative RAX mission to study energy state and data collection capabilities.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Executable time-stepped system-state histories; no productivity metric.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "The integrated toolchain executed RAX mission behavior and parametric analyses and collected time histories.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[0].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0001", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Execution is shown for one prototype mission model using proprietary tools; no independent replication or scalability measurement."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0001::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">Time-history simulation helps understand and verify coupled energy collection and data-download behavior in the CubeSat model.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "RunOperation/UpdateStates activity execution, CubeSatMission states, UpdateEnergy/UpdateDownload parametrics, time-history plots.", "claim_text": "Time-history simulation helps understand and verify coupled energy collection and data-download behavior in the CubeSat model.", "evidence_source": "The time history plots show that the integrated RAX model correctly models the behavior of energy collection and data download, and their interactions.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Energy state over time, Sun/download states, downloaded data over time.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "A late energy dip while in sunlight is explained by simultaneous data transmission, supporting internal behavioral consistency of power/data interactions.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[0].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0001", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The 'correctly models' claim is based on internal plausibility, not comparison with flight telemetry or independent validation."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0001::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">Integrated MBSE enables verification of the impact of design decisions on mission requirements throughout the entire mission, beyond standalone STK/MATLAB analysis practice.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SysML satisfy relationships from requirements to Vehicle properties calculated by mission simulation; RAX requirements verification diagram.", "claim_text": "Integrated MBSE enables verification of the impact of design decisions on mission requirements throughout the entire mission, beyond standalone STK/MATLAB analysis practice.", "evidence_source": "In the current practice of satellite design, tools such as STK and MATLAB are used to analyze mission performance. However, there is no readily available capability that enables verifying the impact of design decisions on mission requirements throughout the entire mission. The integrated model demonstrates how to accomplish this by performing mission simulations using MBSE models.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Minimum energy limit, max battery/data capacity, minimum downloaded data per day.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Requirements were checked using simulation outputs during solar-panel, battery, orbit, and ground-station trade studies.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[0].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0001", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The comparator is described qualitatively rather than tested; requirement checks are limited to modeled energy/data requirements."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0001::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">Solar-panel area trade study supports EPS design decision-making by showing nominal and half-size panels satisfy the energy requirement while quarter-size panels are too small.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "PowerCollection and UpdateEnergy parametric analyses; solar-panel area design instances; energy lower-bound requirement.", "claim_text": "Solar-panel area trade study supports EPS design decision-making by showing nominal and half-size panels satisfy the energy requirement while quarter-size panels are too small.", "evidence_source": "When the solar panel area was reduced further, to a quarter of the nominal, the energy level went below the required minimum at the end of the simulation... The results clearly show that the quarter size solar panel is too small for the mission.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "On-board energy level versus 92,000 J minimum bound and 115,000 J max battery capacity.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Quarter-size solar panel falls below the required minimum by the end of the simulation; half-size and nominal remain within bounds.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[0].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0001", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Results depend on simplified power/mission assumptions and a prototype RAX model not intended to be accurate to the real satellite."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0001::claim-06">
      <data key="d2">Battery-capacity trade study identifies energy spillover at reduced battery capacity and suggests possible solar-panel downsizing.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "UpdateEnergy parametric diagram; max battery capacity design instances; energy time-history plot.", "claim_text": "Battery-capacity trade study identifies energy spillover at reduced battery capacity and suggests possible solar-panel downsizing.", "evidence_source": "When the battery capacity was reduced, energy level could not rise above the max capacity of 100,000 J. This shows that there will be spillover of energy collected by solar panel, and it may be considered to reduce the size of the solar panel.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "On-board energy level and max capacity/spillover behavior.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Reduced capacity caps energy at 100,000 J, indicating collected energy spillover and a possible reason to reduce solar-panel size.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[0].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "study_id": "paper-0001", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The potential cost/size benefit is inferred by authors and not evaluated with mass, cost, degradation, or reliability models."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0001::claim-07">
      <data key="d2">Orbit-altitude and ground-station network trade studies support mission design by estimating downloaded-data performance and checking data-downlink requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "GetStates, UpdateData, UpdateDownload analyses; STK ground-station/orbit opportunities; daily downloaded-data requirement.", "claim_text": "Orbit-altitude and ground-station network trade studies support mission design by estimating downloaded-data performance and checking data-downlink requirements.", "evidence_source": "The nominal configuration using Ann Arbor and Menlo Park stations collected about 3.9 MB of data during 24 hours... Nonetheless, all three configurations satisfy the system requirement that 'the system shall download at least 1MB of data per day'.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Cumulative downloaded data in MB over 24 hours; requirement at least 1 MB/day.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "High orbit and alternative ground-station networks collect more data; all studied ground-station configurations satisfy the 1 MB/day requirement.", "source_claim_id": "C7", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[0].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[6]", "study_id": "paper-0001", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Trade results depend on simplified communication efficiency and selected station/orbit scenarios; financial cost is acknowledged but not modeled."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0001::claim-08">
      <data key="d2">The RAX CubeSat model and manual are intended for academic release and can serve as a starting point for CubeSat teams to develop their own models and trade studies.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "RAX CubeSat model based on published CubeSat reference model; planned model/manual release.", "claim_text": "The RAX CubeSat model and manual are intended for academic release and can serve as a starting point for CubeSat teams to develop their own models and trade studies.", "evidence_source": "The RAX CubeSat model will be made available to the academic community for further study and potential extension for more complex missions.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Planned availability and prospective use; no actual reuse count.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Potential reuse as a starting model is claimed, not demonstrated across teams.", "source_claim_id": "C8", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[0].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[7]", "study_id": "paper-0001", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The paper reports planned availability, not actual release, adoption, or replication evidence."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0001::claim-09">
      <data key="d2">The work demonstrates the power, scalability, and utility of available MBSE tools and methods for increasingly complex spacecraft missions.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Overall integrated executable RAX demonstration using COTS MBSE tools.", "claim_text": "The work demonstrates the power, scalability, and utility of available MBSE tools and methods for increasingly complex spacecraft missions.", "evidence_source": "This work was undertaken to demonstrate the power, scalability, and utility of MBSE tools and methods that are available to help meet the challenge of designing spacecraft missions of ever-increasing complexity.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "No scalability or utility metric is reported.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "A single executable CubeSat mission model is demonstrated; scalability is not measured.", "source_claim_id": "C9", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[0].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[8]", "study_id": "paper-0001", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "A one-case prototype cannot establish scalability; tool utility may be influenced by vendor-specific capabilities and expert users."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0002::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">Compared with a traditional document-based approach, MBSE/model-centric development can enhance communications, reduce development risk, improve quality, and enhance knowledge transfer; the system model serves as a single source of truth.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "model-centric system model / single-source-of-truth", "claim_text": "Compared with a traditional document-based approach, MBSE/model-centric development can enhance communications, reduce development risk, improve quality, and enhance knowledge transfer; the system model serves as a single source of truth.", "evidence_source": "Abstract: 'Some of the benefits of using an MBSE approach over a traditional document-based approach are: enhanced communications, reduced development risk, improved quality, and enhanced knowledge transfer [1].' Section 2: 'the model serves as a single-source-of-truth for the development team'.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative benefit asserted; no measured effect size.", "quote_location": "Abstract and Section 2, Model-Based Systems Engineering", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[1].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0002", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["The benefits are imported from a general MBSE reference and not evaluated for this CubeSat method.", "No CubeSat-specific baseline, metric, or stakeholder validation is reported."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0002::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">The eight-step approach provides a repeatable, generalized method for CubeSat development teams and complements the INCOSE SSWG CubeSat Reference Model.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "eight-step workflow; CubeSat Reference Model examples; requirements/use-case/activity model elements", "claim_text": "The eight-step approach provides a repeatable, generalized method for CubeSat development teams and complements the INCOSE SSWG CubeSat Reference Model.", "evidence_source": "Abstract: 'This approach provides a repeatable, generalized method for CubeSat development teams to follow...' Introduction: the approach 'draws from existing methodologies to provide a repeatable, generalized method for university teams'.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative: method is presented as repeatable/generalized; no reuse count or replication across missions is reported.", "quote_location": "Abstract; Introduction", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[1].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0002", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["Examples are illustrative and limited to mission data collection/distribution.", "No evidence that independent teams reused the method or reference model successfully."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0002::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">The approach creates clear traceability from mission requirements to required functionality.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Figure 1 requirements diagram; Figure 9 use case diagram with activity refine links; activity hierarchy", "claim_text": "The approach creates clear traceability from mission requirements to required functionality.", "evidence_source": "Conclusion: 'Traceability: There is clear traceability from the mission requirements to the functionality required to satisfy those requirements.' Step 7: 'This approach uses the refine relationship... for relating the activities to use cases.'", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative: visible refine links demonstrate a trace path in the example model; no trace coverage metric reported.", "quote_location": "Step 2, Step 7, Conclusion", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[1].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0002", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["Traceability is shown for two example mission requirements/use cases, not a full mission requirements set.", "No verification of completeness or trace correctness by stakeholders/tools is reported."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0002::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">Recursive activity decomposition can be applied at all mission hierarchy levels, producing a functional architecture/activity hierarchy that satisfies mission requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "activity diagrams and BDD activity hierarchy for Collect Mission Data, including Figure 14", "claim_text": "Recursive activity decomposition can be applied at all mission hierarchy levels, producing a functional architecture/activity hierarchy that satisfies mission requirements.", "evidence_source": "Step 8: 'The decomposition of activities into actions can continue down to the subsystem-level of the CubeSat. The end result can be shown in an activity hierarchy representing the full functional decomposition and the resulting functional architecture.' Conclusion: 'Recursive: The approach can be recursively applied at all levels of the mission hierarchy...'", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative: example hierarchy decomposes Collect Mission Data through multiple sub-activities; no completeness metric or full-mission demonstration.", "quote_location": "Step 8 and Conclusion", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[1].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0002", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["Only selected branches of the activity hierarchy are illustrated.", "Future work is needed for allocation, interfaces, and verification, so full architecture completeness is not established."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0002::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">The approach is general enough to be incorporated into many systems-engineering methodologies and is not dependent on a specific tool.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SysML requirements/use-case/activity modeling workflow", "claim_text": "The approach is general enough to be incorporated into many systems-engineering methodologies and is not dependent on a specific tool.", "evidence_source": "Conclusion: 'Generalizability. This approach is not dependent on any specific tool and is general enough to be easily incorporated into many systems engineering methodologies.' Introduction: 'This approach does not attempt to develop an entirely new methodology. Instead, it draws from existing methodologies...'", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative generalizability assertion; no cross-tool or cross-method implementation evidence.", "quote_location": "Conclusion; Introduction", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[1].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0002", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["Only MagicDraw is shown in the paper.", "No interoperability or implementation evidence for other tools/methodologies is provided."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0003::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">An integrated SysML-based modeling environment can extract feasibility, performance, and robustness metrics and visualize physical and functional satellite states for representative RAX mission scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Integrated modeling environment executing SysML-based behavior models for energy collection, data acquisition, and ground-station downloading scenarios.", "claim_text": "An integrated SysML-based modeling environment can extract feasibility, performance, and robustness metrics and visualize physical and functional satellite states for representative RAX mission scenarios.", "evidence_source": "The integrated modeling environment enables users to extract feasibility, performance, and robustness metrics. This enables visualization of both the physical states ... and functional states ... of the satellite for representative mission scenarios.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Feasibility, performance, robustness, position, attitude, subsystem operating points; not quantified as a process metric.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative ability to extract and visualize scenario metrics; no quantified improvement reported.", "quote_location": "Abstract, markdown lines 57-63", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[2].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0003", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The metrics are named but not tabulated for the main power workflow; robustness is not separately evaluated; no baseline or independent validation."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0003::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">The simulation environment reduces ad hoc/manual coupling by supporting automated information flow between simulators and rapid reconfiguration of analyses for different mission scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "MagicDraw/SysML, PHX ModelCenter, STK, MATLAB, ParaMagic, and CST model-based engineering environment.", "claim_text": "The simulation environment reduces ad hoc/manual coupling by supporting automated information flow between simulators and rapid reconfiguration of analyses for different mission scenarios.", "evidence_source": "Unlike these approaches, our simulation environment supports the automated flow of information between simulators, enabling users to easily evaluate different design configurations or reconfigure the analysis for different mission scenarios in a rapid and convenient way.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "No measured time/effort metric; qualitative claim of automated flow and rapid/convenient reconfiguration.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative contrast with hacked/manual simulator coupling; no measured reduction.", "quote_location": "Section 4, Model-Based Engineering Environment", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[2].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0003", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The lessons-learned section also reports wrapper setup and debugging as time-consuming, tempering the automation/effort claim."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0003::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">A single acausal SysML SNR parametric model can be executed with different causalities to compute link SNR, required downlink power, or achievable data rate.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SNR Analysis BDD, SysML parametric diagram, instance structure, and ParaMagic scenario browsers.", "claim_text": "A single acausal SysML SNR parametric model can be executed with different causalities to compute link SNR, required downlink power, or achievable data rate.", "evidence_source": "ParaMagic can be used to execute a given parametric model for different causalities, such that input and output variables can be switched on-the-fly.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "SNR=22.942 dB; required p_dl=0.101 W; achievable r_dl=94,719.799 bit/s for the shown scenarios.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Demonstrates reuse of one parametric model for three analysis questions; Scenario 1 exceeds SNR_min=13 dB.", "quote_location": "Section 6, Communication Subsystem (SNR) Analysis; Figures 12-13", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[2].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0003", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The communications example assumes a single ground station and does not compare model outputs to a separate link tool or flight downlink data."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0003::claim-04">
