      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "External Constraints; FCC/NASA/NOAA regulations; NASA Spectrum Guidance SysML model; Cal Poly CubeSat Specification SysML model; regulatory viewpoints.", "claim_text": "Regulatory requirements/guidelines can be modeled as SysML models linked to the CRM, with viewpoints supporting validation/compliance responsibilities.", "evidence_source": "Abstract/intro text: \"We are exploring having NASA, NOAA, and FCC regulations contained within their own SysML models and connecting those models to our CubeSat Reference Model.\" Section 6: mission-specific model \"will need viewpoints for the compliant model elements, licenses, and authorizations.\"", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "A compliance-traceability concept is described; external model linking is partly future work and not demonstrated with results.", "source_claim_id": "C8_regulatory_compliance_linking", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[4].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[7]", "study_id": "paper-0005", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Compliance remains the responsibility of mission-specific teams; links to external regulatory models and review processes are not fully implemented or evaluated."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0007::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">The approach provides clear traceability from stakeholder concerns through mission objectives, MOEs, MOPs, and TPMs, enabling assessment of impacts when stakeholder concerns change.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "StakeholderConcern, MissionObjective, MOE_specification, MOE value properties, MOPs, TPMs, and SysML «trace» relationships in the CubeSat Reference Model.", "claim_text": "The approach provides clear traceability from stakeholder concerns through mission objectives, MOEs, MOPs, and TPMs, enabling assessment of impacts when stakeholder concerns change.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative effect only: authors claim impact of changes can be easily assessed; figures illustrate trace links but no count or effort reduction is measured.", "quote_location": "Section 5: \"This allows for complete traceability from the quantified value properties of the mission enterprise block back to the originating stakeholder concern. This enables quickly assessing the impact of any changes to stakeholder concerns.\" Conclusion: \"There is clear traceability from stakeholder concerns to TPMs allowing for the impact of any changes to be easily assessed.\"", "source_claim_id": "C1_traceability_impact_assessment", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[5].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0007", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Traceability is shown in illustrative model diagrams, but ease of impact assessment is not evaluated with user tasks, change scenarios, baseline process data, or project outcomes."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0007::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">Constraint blocks and parametric diagrams allow MOPs/TPMs to be analyzed so different system or subsystem solutions can be assessed against MOEs.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SysML constraint blocks and parametric diagrams for service life, total cost, and DeltaV relationships.", "claim_text": "Constraint blocks and parametric diagrams allow MOPs/TPMs to be analyzed so different system or subsystem solutions can be assessed against MOEs.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative capability claim; no executed trade study results or numerical outputs are reported in this paper.", "quote_location": "Section 5: \"In SysML, constraint blocks and parametric diagrams are used to perform this type of analysis... This allows different solutions to be evaluated against the MOEs.\" Section 5: \"This allows for evaluation of different subsystem solutions based on their impact to the MOP.\"", "source_claim_id": "C2_parametric_trade_decision_support", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[5].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0007", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The diagrams may be sufficient for representing relationships, but the paper does not show solver execution, numeric values, sensitivity studies, or decision outcomes."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0007::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">Textual MOE/MOP/TPM specifications let stakeholders express qualitative technical measures before they are translated into quantitative model properties, broadening the set of measures captured in the system model.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "MOE Specification, MOP Specification, and TPM Specification model elements in the Technical Measures Profile.", "claim_text": "Textual MOE/MOP/TPM specifications let stakeholders express qualitative technical measures before they are translated into quantitative model properties, broadening the set of measures captured in the system model.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative effect only: natural-language measures such as service life and total cost are captured and traced to value properties.", "quote_location": "Section 5: \"Users may be well versed at stating the need verbally, but not at capturing value properties. The MOE Specification is a model element created for capturing a user's description of the MOE.\" Conclusion: \"The use of textual specifications for defining technical measures broadens the scope to include all types of technical measures within the system model.\"", "source_claim_id": "C3_qualitative_measure_completeness_stakeholder_alignment", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[5].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0007", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The claim is structurally plausible from the profile and examples, but no stakeholder evaluation demonstrates improved communication or completeness."}</data>
    </node>
