    </node>
    <node id="paper-0007::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">Applying technical measurement in a CubeSat MBSE model could improve mission success by addressing high failure rates and providing insight into development progress and risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Technical measures (MOEs, MOPs, TPMs) represented and traced within the CubeSat system model.", "claim_text": "Applying technical measurement in a CubeSat MBSE model could improve mission success by addressing high failure rates and providing insight into development progress and risks.", "extractor_confidence": "low", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Potential success/risk benefit is asserted conceptually; no reliability proxy results or mission outcome evidence.", "quote_location": "Abstract: \"Using a CubeSat example is appropriate given the historically high failure rate and rapid growth of these missions and the role technical measurement could play in increasing their success.\" Technical measurement definition: measures \"provide insight into the progress... and the associated risks and issues\".", "source_claim_id": "C5_risk_mission_success_context", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[5].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0007", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "High CubeSat failure rates may be driven by factors outside technical measurement; the paper provides no causal evidence that this MBSE approach improves reliability or mission assurance."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0008::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">Integrating enterprise/cost concerns into the CubeSat SysML framework is intended to provide an up-to-date mission cost estimate and enable cost/performance/schedule/risk trades from conceptual design through the lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Parametric cost estimating relationships (CERs/A-PICOMO) using enterprise-model parameters, requirements, system features, and test requirements.", "claim_text": "Integrating enterprise/cost concerns into the CubeSat SysML framework is intended to provide an up-to-date mission cost estimate and enable cost/performance/schedule/risk trades from conceptual design through the lifecycle.", "evidence_source": "Abstract: 'A cost model in the form of parametric, cost estimating relationships (CERs) is described here and is planned to be integrated with the system model architecture to provide an \"up to the minute\" total project cost estimate, with emphasis on assessment at the conceptual design phase.' Section 3: 'it is critical to have cost estimation capabilities throughout the mission lifecycle allowing trades to be conducted between cost, system performance, schedule and risk.'", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Planned/argued ability to refine cost estimates and support trades; no quantitative outcome or completed cost-model integration result is reported.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0008", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["The integration is described partly as planned, not as a completed evaluated capability.", "No numeric cost-estimation accuracy, saved cost, or baseline comparison is reported."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0008::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">The CubeSat architecture framework provides traceability from mission objectives and mission requirements to system components, interfaces, tasks, and operating modes.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Requirements flow-down, subsystem block, Mission CONOPS, components/interfaces/tasks grouping.", "claim_text": "The CubeSat architecture framework provides traceability from mission objectives and mission requirements to system components, interfaces, tasks, and operating modes.", "evidence_source": "Section 2: 'A CubeSat architecture framework ... can provide a traceability map for translating the mission objectives and mission requirements into basic building blocks of CubeSat system components, interfaces and tasks.' Section 2: 'The system requirements when flowed through this block get broken down into components, interfaces, and tasks as basic building blocks.'", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "The paper shows/argues the traceability map but does not quantify link coverage or defect reduction.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0008", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["Traceability is illustrated rather than measured; completeness of links is not reported.", "Detailed requirements tables/matrices are not reproduced in the paper."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0008::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">An integrated SysML, analysis, and simulation toolchain enabled end-to-end mission-scenario simulation, trade studies, and requirements verification involving power/data interdependencies and battery/solar-panel parameters.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "RAX CubeSat integrated model using MagicDraw/Cameo Simulation Toolkit, ModelCenter, STK, MATLAB, and related analyses.", "claim_text": "An integrated SysML, analysis, and simulation toolchain enabled end-to-end mission-scenario simulation, trade studies, and requirements verification involving power/data interdependencies and battery/solar-panel parameters.", "evidence_source": "Section 4: 'This was executed by the Cameo Simulation Toolkit ... which enabled end-to-end simulation of realistic mission scenarios. This enabled requirements verification for mission scenarios and the ability to perform trades on parameters such as orbit latitude, ground network size and distribution, and solar panel and battery sizes.' Section 6: 'The integrated model enabled the execution of trade studies to evaluate mission performance and verify that mission requirements would be satisfied.'", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitatively enabled mission performance evaluation, requirements verification, and trades over orbit latitude, ground network size/distribution, solar panel area, and battery capacity; no numerical results are provided in this paper.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0008", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["The paper reports capability and varied parameters but not the actual simulation outputs or requirements pass/fail tables.", "No independent validation against hardware, operations, or a non-MBSE process is reported."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0008::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">The CubeSat SysML framework/model and manual provide a reusable starting point and learning resource for other CubeSat teams.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "RAX CubeSat model, manual, reusable SysML representation of common CubeSat elements, instructions for analysis tools.", "claim_text": "The CubeSat SysML framework/model and manual provide a reusable starting point and learning resource for other CubeSat teams.", "evidence_source": "Abstract: 'The framework developed is a SysML representation of common CubeSat elements that can be used as a library to build a domain-specific CubeSat.' Model Availability: 'Our RAX CubeSat model and its manual are being made available to the academic community' and intent includes 'A starting point for a CubeSat team to develop their own model.'", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Model and manual are reported as available/being made available; no external reuse case, access URL, or adoption metric is reported.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0008", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["Availability appears community-scoped; a persistent repository or license is not provided in the paper.", "Reuse value is claimed but not measured across independent projects."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0008::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">SLIM links SysML blocks to PLM parts/BOMs, enabling generation/synchronization of part structures and continuity from systems architecture to mechanical/electrical design.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SLIM use cases connecting SysML model elements with Windchill/Teamcenter PLM elements; generated Windchill BOM/part structure.", "claim_text": "SLIM links SysML blocks to PLM parts/BOMs, enabling generation/synchronization of part structures and continuity from systems architecture to mechanical/electrical design.", "evidence_source": "Section 5: 'SLIM enables systems engineers to develop a high-level system model in SysML and connect it to domain-specific models, such as Bills of Materials (BOMs) and Computer Aided Design (CAD)... managed in various enterprise product lifecycle management systems.' Section 5 Use Case 1: 'the block structure is used to generate a part structure in a PLM system Windchill ... Connections are saved between the corresponding parts and blocks so that changes on either side can be synchronized as desired.'", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Demonstrates generation of a Windchill part structure from a SysML block structure and saved connections for synchronization; compare/sync maturity is future work.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0008", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["Demonstration screenshots/use cases do not quantify synchronization accuracy or downstream design effectiveness.", "The paper states comparison/synchronization capabilities are still maturing."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0008::claim-06">
      <data key="d2">A payload part structure from a previous mission can be reused from PLM to generate a SysML block structure for a new CubeSat design, replacing placeholders and supporting mass/cost calculations.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SLIM Use Case 2; Windchill/Teamcenter payload part structure transformed into SysML block structure.", "claim_text": "A payload part structure from a previous mission can be reused from PLM to generate a SysML block structure for a new CubeSat design, replacing placeholders and supporting mass/cost calculations.", "evidence_source": "Section 5 Use Case 2: 'The payload for the mission may be reused from a previous mission enterprise that exists in a PLM system ... Generate a SysML block structure from the payload model in Windchill and use it in the context of a new CubeSat design.' Section 5: 'This may be a preliminary design, perhaps submitted for purposes of mass and/or cost calculation.'", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Illustrated reuse of previous mission payload structure in a new CubeSat context; the previous mission is a source of reused structure rather than an evaluated comparator, and no reuse effort or error reduction metric is reported.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "study_id": "paper-0008", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["The wording 'may be reused' indicates a use-case scenario rather than validated repeat adoption.", "No evidence is provided that reuse preserved semantics or reduced effort."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0008::claim-07">
      <data key="d2">MBSE/SysML and a top-down framework improve team communication and integration of components, interfaces, processes, and tasks into early CONOPS and design choices.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SysML framework, top-down approach, components/interfaces/processes/tasks feeding Mission Operations Concept.", "claim_text": "MBSE/SysML and a top-down framework improve team communication and integration of components, interfaces, processes, and tasks into early CONOPS and design choices.", "evidence_source": "Introduction: 'MBSE and the use of standard languages such as Systems Modeling Language (SysML) and Unified Modeling Language (UML) allow for stronger more integrated communication between engineering teams.' Conclusion: 'an engineering team can more effectively communicate and integrate the system such as the component, interfaces, processes and tasks.'", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Communication and integration benefits are asserted/argued; no stakeholder assessment or team metric is reported.", "source_claim_id": "C7", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[6]", "study_id": "paper-0008", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["Benefit may follow from general systems-engineering discipline rather than the specific MBSE artifacts in this paper.", "No stakeholder/user evaluation is reported."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0008::claim-08">
      <data key="d2">The modeling framework should lead to more robust and reusable CubeSat designs and address reliability/stakeholder concerns by combining top-down architecture with bottom-up component/interface/task overhead estimation.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "CubeSat architecture framework, overhead estimation model, component/interface/task decomposition.", "claim_text": "The modeling framework should lead to more robust and reusable CubeSat designs and address reliability/stakeholder concerns by combining top-down architecture with bottom-up component/interface/task overhead estimation.", "evidence_source": "Abstract/Section 6: 'a modeling framework that allows for analyzing and costing the technical design of the spacecraft throughout the lifecycle of the mission will allow for more robust and reusable designs.' Introduction/third phase: 'a bottom-up development process to address the reliability of CubeSats and stakeholder concerns.'", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Robustness/reliability is an intended design benefit; the paper does not report reliability analysis, failure-rate improvement, or flight evidence.", "source_claim_id": "C8", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[7]", "study_id": "paper-0008", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["Reliability is not measured; design robustness may depend on engineering quality, component choices, and testing rather than MBSE alone.", "EPS-specific reliability outcomes are not separated from system-level claims."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0008::claim-09">
      <data key="d2">The work is claimed to be the first known integration of a space-system SysML model with analytical models, simulation engines, and a special-purpose high-fidelity space-system model.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Integrated RAX/CubeSat model and analysis architecture.", "claim_text": "The work is claimed to be the first known integration of a space-system SysML model with analytical models, simulation engines, and a special-purpose high-fidelity space-system model.", "evidence_source": "Section 6: 'To the best of our knowledge this is the first known integration of a space system SysML model with a set of analytical models, simulation engines, and special purpose high fidelity space system model.'", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Novel integration is asserted based on the authors' knowledge; no systematic comparison to other toolchains is provided.", "source_claim_id": "C9", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[8]", "study_id": "paper-0008", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["The novelty claim is not independently established and is partly a self-assessment.", "The cited prior papers may contain the detailed demonstration rather than this paper."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0010::claim-01">
