      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Candidate OMG CubeSat specification and conformance criteria: five fundamental elements, architecture levels, form factor, and deployer accommodation.", "claim_text": "OMG conformance criteria and retention of core CSRM logical elements can provide a common baseline for comparing, evaluating, sharing, and reusing mission-specific CubeSat implementations.", "evidence_source": "Retention of these logical elements provides a common baseline for comparing and evaluating different mission-specific implementations and for the sharing and reuse of design elements.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Common-baseline value is asserted; no comparison/reuse metric.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Potential common baseline; OMG approval and cross-project use are not demonstrated.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[8].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0011", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Conformance to common elements may not ensure semantic consistency, tool interoperability, or sustained reuse; OMG evaluation was still in progress."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0011::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">The CSRM has been vetted by systems-engineering professionals and introduced to CubeSat development teams with favorable results; it is in use by several university teams.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Formal review/recommendation of the CSRM and use by university CubeSat development teams.", "claim_text": "The CSRM has been vetted by systems-engineering professionals and introduced to CubeSat development teams with favorable results; it is in use by several university teams.", "evidence_source": "The CSRM has been formally reviewed and recommended by 1) a Certified Architect Program engineering fellow and 2) by a team lead by Director level system engineer.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Qualitative indicators: recommendation by reviewers, several universities using it, favorable results; no numeric count beyond 'several'.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Reported favorable vetting and use; detailed results not provided.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[8].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0011", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Review criteria, independence, adoption depth, mission outcomes, and user feedback details are not reported."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0011::claim-06">
      <data key="d2">The CSRM can be adapted to different mission methods because it is methodology-agnostic, provides instructions, and lets teams populate or modify model elements and containment trees.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "CSRM library, population packages, notes, instructions, and modifiable containment tree.", "claim_text": "The CSRM can be adapted to different mission methods because it is methodology-agnostic, provides instructions, and lets teams populate or modify model elements and containment trees.", "evidence_source": "The CSRM provides a library of model elements but does not dictate what model elements and relationships to use... The CSRM is well-documented and explains to the team how to populate it...", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Usability is supported by author report that users found notes easy to follow, but no formal usability metric.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Partial adoption guidance and tailoring flexibility; no measured adoption effort.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[8].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "study_id": "paper-0011", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Flexibility may shift tailoring decisions to teams; easy-to-follow notes are reported without evaluation data."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0011::claim-07">
