      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Third-phase modeling development environment with MagicDraw/Cameo Simulation Toolkit, ModelCenter/MBSE Analyzer, STK, and MATLAB; trade-study variables for power and communications.", "claim_text": "Earlier phases of the CSRM/RAX lineage enabled model-based trade studies of solar-panel area, battery capacity, orbit altitude, and ground-station networks to compare energy and data-downlink outcomes.", "evidence_source": "Different configurations of solar panel areas and maximum battery capacity were traded off to compare on-board energy levels and... orbital altitudes and ground station network configurations were traded off to compare quantity of data downloaded.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "On-board energy levels and quantity of data downloaded are named, but no values/results appear in this paper.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Trade studies are reported as having been carried out; this paper does not present effect sizes or trade results.", "source_claim_id": "C7", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[8].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[6]", "study_id": "paper-0011", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Evidence relies on summarized prior work; the current paper omits model assumptions, configurations, numerical outputs, and validation."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0011::claim-08">
      <data key="d2">Model-integrated technical measures and V&amp;V activity elements support assessment, verification, and validation of requirements, mission objectives, and technical measures.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "MOE/MOP/TPM specifications, methods documents/spreadsheets, constraint blocks, Verification Activity and Validation Activity elements/tables. Also relates to generic buy-offs/design reviews/specifications noted in Figure 2.", "claim_text": "Model-integrated technical measures and V&amp;V activity elements support assessment, verification, and validation of requirements, mission objectives, and technical measures.", "evidence_source": "Verification activities provide data to the technical measurement process... The Verification Activity element describes the process for verifying an element, e.g. a requirement.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Technical measures are described as values and methods; no measured coverage or pass/fail result is reported.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "The CSRM can capture V&amp;V plans/procedures/results/status and link them to requirements/objectives/technical measures.", "source_claim_id": "C8", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[8].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[7]", "study_id": "paper-0011", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "V&amp;V is described structurally; no actual verification execution, acceptance results, or EPS-specific test procedures are shown."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0011::claim-09">
      <data key="d2">If approved by OMG, the model-based CSRM specification would set a precedent for future reference architectures and reusable libraries.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "CSRM submitted to OMG as a model-based CubeSat specification candidate.", "claim_text": "If approved by OMG, the model-based CSRM specification would set a precedent for future reference architectures and reusable libraries.", "evidence_source": "If approved, since the CSRM is model-based, it would serve as a precedent for future reference architectures and reusable libraries.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "No realized specification, reuse count, or library adoption evidence.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Conditional future standards/reuse effect; not realized in the paper.", "source_claim_id": "C9", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[8].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[8]", "study_id": "paper-0011", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Approval, dissemination, format, control, and actual adoption were unresolved at publication."}</data>
