      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "CubeSat Reference Model as framework/checklist for future CubeSat developers.", "claim_text": "A properly designed reference model can reduce systems-engineering burden, serve as a checklist, and promote uniformity and consistency across future CubeSat models.", "evidence_source": "'MBSE holds the promise of reducing the burden of systems engineering tasks... a properly designed reference model can serve as a checklist... and promote uniformity and consistency across future CubeSat models.'", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Not measured; framed as promise/anticipated effect.", "quote_location": "Conclusion.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[14].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "study_id": "paper-0022", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No empirical evidence shows burden reduction, checklist completeness, or consistency gains; effect depends on future model release and user adoption."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0022::claim-07">
      <data key="d2">Distribution mechanisms such as MagicDraw, ZIP/XMI, OpenMBEE, Teamcenter, walk-throughs, and user feedback could support model sharing and reuse.</data>
