    <node id="paper-0024::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">OPM's object-process-state model exposes a core integration problem: PLM is geometry/space-centric and lacks explicit time/state representation needed for behavior/functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "OPM CubeSat/thermal diagrams, CPM thermal representation, STEP/AP242 counts", "claim_text": "OPM's object-process-state model exposes a core integration problem: PLM is geometry/space-centric and lacks explicit time/state representation needed for behavior/functions.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Demonstrates representation gap; not a measured project improvement.", "quote_location": "Section 5: PLM systems represent space in detail but leave time implicit, making it difficult to integrate the digital chain; state is essentially not present in PLM systems.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[16].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0024", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["Simplified assembly may not represent all PLM/AP242 implementations.", "Absence of entities may depend on 3D model construction.", "Detailed example is thermal, not EPS."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0026::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">A Papyrus SysML power-subsystem model plus Java extraction code enables parameter-impact traceability and automatic requirement/constraint verification for CubeSat EPS design scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Papyrus .uml model with blocks, requirements, assumptions, and constraint blocks; Java code extracts these elements and generates traceability/constraint-status tables.", "claim_text": "A Papyrus SysML power-subsystem model plus Java extraction code enables parameter-impact traceability and automatic requirement/constraint verification for CubeSat EPS design scenarios.", "evidence_source": "The code takes as input the Papyrus '.uml' file of the model from which it extracts ... block data, requirement and assumption constraints, and constraint block data", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "In the demonstration scenario, calculated values match expected power-budget results and the output flags 0&lt;PSAM as respected and Batt*1.2&lt;BC as not respected.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[17].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0026", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Only one constructed scenario is shown; no independent validation, integration test, or measured design-process benefit is provided. Correct results may reflect correct equation implementation rather than broader MBSE value."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0026::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">Using open-source Papyrus and a public model repository makes the CubeSat power-subsystem model easier to reproduce, reuse, and adapt.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
