    <node id="paper-0027::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">MBSE can capture CubeSat system dependencies and enable reuse of knowledge from previous CubeSat missions, providing continuity and traceability across missions.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SysML/MBSE diagrams, dependency graph, DSM for CubeSat preliminary design parameters.", "claim_text": "MBSE can capture CubeSat system dependencies and enable reuse of knowledge from previous CubeSat missions, providing continuity and traceability across missions.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Proposed reuse and traceability mechanism; no cross-mission reuse measurement reported.", "quote_location": {"location": "Section III.A", "quote": "MBSE can be used to capture the system dependencies represented in Figs.1 and 2, allowing to reuse knowledge from previous CubeSat missions. The MBSE diagrams can be reshaped to meet new mission expectations without needing to start from zero, guaranteeing continuity and traceability of success within missions."}, "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[18].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0027", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No actual reuse across multiple missions is demonstrated; benefit could arise from any well-maintained dependency model or template, not necessarily MBSE."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0027::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">Dependency graphs and DSMs guide design iteration by showing feedback loops, rerun sequence, and relevant parameters when requirements or constraints are not met.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Design parameter dependency graph, design structure matrix, MB2DM-generated DSM from SysML, Nanospace UI requirement statuses.", "claim_text": "Dependency graphs and DSMs guide design iteration by showing feedback loops, rerun sequence, and relevant parameters when requirements or constraints are not met.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "In CREME scenarios, DSM/dependency graph identifies alternatives such as changing orbit, solar-generator number, altitude, or structural parameters after constraints fail.", "quote_location": {"location": "Section III.C", "quote": "The dependency graph ... or the design structure matrix ... are available to show the feedback loops and sequence of which part of the script should be re-run."}, "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[18].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0027", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The graph/DSM shown can be manually constructed; paper does not quantify improvement in decision quality or iteration time."}</data>
