    <node id="paper-0027::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">Nanospace plus semi-automatic scripts/API stores and shares intermediary results, easing expert collaboration and reducing the risk of non-converging designs.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Nanospace database/API, Python scripts, YAML inputs, graphs, Markdown reports, shared intermediary results.", "claim_text": "Nanospace plus semi-automatic scripts/API stores and shares intermediary results, easing expert collaboration and reducing the risk of non-converging designs.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Parameters are automatically updated in Nanospace and results are shared; avoidance of non-converging designs remains a qualitative assertion requiring human expertise.", "quote_location": {"location": "Section III.C", "quote": "The process is semi-automatic, which allows to avoid getting stuck in non-converging designs (human expertise is required). Intermediary results are also stored in Nanospace, and can therefore be easily shared between the experts."}, "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[18].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0027", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No measurement of collaboration, effort, or convergence is provided; benefits may reflect database sharing and scripts rather than MBSE integration."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0027::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">Executable preliminary-design analyses support requirement/constraint checking and design decisions for power, communications, and reentry before physical development.</data>
