    <node id="paper-0033::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">The cyber-physical MAM plus MBSE toolchain enables visual configuration and verification/validation of CubeSat operations scenarios by modeling and simulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Cyber-Physical abstraction, Mission Architecture Model, C2F transformation, ForPlan simulation", "claim_text": "The cyber-physical MAM plus MBSE toolchain enables visual configuration and verification/validation of CubeSat operations scenarios by modeling and simulation.", "evidence_source": "From these graphs, we can infer that the power and data balances are stable, i.e. the satellite is capable of charging the batteries for the amount used each orbit, and download the generated mission data. This means, for this perspective, that this is a valid operation scenario.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Battery charge stability and mass-memory/data usage in final scenario.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Final NCBR2 simulation was judged a valid operation scenario because power and data balances were stable.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[21].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0033", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Simulation validity depends on accuracy of model parameters and ForPlan abstractions; no physical/flight validation or independent verification is reported."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0033::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">Automatically generating the ForPlan configuration script from the MAM removes the need for users to understand simulator source code or manually code each scenario, making scenario changes more practical and faster.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "C2F Capella plugin and generated Julia configuration script", "claim_text": "Automatically generating the ForPlan configuration script from the MAM removes the need for users to understand simulator source code or manually code each scenario, making scenario changes more practical and faster.", "evidence_source": "By using the MAM and automatically generating the input configuration script, the user is no longer required to understand how the simulator source code works, and does not have to manually code the configurations for each scenario, permitting a straightforward use of the simulator. Also, it is much more practical and faster to change scenario parameters in the model than manually in the configuration script", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "No effort/time metric reported.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitatively asserted easier and faster scenario parameter changes; generated script excerpt demonstrates feasibility.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[21].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0033", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No time/effort baseline or user study; the claim may depend on users' familiarity with Capella and correctness of C2F."}</data>
    </node>
