    <node id="paper-0034::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">Applying RML to CubeSat/engineering-system development enhances requirements quality and eases analysis and elicitation by reducing miscommunication among heterogeneous stakeholders.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Visual RML objective models for functional and nonfunctional requirements.", "claim_text": "Applying RML to CubeSat/engineering-system development enhances requirements quality and eases analysis and elicitation by reducing miscommunication among heterogeneous stakeholders.", "evidence_source": "Developing cyber-physical systems such as CubeSats requires dynamic engagements of stakeholders, developers, tester, analysts, and project managers. With their different backgrounds, the technicality of analyzing functional and nonfunctional requirements may lead to miscommunication between groups. Thus, applying requirements modeling language (RML) into an engineering system development project will enhance the quality of requirements as well as ease the analysis and elicitation processes.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "No measured quality, ambiguity, consistency, or stakeholder-comprehension metric is reported.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Expected improvement in requirements quality and analysis/elicitation ease; no observed effect size reported.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[22].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0034", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Claim is plausible but based on rationale and a conceptual contrast with UML/SysML, not stakeholder evaluation or comparative measurement."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0034::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">RMM traceability from requirements to process steps, code, and test cases helps ensure that every requirement is adequately tested.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "RMM and NDSAT example mapping of requirements, business rules, code functions, test case IDs, and pass results.", "claim_text": "RMM traceability from requirements to process steps, code, and test cases helps ensure that every requirement is adequately tested.", "evidence_source": "It works as a high-level documentation, which maps and traces user requirements with the corresponding test cases. This is intended to ensure that for each and every requirement there is an adequate level of testing successfully fulfilled.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "The paper uses trace links and test coverage conceptually but does not compute coverage percentages or link counts beyond illustrative rows.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Illustrative RMM rows show requirements linked to code and test cases with pass results.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[22].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0034", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The example demonstrates representation of links, not that all real project requirements were covered or that defects were reduced."}</data>
    </node>
