      <data key="d2">A requirements management model tool can use RMM to automate missing-link checks and support accurate linkage of requirements, test cases, and defects.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "RMM as used by a requirements management model tool; defect mapping to business requirements, scenarios, and test cases.", "claim_text": "A requirements management model tool can use RMM to automate missing-link checks and support accurate linkage of requirements, test cases, and defects.", "evidence_source": "A Requirements Mapping Matrix (RMM) is best used by a requirement management model tool which can automate the process of checking for missing links [12].", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "No automated-tool run, missing-link count, or defect metric is reported.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Automation capability is described conceptually; defect mapping is illustrated as a procedure.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[22].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0034", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The paper does not name or demonstrate the requirements tool, so automation may remain aspirational."}</data>
