    <node id="paper-0037::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">The MBSE/docs-as-code approach is intended to improve CubeSat success rates and mission assurance for university teams by improving planning, documentation, project management, and simplicity.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Mission architecture process and docs-as-code tooling for university CubeSat team coordination.", "claim_text": "The MBSE/docs-as-code approach is intended to improve CubeSat success rates and mission assurance for university teams by improving planning, documentation, project management, and simplicity.", "evidence_source": "The SeaLion mission architecture team sought to create a model-based systems engineering approach to assist improving CubeSat success rates", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "No observed mission-success effect; the claim is motivational and based on literature/context about CubeSat failures and systems-engineering needs.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[23].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0037", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "CubeSat success depends on hardware, launch, operations, funding, and team factors beyond the architecture method."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0037::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">The component/DOF extension and planned N2 diagrams can improve integrability by documenting components, interfaces, BOMs, assembly instructions, and areas where interface conflicts may arise.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "DOF component YAML, parts/components/functions/interfaces, BOM/assembly instruction generation, planned N2 chart.", "claim_text": "The component/DOF extension and planned N2 diagrams can improve integrability by documenting components, interfaces, BOMs, assembly instructions, and areas where interface conflicts may arise.", "evidence_source": "structured as a Distributed OSHW Framework (DOF)—component for defining the contents of the Mission concept of operations (ConOps) as a collection of nested subcomponents, component interfaces, and component functions for generating bill of materials (BOMs) and assembly instructions", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Conceptual/future claim that generated N2 diagrams would help identify interface conflicts and assumptions.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[23].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0037", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The ability to detect conflicts depends on completeness and correctness of interface data entered by subsystem teams."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0037::claim-06">
      <data key="d2">The extended data model and SeaLion implementation could be reused by future CubeSat projects as a self-describing specification/reference implementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Public SeaLion mission architecture repository and DOF CubeSat data-model extension.", "claim_text": "The extended data model and SeaLion implementation could be reused by future CubeSat projects as a self-describing specification/reference implementation.", "evidence_source": "This extended data model would serve as a self-describing specification that new CubeSat projects could adopt for their own CubeSat missions, whereby the SeaLion mission would serve as the first reference implementation.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Future-oriented reuse claim; SeaLion serves as first implementation, not evidence of repeated reuse.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[23].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "study_id": "paper-0037", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Adoption may require tutorials, customization, and team communication practices not yet fully documented."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0039::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">A CSRM-derived standardized MBSE template can make CubeSat design cycles more efficient and reduce future design/development time by preventing repeated trade studies on well-understood subsystems/components.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "CSRM-based PSAT1U standardized template/baseline model used as a starting point for mission-specific CubeSats.", "claim_text": "A CSRM-derived standardized MBSE template can make CubeSat design cycles more efficient and reduce future design/development time by preventing repeated trade studies on well-understood subsystems/components.", "evidence_source": "The aim of this model is to aid in the education of undergraduate engineering students in their capstone design course as well as to reduce design and development times for future CubeSat systems.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative expected reduction in design/development time; no measured effect size.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[24].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0039", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No time/effort metrics, baseline project, or student/team evaluation; the physical PSAT1U standard design itself may also reduce trade-study effort independent of MBSE."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0039::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">The baseline model defines PSAT1U subsystems/components/interfaces while leaving payload and mission modules undefined, helping users understand the payload design space and create mission-specific instances.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "PSAT1U Baseline Model, mission payload BDD, generic payload specification, and editable payload documentation/specification.", "claim_text": "The baseline model defines PSAT1U subsystems/components/interfaces while leaving payload and mission modules undefined, helping users understand the payload design space and create mission-specific instances.", "evidence_source": "The baseline model is unique in that it defines all of the important subsystems, components, and interfaces of the PSAT1U, but leaves the payload and mission specific modules undefined.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitatively claimed clearer payload design space and model tailoring; no reuse count or validation.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[24].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0039", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The paper demonstrates editing payload documentation but does not show successful independent reuse by other teams or missions."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0039::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">Model relationships automatically propagate a Watchdog Timer specification change from ADCS to the Power subsystem and other related elements, avoiding manual propagation and improving consistency/traceability.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Cameo model relationship between Watchdog Timer Reset Circuit, ADCS subsystem, and Power subsystem.", "claim_text": "Model relationships automatically propagate a Watchdog Timer specification change from ADCS to the Power subsystem and other related elements, avoiding manual propagation and improving consistency/traceability.", "evidence_source": "As a result, any changes made to the Watchdog Timer specification are automatically propagated to the Power subsystem and to any other subsystems or components with a relationship to the Watchdog Timer. The user does not need to manually propagate this change.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Concrete model relationship shown; authors claim no manual propagation is needed. No metric for avoided errors or time saved.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[24].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0039", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The demonstration is a single illustrative trace; it does not verify semantic correctness, requirements impact, or effects in a changing project over time."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0039::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">Storing critical PSAT1U design information inside model documentation tabs makes it viewable/editable by practitioners and supports shared understanding.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Subsystem/component specification documentation tabs, including EPS power budget and payload envelope information.", "claim_text": "Storing critical PSAT1U design information inside model documentation tabs makes it viewable/editable by practitioners and supports shared understanding.", "evidence_source": "The model stores design specifics of the PSAT1U as text data within the documentation tab of the appropriate subsystem or component specification. In this way, critical design information is stored in the model and can be viewed or edited as needed by practitioners.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative claim that critical design information is stored, viewable, and editable in the model.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[24].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0039", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Storing information as text documentation may not provide formal analyzability or consistency checking; no user evidence is reported."}</data>
    </node>
