    <node id="paper-0043::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">MOSAiC connects ARCADIA-based MBSE models with open-source multi-domain simulations to improve traceability, reusability, and lifecycle fidelity.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "ARCADIA/Capella authoritative model, MOSAiC modeling and simulation modules, open-source repository.", "claim_text": "MOSAiC connects ARCADIA-based MBSE models with open-source multi-domain simulations to improve traceability, reusability, and lifecycle fidelity.", "evidence_source": "This paper presents the first version of the unified Modeling and Simulation (M&amp;S) framework MOSAiC ... which connects MBSE with open source, multi-domain simulation environments, with the goal of improving traceability, reusability, and fidelity in the system lifecycle.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative; no measured traceability or reuse metric.", "source_claim_id": "C1_traceable_reusable_simulation_framework", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[26].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0043", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Benefits may derive from disciplined modeling and open tooling generally rather than from MOSAiC specifically; no baseline process is evaluated."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0043::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">Model-to-simulation extraction improves consistency between system models, operational modes, and simulation artifacts.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "PVMT-enriched Capella model, custom Python parser, extracted dataset of subsystem parameters, exchanges, modes, and transitions.", "claim_text": "Model-to-simulation extraction improves consistency between system models, operational modes, and simulation artifacts.", "evidence_source": "The extracted dataset includes subsystem-level parameters such as mass, volume, and power consumption—both static and mode-dependent—as well as functional and component exchanges, OMs definitions, and their associated transition conditions.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative report of improved consistency; no trace-link count or defect metric.", "source_claim_id": "C2_consistency_model_simulation_artifacts", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[26].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0043", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Consistency may depend on parser implementation and model discipline; no automated semantic validation results are reported."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0043::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">Simulation integrated with the MBSE model enables early validation of design choices, trade-off exploration, and data-driven architectural refinement.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Orbital analysis, power budget simulation, link budget evaluation, ConOps/mode-driven simulations.", "claim_text": "Simulation integrated with the MBSE model enables early validation of design choices, trade-off exploration, and data-driven architectural refinement.", "evidence_source": "Overall, this early feedback loop enabled more informed and data-driven design decisions, provided justification for architectural refinements, and strengthened the confidence in the system's capacity to meet mission-level constraints, while moving onto the Physical Architecture layer.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Revisit/coverage, data transfer opportunities, outage periods, power and link budget profiles are discussed; only selected quantitative outputs are shown.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative justification for architectural refinements and confidence in mission-level constraints.", "source_claim_id": "C3_early_validation_tradeoffs", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[26].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0043", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The case is representative; effectiveness for other missions or teams is not evaluated."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0043::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">The EPS/power simulation can verify battery capacity and power balance across operational modes and eclipse/contact periods before hardware implementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "EPS physical architecture, battery/solar/PCDU component properties, operational modes, battery consumption plot.", "claim_text": "The EPS/power simulation can verify battery capacity and power balance across operational modes and eclipse/contact periods before hardware implementation.", "evidence_source": "during eclipse periods, the simulation would verify whether battery capacity was sufficient to sustain system operation until sunlight was available for recharging.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Battery charge percentage over 72 hours and component-specific power consumption/margins.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Battery state of charge in Figure 14 remains roughly between 86% and 100% in the rendered plot; no formal margin threshold is reported.", "source_claim_id": "C4_eps_power_feasibility", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[26].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0043", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The outcome depends on fidelity of assumed component parameters and orbital/eclipse inputs; no hardware or flight data validation is provided."}</data>
    </node>
