    <node id="paper-0043::claim-08">
      <data key="d2">Mixed-resolution LA/PA simulation allows incremental validation even when only some subsystems are physically detailed, avoiding analysis bottlenecks during staggered subsystem development.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Capella realization links between LA and PA elements, hybrid data extraction, EPS/TTC PA-level details, Basic operating mode.", "claim_text": "Mixed-resolution LA/PA simulation allows incremental validation even when only some subsystems are physically detailed, avoiding analysis bottlenecks during staggered subsystem development.", "evidence_source": "This hybrid resolution allowed the simulation to produce a more accurate and nuanced performance assessment of the system in its current state, particularly with respect to power and communication resource usage, while maintaining full system-level coherence.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "metric_detail": "Hybrid-resolution use of detailed EPS/TTC parameters and LA defaults; no schedule metric reported.", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative claim that analyses continued without waiting for full system completion.", "source_claim_id": "C8_mixed_resolution_incremental_validation", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[26].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[7]", "study_id": "paper-0043", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The schedule benefit is inferred from capability; accuracy depends on correctness of LA defaults and realization mappings."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0046::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">Students could learn and use OPAL effectively after a short introduction; most reported it easy to use.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "OPAL GUI, SAPPhIRE-based framework, 15-minute introduction and task evaluation.", "claim_text": "Students could learn and use OPAL effectively after a short introduction; most reported it easy to use.", "evidence_source": "students were able to effectively utilize OPAL's functions with only a short introduction, with 85% reporting it easy to use.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "High average ratings after approximately 15 minutes of instruction.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[27].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0046", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Student participants, short lab tasks, no objective baseline, and novelty/GUI effects may explain high ratings."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0046::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">OPAL's SAPPhIRE visual causal links made it easier to track, find, and navigate conceptual design data across subsystems.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SAPPhIRE system/subsystem model scenes linked to conceptual design files; OPAL central repository.", "claim_text": "OPAL's SAPPhIRE visual causal links made it easier to track, find, and navigate conceptual design data across subsystems.", "evidence_source": "the visual representation of the data via the SAPPhIRE Models made it significantly easier to be able to track and find data using the causal links, regardless of the subsystem being studied.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Authors describe significantly easier tracking/finding compared with traditional file management practices; layout and relationships received high user ratings.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[27].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0046", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Comparator is qualitative rather than experimentally controlled; participants had varying CubeSat familiarity but sample remains small."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0046::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">OPAL can integrate CubeSat conceptual design files into a sufficiently detailed system and subsystem model.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "OPAL repository, Table 3 requirements, Table 1 EPS file mapping, Table 2 subsystem behavior/analysis files.", "claim_text": "OPAL can integrate CubeSat conceptual design files into a sufficiently detailed system and subsystem model.", "evidence_source": "The results indicate that OPAL can integrate the data files to create a sufficiently detailed system model.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Authors conclude OPAL integrated the data files into a sufficiently detailed system model.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[27].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0046", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Manual proof-of-concept links, no independent assessment of model completeness, and no public model/data availability limit confidence."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0046::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">OPAL supports understanding and management of design changes and change propagation during iterative conceptual design.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Segment 3 change-propagation task; OPAL system and subsystem GUIs.", "claim_text": "OPAL supports understanding and management of design changes and change propagation during iterative conceptual design.", "evidence_source": "Does OPAL clearly show how changes propagate? 6.00", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "High user ratings and qualitative feedback suggest OPAL aided change propagation reasoning.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[27].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0046", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Task was idealized; no objective change-management outcomes, defect rates, or integration failures were measured."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0046::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">The consistent SAPPhIRE representation can serve as a simplified, general way to represent an entire system and navigate across function, structure, and behavior domains.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SAPPhIRE template/pattern across OPAL subsystem views; comparison with SysML domains.", "claim_text": "The consistent SAPPhIRE representation can serve as a simplified, general way to represent an entire system and navigate across function, structure, and behavior domains.", "evidence_source": "At the very least, the concept of a simplified representation of an entire system has been shown to be feasible using SAPPhIRE.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Authors state a simplified representation of the entire system is feasible using SAPPhIRE.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[27].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0046", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Generic MBSE/SysML-domain claim is extrapolated from one proof-of-concept CubeSat case and participant study."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0053::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">The concurrent-engineering toolchain produces an adaptable and interoperable model in which mission or satellite-configuration changes can be studied quickly/easily.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "IDM-CIC system description, Simu-CIC ephemeris, IDM-Power profile, Flows Manager conversion, Opalis energy-balance model.", "claim_text": "The concurrent-engineering toolchain produces an adaptable and interoperable model in which mission or satellite-configuration changes can be studied quickly/easily.", "evidence_source": "The main added value of this process is that it allows to define an adaptable and interoperable model. For instance, any change on the mission can be studied almost instantly by regenerating the corresponding ephemeris data.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Authors state mission changes can be studied almost instantly and solar-panel configuration changes can be compared easily, but no timing or effort metric is reported.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[28].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0053", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Ease and speed are asserted without a baseline or measured iteration times; improvements could depend on CNES tool familiarity and data-preparation effort."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0053::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">The simulation workflow enables EPS sizing and stable energy-budget assessment under worst-case mission and environmental conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Opalis power-subsystem model, energy flows from Simu-CIC/Flows Manager, power profile from IDM-Power, SOC thresholds and final architecture selections.", "claim_text": "The simulation workflow enables EPS sizing and stable energy-budget assessment under worst-case mission and environmental conditions.", "evidence_source": "One last thing to mention is that the minimum SOC (State Of Charge) reached during the simulation is 85%", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "The reported stable configuration has SOC minimum 85% for nominal energy balance and survival scenario SOC minimum 27.7% against a 20% acceptable minimum.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[28].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0053", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Simulation assumptions, tool fidelity, worst-case selection, and input power/thermal data are not independently validated; no physical or flight test confirms the modeled margins."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0053::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">The workflow enables trade studies of observation plans, technologies, regulator types, bus voltages, solar-cell placement, thermal sensitivity, and battery configurations.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Observation planning, 48-hour worst-case scenario, power budget by mission modes, Opalis simulation runs and technology/configuration parameters.", "claim_text": "The workflow enables trade studies of observation plans, technologies, regulator types, bus voltages, solar-cell placement, thermal sensitivity, and battery configurations.", "evidence_source": "This step is also an opportunity to carry out various trade-offs between technologies and architecture principles (type of battery/solar cell, power bus topologies, control principles, etc.).", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "The authors report the process supported final architecture choices and multiple what-if analyses, including revising scientific ambitions if energy feasibility fails.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[28].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0053", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The paper reports examples and final choices but does not provide a systematic trade-space exploration, uncertainty analysis, or baseline design process."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0053::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">Standardized files and interoperable tools enable subsystem experts to exchange data, communicate through engineering models, and keep dedicated specialized tools compatible.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Common technical reference, common database, standard files, IDM-CIC/Simu-CIC/Opalis plugins.", "claim_text": "Standardized files and interoperable tools enable subsystem experts to exchange data, communicate through engineering models, and keep dedicated specialized tools compatible.", "evidence_source": "It allows everyone to use their own dedicated and specialized tools by still ensuring compatibility with inputs/outputs of other tools, leading to a smooth workflow.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Authors state interoperability makes data exchange and communication easy and leads to a smooth workflow.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[28].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0053", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No stakeholder evaluation, interoperability failure data, or independent assessment is provided; compatibility may be conditional on CNES standards and tool availability."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0053::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">The preliminary-phase workflow could be extended to phases A/B/C/D by adding the satellite manufacturer/provider if file standards are respected.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Standard-file workflow and concurrent engineering process.", "claim_text": "The preliminary-phase workflow could be extended to phases A/B/C/D by adding the satellite manufacturer/provider if file standards are respected.", "evidence_source": "it could also be implemented for phases A/B/C/D by adding a satellite manufacturer/provider in the loop as long as the files standard is still respected", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Future/conditional claim only.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[28].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0053", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No later-phase case, manufacturer integration evidence, model-governance mechanism, or configuration-control process is reported."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0054::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">The custom MBSE tradespace model supports objective architecture selection and optimization of the BOREALIS baseline configuration.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "AD matrix, MAU/cost functions, utility-vs-cost tradespace, Pareto front, Concept 10 baseline selection.", "claim_text": "The custom MBSE tradespace model supports objective architecture selection and optimization of the BOREALIS baseline configuration.", "evidence_source": "Concept 10 emerges as a standout, positioned prominently on the Pareto front.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Concept 10 selected as baseline; paper states it balances performance, cost, robustness, and feasibility and improves on initial Concept 8 preference.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[29].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0054", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Weights are subjective; reference missions benchmark architectures but do not validate MBSE process value; no independent review or physical test is reported."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0054::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">Monte Carlo and sensitivity analyses make the architecture decision robust against uncertainty and subjective weight variation.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Monte Carlo uncertainty modeling, utility/cost error bars, sensitivity analyses by AD and concept.", "claim_text": "Monte Carlo and sensitivity analyses make the architecture decision robust against uncertainty and subjective weight variation.", "evidence_source": "Concept 10 maintains its relative position as a robust and cost-effective solution, with minimal variability in both utility and cost with respect to the other concepts.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "1000 Monte Carlo iterations at 95% confidence; all utilities remained within about +/-8% under +/-30% weight changes; Concept 10 retained a robust position.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[29].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0054", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Robustness is internal to the model assumptions and distributions; it does not demonstrate hardware reliability or mission reliability."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0054::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">The workflow is reusable/adaptable for other CubeSat missions of the same or similar class.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Reusable AD-to-concept-to-MAU/cost workflow, equations, rationale for adapting weights and performance parameters, Appendix A inputs.", "claim_text": "The workflow is reusable/adaptable for other CubeSat missions of the same or similar class.", "evidence_source": "Emphasis will be given to the model built for the tradeoff analysis, explaining how it was built and used and providing the reader with all the elements to possibly reuse it for another mission design of the same satellite class.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Authors provide method and inputs and argue adaptiveness; no reuse across independent projects is demonstrated.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[29].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0054", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Reuse is prospective and would require retuning ADs, weights, and performance variables for other missions."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0054::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">The structured workflow improves traceability and repeatability from requirements and constraints to architectural decisions and concepts.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Scientific Requirement Document DEL09, Mission Requirement Document DEL08, System Requirement Document DEL03, ADs, concept selection, CONOPS.", "claim_text": "The structured workflow improves traceability and repeatability from requirements and constraints to architectural decisions and concepts.", "evidence_source": "Unlike traditional document-centric approaches, MBSE employs a model-driven framework to manage requirements, design, analysis, and validation within a centralized environment, which greatly enhances collaboration and traceability across multidisciplinary teams.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Traceability/repeatability are asserted and supported by a structured case workflow, but no trace-link counts or verification matrix are reported.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[29].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0054", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Traceability is not directly observable in a model repository or trace matrix; document relationships may remain manual."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0054::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">A Valispace-based integrated design model will improve collaborative lifecycle continuity and real-time subsystem-data management.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Planned Valispace IDM, simplified Excel precursor, mission data and requirements tracking.", "claim_text": "A Valispace-based integrated design model will improve collaborative lifecycle continuity and real-time subsystem-data management.", "evidence_source": "Integrated Design Model (IDM): Once the mission concept baseline is chosen, a dynamic model hosted within Valispace environment [47] that integrates all subsystems will be developed, facilitating real-time updates and collaborative design efforts across different teams.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Claim is future-oriented; no implemented Valispace model results are evaluated in this article.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[29].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0054", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The IDM is under development and outside article scope; no interoperability or user-evaluation evidence is provided."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0054::claim-06">
      <data key="d2">Generic MBSE use can reduce development time, mitigate late design-change risks, enhance collaboration, and support early issue identification in complex space systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Centralized model/single source of truth and early-stage simulations described in the MBSE background section.", "claim_text": "Generic MBSE use can reduce development time, mitigate late design-change risks, enhance collaboration, and support early issue identification in complex space systems.", "evidence_source": "This centralized model enables engineers to perform early-stage simulations, identify potential issues, and make informed trade-offs, ultimately reducing development time and mitigating risks associated with late-stage design changes.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "No BOREALIS-specific measurement of development time, collaboration, or rework reduction is given.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[29].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "study_id": "paper-0054", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "This is a background rationale for MBSE rather than evaluated evidence from the case study."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0059::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">Implementing RFLP/MBSE inside 3DEXPERIENCE PLM keeps CubeSat requirements-in-loop and improves requirements traceability in early development.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "ENOVIA requirement structure with numerical parameters linked into CATIA functional/logical architecture and Dymola behavior models via RFLP.", "claim_text": "Implementing RFLP/MBSE inside 3DEXPERIENCE PLM keeps CubeSat requirements-in-loop and improves requirements traceability in early development.", "evidence_source": "Requirements are gathered from stakeholder analysis and integrated into the PLM environment to ensure traceability throughout the product development phase.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative: authors state that requirements are kept in-loop and traceable; no trace-link counts or baseline are reported.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[30].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0059", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Traceability may be a capability of the proprietary PLM environment rather than the RFLP method alone; no quantitative trace coverage or independent assessment is provided."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0059::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">DOE and linked requirement parameters support timely decision support, change management, and reduced configuration-management complexity during product development.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Design-of-experiments matrix of configurations modifies battery/EPS parameters and checks conformance against power requirements.", "claim_text": "DOE and linked requirement parameters support timely decision support, change management, and reduced configuration-management complexity during product development.", "evidence_source": "The product being design is optimized using design of experiments tools which allows to built a web of different configurations and test each of them out to provide decision support", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative and procedural: hundreds of configurations are said to be evaluated; no time/effort/configuration-complexity metric is reported.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[30].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0059", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The decision-support value is plausible but not measured; the number of configurations is not tied to decision quality, schedule, or avoided rework."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0059::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">The EPS simulation verifies that the selected battery capacity and power management/distribution unit satisfy the SoC requirement and support CubeSat operation over the simulated period.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Dymola behavior model using eclipse data, power profile, solar-panel production, battery voltage/SoC, PMDU, and SoC acceptance threshold.", "claim_text": "The EPS simulation verifies that the selected battery capacity and power management/distribution unit satisfy the SoC requirement and support CubeSat operation over the simulated period.", "evidence_source": "after 300 minutes the battery has replenished to its initial value. It shows that the the Cubesat will have no trouble during its operation. It also verifies that the battery capacity is sufficient and power management unit is working as intended.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Reported SoC remains above 90% for 300 minutes against a 60% threshold; battery replenishes to initial value after 300 minutes.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[30].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0059", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Simulation duration is short and no degradation, physical test, or flight validation is reported; results depend on assumed power profile and model fidelity."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0059::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">Integrating SysML logical/functional architecture with Dymola behavior models enables comprehensive CubeSat behavior evaluation and helps ensure requirements are met.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SysML functional/logical architecture, Dymola behavior models per logical component, and numerical requirement parameters.", "claim_text": "Integrating SysML logical/functional architecture with Dymola behavior models enables comprehensive CubeSat behavior evaluation and helps ensure requirements are met.", "evidence_source": "This integration of SysML and Dymola enables a comprehensive evaluation of the Cubesat's behavior and helps ensure that the requirements are met.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative: comprehensive evaluation is claimed; simulation outputs are shown for the power-view case.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[30].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0059", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The comprehensiveness of behavior evaluation is limited by the electrical-power viewpoint, omitted launch segment, and lack of model-fidelity validation."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0059::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">A web of connections across requirements, behavior, structure, and verification domains supports data sharing, analysis, validation, and verification.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Cross-domain model relationships among requirements, behavior, structure, and verification.", "claim_text": "A web of connections across requirements, behavior, structure, and verification domains supports data sharing, analysis, validation, and verification.", "evidence_source": "These connections enable the sharing of data and information between different domains, facilitating the analysis, validation, and verification of system requirements.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Conceptual: paper explains cross-domain connections but reports no measured interoperability or validation effect.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[30].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0059", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Figure/text demonstrate a concept of connections but not semantic correctness, maintenance effort, or interoperability robustness."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0059::claim-06">
      <data key="d2">Following RFLP ensures all requirements are captured and addressed across stages/levels so the final product meets requirements and functions as intended.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "RFLP requirements, functional, logical, and physical levels during early development.", "claim_text": "Following RFLP ensures all requirements are captured and addressed across stages/levels so the final product meets requirements and functions as intended.", "evidence_source": "By following the RFLP approach, all requirements are captured and addressed across various stages of development, ensuring that the final product meets all necessary requirements and functions as intended.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Broad qualitative assertion; no requirement coverage metric or final-product validation is reported.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[30].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "study_id": "paper-0059", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The paper only demonstrates selected power requirements, not all system requirements or final product behavior."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0061::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">The CE-MBSE/concurrent model-based approach shortens the BOSS feasibility analysis relative to the traditional methodology.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Four concurrent design sessions using S3D calculation sheets, CUTE-DB, and a Central Data Exchange System.", "claim_text": "The CE-MBSE/concurrent model-based approach shortens the BOSS feasibility analysis relative to the traditional methodology.", "evidence_source": "Using the CE-MBSE methodology, the feasibility study was completed in one month, compared to the three months required when using the traditional approach.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Feasibility analysis duration reported as 1 month with CE-MBSE versus 3 months with the traditional methodology.", "source_claim_id": "C1_schedule_reduction", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[31].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0061", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Comparator details are limited; authors note the shown results only include the four sessions and not post-study refinement."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0061::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">The CE-MBSE approach reduces the estimated mission cost for the BOSS feasibility study compared with a traditional methodology.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Concurrent design sessions, cost spreadsheet, shared assumptions, and early cross-discipline iteration.", "claim_text": "The CE-MBSE approach reduces the estimated mission cost for the BOSS feasibility study compared with a traditional methodology.", "evidence_source": "The CE-MBSE approach projected a total mission cost of 15 million euros, which is significantly lower than the 22 million euros estimated through the traditional approach.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Cost assessment is 15M€ for CE-MBSE versus 22M€ for traditional methodology.", "source_claim_id": "C2_cost_reduction", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[31].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0061", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The paper says the lower cost likely stems from minimized redesigns and optimized resources, but does not provide the cost model details or independent validation."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0061::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">The CE-MBSE workflow produced different/lower mass and other feasibility figures of merit, interpreted as evidence of integrated iterative design effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Central Data Exchange System mass/volume budgets, S3D sizing sheets, and BOSS feasibility comparison.", "claim_text": "The CE-MBSE workflow produced different/lower mass and other feasibility figures of merit, interpreted as evidence of integrated iterative design effectiveness.", "evidence_source": "The CE-MBSE methodology resulted in a spacecraft mass of 22.59 kg, which is approximately 15% lower than the 26.6 kg calculated using the traditional methodology.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Mass budget 22.59 kg with CE-MBSE versus 26.6 kg traditional; Delta-V 1.33 m/s versus 0.68 m/s.", "source_claim_id": "C3_design_performance_figures_of_merit", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[31].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0061", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Mass reduction is attributed as likely due to the integrated approach; Delta-V result favors traditional refinement and is affected by differing time allocation."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0061::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">The Central Data Exchange System improves cross-discipline consistency, validation, and error reduction by sharing up-to-date data and checking common inputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Linked Excel central repository with Inputs/Outputs tables and Check column for common input values.", "claim_text": "The Central Data Exchange System improves cross-discipline consistency, validation, and error reduction by sharing up-to-date data and checking common inputs.", "evidence_source": "It allows automated data transfer from the other spreadsheets of the S3D Tool and enables faster validation of the sizing, budgets and design, reducing manual effort and minimizing errors.", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Faster validation, less manual effort, and fewer errors are claimed qualitatively; no error counts are measured.", "source_claim_id": "C4_consistency_error_reduction", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[31].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0061", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No measured defect reduction or validation-time metric is reported; external tools still require manual entries."}</data>
    </node>
