      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "S3D Tool, Central Data Exchange System, CUTE-DB, and adapted four-session concurrent workflow.", "claim_text": "The Concurrent Model-Based approach and tools are reusable across multiple CubeSat/small-satellite mission case studies.", "evidence_source": "the Concurrent Model-Based approach and the related tools (both S3D Tool and CUTE-DB) have been implemented and tested in several case studies, including the Bennu Observer Small Satellites (BOSS) mission, the Geo-Profundo mission [13], and the Cislunar mission [15].", "extractor_confidence": "high", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Authors report application/testing in BOSS, Geo-Profundo, and a cislunar in-orbit servicing case; only BOSS is detailed in this paper.", "source_claim_id": "C7_reuse_across_case_studies", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[31].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[6]", "study_id": "paper-0061", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Only one case has detailed results in the paper; other cases are briefly described or referenced."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0061::claim-08">
      <data key="d2">Early model integration and concurrent refinement can identify risks/issues earlier and allow verification to begin before traditional approaches.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Integrated models/tools, risk assessment spreadsheets, and consistency checks.", "claim_text": "Early model integration and concurrent refinement can identify risks/issues earlier and allow verification to begin before traditional approaches.", "evidence_source": "Parallel system development and early identification of potential issues and risks ensures a continuous refinement of the models and leads to optimized system design.", "extractor_confidence": "medium", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Conceptual claim only; no verification artifact results, risk-reduction metric, or test evidence is shown.", "source_claim_id": "C8_risk_early_verification", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[31].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[7]", "study_id": "paper-0061", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The paper does not provide risk metric changes, formal verification model evidence, or physical/integration test outcomes."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0063::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">A single integrated MBSE environment ensures verification is planned and executed in the correct sequence with full requirements traceability across the CubeSat lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "NSM lifecycle model and requirements-based verification planning/execution environment.", "claim_text": "A single integrated MBSE environment ensures verification is planned and executed in the correct sequence with full requirements traceability across the CubeSat lifecycle.", "evidence_source": "A single integrated environment ensures that system verification is planned and executed in the correct sequence with full traceability based on requirements.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Asserted full traceability and correct verification sequence; no measured effect reported.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[32].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0063", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Lifecycle-wide traceability is presented as a project aim; only a Phase C-D communications exemplar is described."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0063::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">Integrating system models with programmatic tools enables data exchange and automated verification of requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SysML verification model, interface plugins, external Python/test scripts, requirements compliance artifacts.", "claim_text": "Integrating system models with programmatic tools enables data exchange and automated verification of requirements.", "evidence_source": "With the MBSE approach, the system models are integrated with other programmatic tools to enable exchange of data and allow automated verification of requirements.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Automated requirements verification is demonstrated conceptually through an EIRSAT-1 communications end-to-end test workflow; no numeric coverage reported.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[32].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0063", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Automation could depend on custom plugin/script implementation not provided; no independent test-result data are shown."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0063::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">The MBSE verification model can command the test setup and use parametric diagrams to validate exchanged data and confirm requirements compliance during test runs.</data>
