    <node id="paper-0068::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">DSM/DMM can represent CubeSat subsystems, interfaces, objects, processes, and states in one concise representation.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "OPM object-process-state model transformed/encoded as DSM/DMM for the Thermal Control System interface/function/state representation.", "claim_text": "DSM/DMM can represent CubeSat subsystems, interfaces, objects, processes, and states in one concise representation.", "evidence_source": "A practical utility of Figure 5 is the ability to represent the CubeSat subsystems and their interfaces including objects/processes/states in one DSM/DMM representation.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "The matrix representation identifies mechanical/energy interfaces and associates heating/cooling processes with state changes for the thermal-control subsystem.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[33].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0068", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The result demonstrates representability in a simplified subsystem example; it does not show scalability, correctness against an independent model, or measurable integration benefit."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0068::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">The approach facilitates a digital information flow or digital thread from MBSE conceptual design to PLM/detailed design.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "OPM/DSM/DMM conceptual model elements are mapped to CPM Radiator artifact behavior, function, form, geometry, material, and flow, and to an OPM-CPM DSM ontology map.", "claim_text": "The approach facilitates a digital information flow or digital thread from MBSE conceptual design to PLM/detailed design.", "evidence_source": "Based on the data that is encoded in DSM/DMM in Figure 5 we could trace the flow of data that was created during the conceptual design phase to the next phase of the design process.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "The paper traces the cooling process and related state information from the conceptual model to CPM entities for the Radiator and then maps OPM and CPM ontologies in Figure 7.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[33].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0068", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The mapping is shown as a matrix/table, but no executable exchange, round-trip synchronization, or downstream engineering validation is reported."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0068::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">The proposed DSM-based exchange approach may reduce complexity and errors associated with different ontologies in different design tools and expose exchange gaps.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "DSM/DMM and OPM-CPM ontology map used to relate entities and detect gaps between conceptual and detailed-design ontologies.", "claim_text": "The proposed DSM-based exchange approach may reduce complexity and errors associated with different ontologies in different design tools and expose exchange gaps.", "evidence_source": "A proposed approach might serve as an effective method to reduce complexity associated with different ontologies in different design tools.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative claim only: complexity/error reduction is asserted as an expected utility; no measured reduction is reported.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[33].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0068", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The matrix may make relationships visible, but the paper provides no baseline complexity measure, error data, or user evaluation."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0068::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">The approach can help engage digital tools in a concurrent engineering environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Complementary ontologies and DSM relationships proposed as a basis for a digital engineering environment.", "claim_text": "The approach can help engage digital tools in a concurrent engineering environment.", "evidence_source": "Ultimately, it allows engaging digital tools in a concurrent engineering environment.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "No observed effect; concurrent-engineering application is asserted in the abstract and deferred to future work.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[33].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0068", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No concurrent design session, stakeholder evaluation, collaboration data, or tool-integration demonstration is reported."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0068::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">The same modeling principles can be applied across decomposition levels, supporting a reusable workflow for system and subsystem modeling.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "CubeSat system decomposition and Thermal Control System subsystem decomposition using OPM/DSM/DMM principles.", "claim_text": "The same modeling principles can be applied across decomposition levels, supporting a reusable workflow for system and subsystem modeling.", "evidence_source": "The utility of the proposed approach is that it keeps the same principles regardless of the level of decomposition.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "The method is shown at CubeSat system level and then at Thermal Control System level; reuse across independent missions is not demonstrated.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[33].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0068", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The evidence is recursive use within one illustrative case only, not reuse or replication across projects."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0071::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">A SysML risk model can improve system-level understanding of risks and how they affect subsystems compared with document-based RRM practice.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Risk Management block, risk identification layer, risk attributes layer, RRM elements represented in SysML.", "claim_text": "A SysML risk model can improve system-level understanding of risks and how they affect subsystems compared with document-based RRM practice.", "evidence_source": "Through these proposed risk models, unprecedented levels of systems understanding can be achieved through integrated analytics, coalesced with a model-centric technical baseline.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative only: improved systems understanding and intuitive assessment are asserted; no measured effect size.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[34].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0071", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No populated risk register, baseline comparison, independent validation, or mission outcome evidence is provided; benefits may follow from documentation reorganization rather than MBSE specifically."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0071::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">Layered/hyperlinked SysML artifacts provide traceability and ease of access for validation and verification activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "System architecture BDD, subsystem BDDs, Risk Management block, risk-management layers.", "claim_text": "Layered/hyperlinked SysML artifacts provide traceability and ease of access for validation and verification activities.", "evidence_source": "This structure allows for seamless traceability and ease of access when performing validation and verification activities.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative only: seamless traceability and ease of access are claimed.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[34].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0071", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Traceability is described as hyperlinks/navigation, not as tested requirements/V&amp;V/design-decision trace chains; no trace completeness metric is reported."}</data>
