    <node id="paper-0071::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">Risk Precedence Index and risk-cube color coding enable quick overview, prioritization, and easier access to system/subsystem risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Risk identification use case diagram, RPI thresholds, high/medium/low risk color categories.", "claim_text": "Risk Precedence Index and risk-cube color coding enable quick overview, prioritization, and easier access to system/subsystem risks.", "evidence_source": "This representation helps in providing a quick overview of the risks associated with the system or any of the subsystems of the project.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative only: quick overview and intuitive categorization are asserted.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[34].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0071", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "RPI is a risk-prioritization indicator, not evidence that risks are reduced or decisions improved; thresholds are not validated for this project."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0071::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">The model-based approach reduces document-centric bookkeeping and lets systems engineers focus on value-added risk-management tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Layered SysML model and risk-management model replacing/augmenting RRM documentation.", "claim_text": "The model-based approach reduces document-centric bookkeeping and lets systems engineers focus on value-added risk-management tasks.", "evidence_source": "The proposed model for risk management enables ease of access and optimization, allowing the systems engineers to focus on value added tasks and ensure that a balanced approach is adopted towards managing risks.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative only: ease of access, optimization, and reduced bookkeeping are asserted.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[34].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0071", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No time/effort measurements or user evaluation demonstrate that bookkeeping or workload is actually reduced."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0071::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">A model-based approach supports design-change interpretation, communication of objectives, consistency/completeness assessment, and knowledge reuse compared with scattered documents.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "General MBSE system model and SysML blocks/relations.", "claim_text": "A model-based approach supports design-change interpretation, communication of objectives, consistency/completeness assessment, and knowledge reuse compared with scattered documents.", "evidence_source": "Shifting to a model-based approach enables engineering teams to effortlessly interpret design change consequences, communicate design objectives and examine a system design with greater rigor.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative/generic MBSE rationale only.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[34].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0071", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "This is a generic MBSE argument cited in background, not a demonstrated outcome of the RVSAT-1 risk model."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0071::claim-06">
      <data key="d2">The framework is reusable/modular and can be modified or applied to systems beyond RVSAT-1; future interfaces may improve development and verification efficiency/quality.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Layered SysML framework; proposed future MATLAB Systems Composer/Simulink interfaces.", "claim_text": "The framework is reusable/modular and can be modified or applied to systems beyond RVSAT-1; future interfaces may improve development and verification efficiency/quality.", "evidence_source": "Though developed for RVSAT-1, a student nano-satellite, this approach can be utilized for other complex systems as well.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Future/qualitative only; no reuse or interoperability demonstration.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[34].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "study_id": "paper-0071", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No reuse across projects, model package, or implemented interface is reported; future integration may require nontrivial toolchain work."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0077::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">Using CSRM as the basis for a mission-specific CubeSat model enables reuse of logical components and sharing/reuse across design activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "CSRM logical architecture and logical components reused to create MSM logical architecture.", "claim_text": "Using CSRM as the basis for a mission-specific CubeSat model enables reuse of logical components and sharing/reuse across design activities.", "evidence_source": "The CSRM logical components are intended to be reused as a starting point for a mission-specific CubeSat logical architecture followed by the development of physical architecture during CubeSat development.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative reuse mechanism asserted; no measured reuse count or effort saving.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[35].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0077", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["No reported mission-team reuse outcome or replication evidence.", "The model is not pre-populated with mission-specific requirements and must be tailored."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0077::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">The MSM can serve as the single central design baseline throughout development and operations, replacing dispersed document-centric artifacts.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Mission-specific CubeSat Model maintained across development and operations.", "claim_text": "The MSM can serve as the single central design baseline throughout development and operations, replacing dispersed document-centric artifacts.", "evidence_source": "The MSM is maintained throughout all phases of development and operations as the single and central design baseline.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Central baseline continuity asserted; no observed effect size.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[35].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0077", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["No evidence that a real mission maintained an MSM through operations.", "No baseline comparison to document-centric process is measured."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0077::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">Explicit relationships among stakeholders, concerns, requirements, use cases, and technical measures support traceability, completeness, and stakeholder alignment.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Stakeholder Concern, Mission Need, Mission Objective, Mission Constraint, Mission Requirement, Use Case, MOE/MOP/TPM specification relationships and tables.", "claim_text": "Explicit relationships among stakeholders, concerns, requirements, use cases, and technical measures support traceability, completeness, and stakeholder alignment.", "evidence_source": "The CSRM has model elements for stakeholders, concerns, mission needs, mission objectives, mission constraints and mission requirements. These model elements and their relationships are mission and engineering methodology specific.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Conceptual traceability structure shown; no coverage metric reported.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[35].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0077", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["Completeness depends on mission-team tailoring and population.", "No stakeholder evaluation is reported."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0077::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">Verification and validation activities linked to requirements, technical measures, mission objectives, and stakeholders support mission assurance and requirements satisfaction evidence.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Verification Activity, Validation Activity, Requirement, Technical Measure, Mission Objective, test cases, and linked Word/activity documents.", "claim_text": "Verification and validation activities linked to requirements, technical measures, mission objectives, and stakeholders support mission assurance and requirements satisfaction evidence.", "evidence_source": "The verify relationship is a relationship between a requirement and a test case or other model element that is used to verify the requirement is satisfied.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "The paper defines traceable V&amp;V structures but reports no executed verification/validation results.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[35].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0077", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["V&amp;V is conceptual and generic, not EPS-specific.", "No physical test, simulation, or flight evidence is reported."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0077::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">Web-published CSRM, XMI files, and exportable tables improve model access, interoperability, and reviewability for mission teams and external reviewers.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Foundational CSRM, Web Published CSRM, CSRM XMI File, exported CSRM tables.", "claim_text": "Web-published CSRM, XMI files, and exportable tables improve model access, interoperability, and reviewability for mission teams and external reviewers.", "evidence_source": "The Web Published CSRM allows a user to explore and evaluate the CSRM without the need to acquire a graphical modeling tool. The CSRM XMI File is the OMG normative specification.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Access/interoperability mechanisms asserted; no interoperability test or user evaluation reported.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[35].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0077", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["No model URL or XMI file is provided in the paper.", "Tool compatibility is not demonstrated."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0077::claim-06">
      <data key="d2">Technical measures and component property roll-up can provide stakeholders with insight for design assessment and decision support.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Technical Measure specifications/methods and component power, weight, cost, and performance properties.", "claim_text": "Technical measures and component property roll-up can provide stakeholders with insight for design assessment and decision support.", "evidence_source": "Technical Measures provide a stakeholder insight into the definition and development of a technical solution.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Potential design insight asserted; no trade-study or parametric result is reported.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[35].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "study_id": "paper-0077", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["Parametrics for power, weight, and cost are explicitly not added to CSRM in this status.", "No analysis results or decision examples are reported."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0077::claim-07">
      <data key="d2">CSRM validation against OMG RFP requirements, Practical Guide model-evaluation criteria, and mission-team evaluations supports governance and model quality assurance.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "OMG CSRM RFP requirements, CSRM validation tables, Practical Guide model validation questions/requirements, trusted partner evaluation plan.", "claim_text": "CSRM validation against OMG RFP requirements, Practical Guide model-evaluation criteria, and mission-team evaluations supports governance and model quality assurance.", "evidence_source": "Satisfaction of the requirements will be recorded in the tables with links to CSRM elements and packages. The tables can be exported for external review.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Validation approach described; no completed independent validation results are reported.", "source_claim_id": "C7", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[35].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[6]", "study_id": "paper-0077", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": ["Initial satisfaction is based on development-team judgment.", "Mission-specific team evaluation is proposed as future/better evaluation."]}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0078::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">MBSE managed technical consistency across architectural documents, ensuring coherency and minimizing errors.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Capella/Arcadia model containing requirements, architecture, interfaces, and architectural documents.", "claim_text": "MBSE managed technical consistency across architectural documents, ensuring coherency and minimizing errors.", "evidence_source": "Through Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE), technical consistency was rigorously managed across various architectural documents, ensuring coherency and minimizing errors.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Authors report coherency/minimized errors qualitatively; no defect counts are provided.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[36].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0078", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No defect baseline or independent check; Agile meetings and centralized governance may also explain consistency improvements."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0078::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">Capella/Arcadia established bidirectional traceability from needs/requirements to functions, logical/physical components, and test cases, supporting continuous verification and validation.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Capella Requirement Viewpoint, traceability links, requirement allocation matrix, logical/physical architecture, test cases and validation criteria.", "claim_text": "Capella/Arcadia established bidirectional traceability from needs/requirements to functions, logical/physical components, and test cases, supporting continuous verification and validation.", "evidence_source": "Bidirectional traceability was established to ensure that each requirement could be traced forward to its corresponding design elements and backward to its source.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Detailed traceability mechanisms and examples are reported, but no quantitative coverage percentage is given.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[36].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0078", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Traceability is author-reported; no model export or independent verification of link completeness is provided."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0078::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">The integrated Agile/Arcadia/Capella approach streamlined preliminary design and completed it in about four months.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Weekly general sprints, subsystem backlogs, Arcadia process framework, centralized Capella model.", "claim_text": "The integrated Agile/Arcadia/Capella approach streamlined preliminary design and completed it in about four months.", "evidence_source": "the preliminary design process was streamlined and completed within an accelerated time frame of 4 months, with weekly sprints driving progress based on the scrum methodology", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Reported preliminary-design duration of 4 months; authors state this is within/favorable to ECSS/NASA recommended 1-6 month ranges, but no counterfactual team/process was used.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[36].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0078", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No traditional-process comparator; schedule may reflect project scope, team size, proposal deadlines, or prior internal documents."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0078::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">The shared Capella model and Agile coordination improved communication, alignment, and integration among distributed subsystem teams.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Unified Capella model, weekly cross-functional meetings, subsystem-specific backlogs, centralized model updates.", "claim_text": "The shared Capella model and Agile coordination improved communication, alignment, and integration among distributed subsystem teams.", "evidence_source": "This case study highlights the effectiveness of Agile Systems Engineering principles to improve the team communication accuracy, communication, and efficiency", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Authors report improved communication and easier integration qualitatively; no stakeholder survey or communication metric is given.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[36].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0078", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Collaboration gains may be due to weekly meetings, management effort, or institutional roles rather than MBSE artifacts alone."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0078::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">MBSE supported early requirement identification, risk management, performance optimization, avoidance of rework, and a more reliable design.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Capella model, power budget, thermal analysis, orbital/link-budget simulations, validation checks.", "claim_text": "MBSE supported early requirement identification, risk management, performance optimization, avoidance of rework, and a more reliable design.", "evidence_source": "MBSE facilitated the early identification of key requirements, efficient risk management, and the optimization of system performance.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Technical feasibility indicators include simulated contacts/lifetime, power/energy budgets, and thermal limits; no direct reliability metric or flight evidence is provided.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[36].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0078", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Technical analyses support feasibility but do not prove MBSE caused reliability improvement; physical tests and flight evidence are absent."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0078::claim-06">
      <data key="d2">The presented Agile/MBSE workflow provides reusable guidance and a precedent for future CubeSat missions.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Arcadia method stages, Capella model architecture, Agile sprint framework, model governance roles.", "claim_text": "The presented Agile/MBSE workflow provides reusable guidance and a precedent for future CubeSat missions.", "evidence_source": "providing valuable insights for future missions", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "The paper offers case-based process knowledge but no reuse across multiple missions.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[36].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "study_id": "paper-0078", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Generality is asserted from one mission case; no replication or downloadable template/model is provided."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0079::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">SysML supports more structured and transparent nanosatellite requirements development and verification, with improved traceability and consistency.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SysML requirement stereotypes, requirement diagrams/tables, derive/trace/refine/satisfy relations, requirements package.", "claim_text": "SysML supports more structured and transparent nanosatellite requirements development and verification, with improved traceability and consistency.", "evidence_source": "System requirements are derived by means of the following sequence of suggested activities ... Derive system requirements from mission requirements, Use Cases, system context diagram mission phases diagram and functional analysis ... Model 'derived', 'trace', or 'Refine' relations when applicable in new requirements diagrams.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative: requirements traceability 'very much improved' and model consistency assured by cross-checks; no counts or baseline.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[37].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0079", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Improvement is asserted from one case without a measured comparison to the prior document-centric process; relation semantics were noted as ambiguous."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0079::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">Executable SysML connected to MATLAB/Simulink can automatically verify an ADCS design requirement before hardware by running simulations and updating requirement status.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "ADCS-F.34 detumbling requirement refined to a constraint block; ADCS4simulation parametric model; ParaSolver/Artisan Studio to MATLAB/Simulink; requirement status TBC-to-Satisfied.", "claim_text": "Executable SysML connected to MATLAB/Simulink can automatically verify an ADCS design requirement before hardware by running simulations and updating requirement status.", "evidence_source": "ADCSF.34 is connected to a constraint block by means of 'refine' relationship. This is the way SysML adopts indicate that a requirement can be analyzed executi parametric models.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "The detumble simulation indicated angular rates reached the requirement goal by the one-day limit and ADCS-F.34 changed from TBC to Satisfied.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[37].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0079", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Only the detumble mode is presented; simulation correctness and model fidelity are not independently validated; result concerns ADCS, not EPS."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0079::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">Model sharing between MBSE and MDE reuses early ADCS models for onboard software development and allows engineers to focus more on models than programming.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Simulink ADCS blocks verified using executable SysML, then translated to hardware-independent C and fed back as code verification model.", "claim_text": "Model sharing between MBSE and MDE reuses early ADCS models for onboard software development and allows engineers to focus more on models than programming.", "evidence_source": "From the case study of DelFFi, it can be observed that the key of both MBSE and MDE-based onboard software development is the model. Therefore a bridge between MBSE and onboard software development can be built up through model sharing.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative/proposed: earlier ADCS models can be reused and programming duplication reduced; no measured effort saving.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[37].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0079", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The bridge to code/HIL/FM is described as an approach and 'foreseen' steps, with no completed HIL or flight evidence in the paper."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0079::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">Automatic generation from executable Simulink solutions and consistency between simulation models and onboard software should improve code/product quality and reliability.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Executable Simulink Solution to C code; onboard software testing/operation; consistency of model and code across stages.", "claim_text": "Automatic generation from executable Simulink solutions and consistency between simulation models and onboard software should improve code/product quality and reliability.", "evidence_source": "If the Simulink Solution works well and the AOCS/GNC algorithms have been executed so far with desirable results in simulation, the C code be generated directly from an executable Simulink Solution. On this basis, the Onboard Software is ready for testing and after some necessary items will be the exact software running in operation.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Expected qualitative increase in reliability/quality from structural consistency; no defect, failure, or test metric.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[37].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0079", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Reliability/quality is expected rather than demonstrated; generated code still requires integration with low-level software and verification."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0079::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">Reusable Simulink model libraries and flexible configurations enable quick response to changing requirements and reduce design time.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Models &amp; Blocks library, Simulink Solution, iterative modification of models/parameters/algorithms.", "claim_text": "Reusable Simulink model libraries and flexible configurations enable quick response to changing requirements and reduce design time.", "evidence_source": "This is basically a set of libraries which collect the MATLAB/Simulink models, including the spacecraft hardware (sensors/actuators), kinematics dynamics, the space environment, as well as some generic functions and algorithms.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Expected faster configuration/reconfiguration and reduced design time; no schedule metric.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[37].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0079", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The schedule benefit may depend on model library maturity, tool expertise, and mission similarity; no measured before/after data."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0079::claim-06">
      <data key="d2">A collaborative MBSE workspace can seamlessly integrate requirement development, model verification, automatic code generation, and verification with high efficiency and quality.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Executable SysML workspace integrating requirement model, ADCS model, verification model, code verification model, generated ADCS C code, and flight model verification links.", "claim_text": "A collaborative MBSE workspace can seamlessly integrate requirement development, model verification, automatic code generation, and verification with high efficiency and quality.", "evidence_source": "A collaborative MBSE workspace/environment is provided. This workspace integrates discipline-specific models capable of performing all aspects of the system definition. With proper construction of Simulink models and wrap-up of engineering model and flight model of onboard software, this workspace even allows a seamless integration of requirement development, model verification, code automatic generation and verification with high efficiency and quality.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative claim of seamless integration and high efficiency/quality; only partial toolchain demonstration is reported.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[37].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "study_id": "paper-0079", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Workspace integration is not evaluated against manual processes or alternative toolchains; proprietary tool dependencies may affect generalization."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0080::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">MBSE/SysML improves consistency, traceability, V&amp;V, and change-impact assessment compared with document/tool-spread traditional SE.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "SysML model repository, requirements diagrams, trace/derive/satisfy/verify/refine relationships, generated traceability and verification matrices.", "claim_text": "MBSE/SysML improves consistency, traceability, V&amp;V, and change-impact assessment compared with document/tool-spread traditional SE.", "evidence_source": "MBSE provides a consistent and automatically traceable system design, which enhances the quality of traceability and change impact assessment.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative: authors state tool-generated matrices and impact analysis are time-saving and helpful for NSS-1 V&amp;V; no effect size.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0080", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No measured trace coverage, defect rate, or comparison with the previous process; benefits may follow from disciplined requirements work rather than SysML alone."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0080::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">SysML parametric constraints linked to requirements verify NSS-1 mass and power budget margins before physical development.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Mass_Balance and Power_Balance constraint blocks, Figure 9 parametric diagram, Figure 12 verify relationship, ParaMagic/MATLAB SMT solver.", "claim_text": "SysML parametric constraints linked to requirements verify NSS-1 mass and power budget margins before physical development.", "evidence_source": "After connecting the parameter ports to respective inputs and outputs, we validated the model using ParaMagic.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "mass_MOS=0.082 and power_MOS=0.47, both positive, verify the mass and power requirements; no baseline.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0080", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Verification covers simple budget equations only; input values and assumptions are not independently validated; no physical EPS test or full EPS behavior model."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0080::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">Connecting SysML to Excel and MATLAB/Simulink enables interoperability and on-the-fly parameter tuning using existing SE tools.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "MagicDraw Excel import/export, ParaMagic instance slots, InterCAX MATLAB integration, intermediary MATLAB scripts for Simulink.", "claim_text": "Connecting SysML to Excel and MATLAB/Simulink enables interoperability and on-the-fly parameter tuning using existing SE tools.", "evidence_source": "Seamless interface of existing system-level design tools (Satellite Tool Kit [STK], matrix laboratory [MATLAB]/ Simulink, and Microsoft Excel) with the SysML satellite model to assist on-the-fly parameter tuning", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative data-flow demonstration between SysML, spreadsheets, and MATLAB; no quantified tuning-time reduction.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0080", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "STK direct integration is future work; interfaces rely on proprietary plug-ins and local scripts; no semantic consistency checks across tools are reported."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0080::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">The NSS-1 model repository supports reuse, generic nanosatellite patterns, and knowledge transfer to future missions such as NSS-2.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "FireSat-derived elements, NSS-1 SysML repository, common design patterns, Figure 2 model reuse path to NSS-2.", "claim_text": "The NSS-1 model repository supports reuse, generic nanosatellite patterns, and knowledge transfer to future missions such as NSS-2.", "evidence_source": "We reused some model elements from the FireSat SysML model", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative reuse path; no reuse across multiple completed missions is demonstrated.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0080", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Reuse for NSS-2 is prospective; no released reusable library/template or replication evidence."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0080::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">Automatic report/table/code generation from SysML supports automated systems engineering and downstream simulation/software implementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Allocation tables, requirement tables, coverage analysis, code structure in Java/C++/C#.", "claim_text": "Automatic report/table/code generation from SysML supports automated systems engineering and downstream simulation/software implementation.", "evidence_source": "from SysML models, an allocation table, a requirement table, and coverage analysis are generated automatically from the model repository", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Generated artifacts are described; no generated artifact sample counts, defect reduction, or implementation evidence.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0080", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "The paper does not show generated reports/code or demonstrate software integration outcomes."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0080::claim-06">
      <data key="d2">Extensible SysML structures reduced model development time and are expected to reduce future cost to change designs.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "BDD physical architecture and extensible system structures.", "claim_text": "Extensible SysML structures reduced model development time and are expected to reduce future cost to change designs.", "evidence_source": "We have also adopted design techniques for creating extensible system structures. This practice reduced the model development time. In the future, this will also reduce the cost to change the design", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Authors state reduced model development time and future cost-to-change reduction, without quantitative effect size.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "study_id": "paper-0080", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No time/cost data or baseline; future cost reduction is prospective."}</data>
    </node>
