      <data key="d2">Overall MBSE approach is promising for reduced development risk, improved quality, and increased productivity.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "General NSS-1 model repository and concluding synthesis of advantages.", "claim_text": "Overall MBSE approach is promising for reduced development risk, improved quality, and increased productivity.", "evidence_source": "The model-based approach is found to be promising for a reduced development risk, improved quality, and increased productivity.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "No effect size; conclusion-level assertion.", "source_claim_id": "C7", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[6]", "study_id": "paper-0080", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Could reflect author expectation from method adoption rather than observed NSS-1 outcomes."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0080::claim-08">
      <data key="d2">SysML diagrams improve communication and make missing or relevant design information easier to find.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Use-case diagrams, package navigation, formal diagram semantics, model repository.", "claim_text": "SysML diagrams improve communication and make missing or relevant design information easier to find.", "evidence_source": "Users, project managers, analysts, developers, quality-assurance engineers, and anyone else interested in the system as a whole can inspect these diagrams and understand what the system is supposed to accomplish.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative: diagrams can be inspected by stakeholders and point out missing design information.", "source_claim_id": "C8", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[7]", "study_id": "paper-0080", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "No stakeholder evaluation; authors also warn diagrams may be misinterpreted without SysML training."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0081::claim-01">
      <data key="d2">Automated object-oriented/System-as-Code workflow supports fast, consistent deployment of satellite digital models across missions.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Python4Capella/custom API generation of Capella model elements from standard functional libraries and reusable baselines.", "claim_text": "Automated object-oriented/System-as-Code workflow supports fast, consistent deployment of satellite digital models across missions.", "evidence_source": "An automated framework was developed to support fast, consistent deployment of satellite digital models across missions", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Feasibility and technical potential demonstrated; no quantitative deployment-time or effort reduction reported.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[39].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "study_id": "paper-0081", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Single demonstration mission; manual process comparator not quantified; authors also report higher initial modeling effort."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0081::claim-02">
      <data key="d2">Functional grouping and functional libraries improve modularity, reuse, and replicability of satellite platform architectures.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "System Support capability groups, pre-validated logical baselines, and Use Case Functional Libraries for functions/components/exchanges.", "claim_text": "Functional grouping and functional libraries improve modularity, reuse, and replicability of satellite platform architectures.", "evidence_source": "multiple baselines are often available, each representing a pre-validated logical architecture reused from previous missions", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Pilot confirmed technical potential and functional library integration, but reuse across multiple real missions was not shown.", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[39].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "study_id": "paper-0081", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Reuse is demonstrated as architecture/library feasibility, not measured replication across projects; underlying standard baselines are not provided."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0081::claim-03">
      <data key="d2">The approach strengthens traceability from stakeholder needs and mission objectives to system functions, logical architecture, physical architecture, and design decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "ARCADIA OA/SA/LA/PA layers, capabilities, functional elements/interfaces/connections, logical components, product breakdown, and documentation.", "claim_text": "The approach strengthens traceability from stakeholder needs and mission objectives to system functions, logical architecture, physical architecture, and design decisions.", "evidence_source": "This approach strengthens traceability between stakeholder needs and system functionality", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Traceability is structurally argued and diagrammed, but no trace coverage or concrete requirement-to-verification matrix is reported.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[39].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "study_id": "paper-0081", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Traceability could depend on disciplined library/model maintenance; no empirical trace-audit evidence."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0081::claim-04">
      <data key="d2">Python4Capella-based APIs and structured data sources enable bidirectional model-data interaction and improve toolchain interoperability/digital-thread continuity.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Python4Capella scripts/custom APIs connecting Capella to Excel, JSON, YAML/spreadsheets, PVMT, and external data sources/simulation environments.", "claim_text": "Python4Capella-based APIs and structured data sources enable bidirectional model-data interaction and improve toolchain interoperability/digital-thread continuity.", "evidence_source": "Through Python4Capella, it becomes possible to dynamically access and update model elements, enabling bidirectional integration with external data sources and simulation environments.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Bidirectional data flow and automated generation were demonstrated; no interoperability failure-rate or data-integrity metric is reported.", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[39].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "study_id": "paper-0081", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "External-source examples are limited; simulation environment integration is described as possible rather than demonstrated in detail."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0081::claim-05">
      <data key="d2">The automated workflow can generate semantically correct and structurally consistent models without omissions or unintended artifacts.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Generated Capella model elements and functional group implementations checked by manual inspection, functional-library tests, interconnection validation, and Capella built-in validation tools.", "claim_text": "The automated workflow can generate semantically correct and structurally consistent models without omissions or unintended artifacts.", "evidence_source": "ensuring that automation produced the correct elements without omissions or unintended artifacts", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Authors report confirmation of semantic correctness and structural consistency; no defect counts or pass/fail coverage reported.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[39].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "study_id": "paper-0081", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Manual inspection may miss issues; checks are not independently replicated or quantified."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0081::claim-06">
      <data key="d2">The approach supports model variability and configuration management for mission-specific customization of standardized satellite platforms.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "Baseline logical architectures, 150% models via the Filtering Add-On, inclusion/dependency fields in functional libraries, and mission-specific extension of imported baselines.", "claim_text": "The approach supports model variability and configuration management for mission-specific customization of standardized satellite platforms.", "evidence_source": "the most appropriate baseline can be imported into the current model and extended to accommodate mission-specific elements", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Initial support for model variability is reported; no configuration-selection or trade-study result is provided.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[39].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "study_id": "paper-0081", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Variability support is initial; no evidence of decisions made, configurations compared, or mission variants deployed."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0081::claim-07">
      <data key="d2">Despite higher initial modeling effort, faster deployment and consistent reusability outweigh short-term cost and can reduce implementation time and error.</data>
      <data key="d3">Claim</data>
      <data key="d4">{"artifact_or_process_linked": "System-as-Code automation and scriptable initialization of functional libraries from dedicated models.", "claim_text": "Despite higher initial modeling effort, faster deployment and consistent reusability outweigh short-term cost and can reduce implementation time and error.", "evidence_source": "While the initial modeling effort is higher... the benefits in terms of faster model deployment and consistent reusability outweigh the short-term cost.", "field_path": "claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]", "observed_effect_or_qualitative_effect": "Qualitative author assertion; no numerical cost, schedule, effort, or defect reduction is provided.", "source_claim_id": "C7", "source_codebook_version": "1.1", "source_generated_at": "2026-05-28T15:59:44-06:00", "source_path": "studies[39].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[6]", "study_id": "paper-0081", "threats_or_alternative_explanations": "Cost/schedule benefits could be offset by custom API maintenance and manual library construction; no quantified baseline."}</data>
    </node>
    <node id="paper-0081::claim-08">
      <data key="d2">The digital-thread model improves accessibility of model information and supports multidisciplinary decisions, including physical-architecture decisions such as PCDU/electronics layout and cable routing when power-demanding components are added.</data>
