      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">When the solar panel area was reduced further, to a quarter of the nominal, the energy level went below the required minimum at the end of the simulation... The results clearly show that the quarter size solar panel is too small for the mission.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0001::claim-05", "claim_text": "Solar-panel area trade study supports EPS design decision-making by showing nominal and half-size panels satisfy the energy requirement while quarter-size panels are too small.", "evidence_confidence": "Moderate", "observed_effect": "Quarter-size solar panel falls below the required minimum by the end of the simulation; half-size and nominal remain within bounds.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_path": "studies[0].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0001::claim-05", "study_id": "paper-0001"}</data>
