      <data key="d7">automation</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Section 5: 'SLIM enables systems engineers to develop a high-level system model in SysML and connect it to domain-specific models, such as Bills of Materials (BOMs) and Computer Aided Design (CAD)... managed in various enterprise product lifecycle management systems.' Section 5 Use Case 1: 'the block structure is used to generate a part structure in a PLM system Windchill ... Connections are saved between the corresponding parts and blocks so that changes on either side can be synchronized as desired.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0008::claim-05", "claim_text": "SLIM links SysML blocks to PLM parts/BOMs, enabling generation/synchronization of part structures and continuity from systems architecture to mechanical/electrical design.", "evidence_confidence": "Moderate", "observed_effect": "Demonstrates generation of a Windchill part structure from a SysML block structure and saved connections for synchronization; compare/sync maturity is future work.", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::claim-05", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
