      <data key="d9">Abstract/Section 6: 'a modeling framework that allows for analyzing and costing the technical design of the spacecraft throughout the lifecycle of the mission will allow for more robust and reusable designs.' Introduction/third phase: 'a bottom-up development process to address the reliability of CubeSats and stakeholder concerns.'</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0008::claim-08", "claim_text": "The modeling framework should lead to more robust and reusable CubeSat designs and address reliability/stakeholder concerns by combining top-down architecture with bottom-up component/interface/task overhead estimation.", "evidence_confidence": "Unsupported", "observed_effect": "Robustness/reliability is an intended design benefit; the paper does not report reliability analysis, failure-rate improvement, or flight evidence.", "source_claim_id": "C8", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[7]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::claim-08", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
