      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The CSRM provides a library of model elements but does not dictate what model elements and relationships to use... The CSRM is well-documented and explains to the team how to populate it...</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0011::claim-06", "claim_text": "The CSRM can be adapted to different mission methods because it is methodology-agnostic, provides instructions, and lets teams populate or modify model elements and containment trees.", "evidence_confidence": "Weak", "observed_effect": "Partial adoption guidance and tailoring flexibility; no measured adoption effort.", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_path": "studies[8].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "source_record_id": "paper-0011::claim-06", "study_id": "paper-0011"}</data>
