    <edge source="paper-0023::claim-01" target="outcomecategory::communication_stakeholder_alignment" id="e0000642">
      <data key="d5">CLAIMS_OUTCOME</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[].outcome_category</data>
      <data key="d7">communication/stakeholder alignment</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Section 2: "The aim of using MBSE for a nanosatellite project is to create a model framework or repository that can be used by university teams (with limited resources) wishing to design CubeSat or Nanosatellite projects. This type of formal modeling application will guide them through the entire nanosatellite mission design and management process (mission analysis, system design verification, and validation)." Section 3.2/Fig. 4: the authors adopt "an MBSE Framework approach based on a model comprising a consistent set of views reflecting multiple viewpoints and stages in the nanosatellite project"; Fig. 4 shows Mission Analysis, System Formal Design, System Production &amp; Integration, and System Deployment &amp; Operation views.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0023::claim-01", "claim_text": "A reusable MBSE framework/repository can guide limited-resource university teams through nanosatellite mission design and management, including mission analysis, design verification, and validation.", "evidence_confidence": "Weak", "observed_effect": "Framework and MASAT1 package examples are presented as reusable guidance; reuse beyond MASAT1 is not demonstrated.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_path": "studies[15].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0023::claim-01", "study_id": "paper-0023"}</data>
    </edge>
