      <data key="d7">consistency</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">From these graphs, we can infer that the power and data balances are stable, i.e. the satellite is capable of charging the batteries for the amount used each orbit, and download the generated mission data. This means, for this perspective, that this is a valid operation scenario.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0033::claim-01", "claim_text": "The cyber-physical MAM plus MBSE toolchain enables visual configuration and verification/validation of CubeSat operations scenarios by modeling and simulation.", "evidence_confidence": "Moderate", "observed_effect": "Final NCBR2 simulation was judged a valid operation scenario because power and data balances were stable.", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_path": "studies[21].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0033::claim-01", "study_id": "paper-0033"}</data>
