    <edge source="paper-0079::claim-03" target="outcomecategory::effort_reduction" id="e0001075">
      <data key="d5">CLAIMS_OUTCOME</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[].outcome_category</data>
      <data key="d7">effort reduction</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">From the case study of DelFFi, it can be observed that the key of both MBSE and MDE-based onboard software development is the model. Therefore a bridge between MBSE and onboard software development can be built up through model sharing.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0079::claim-03", "claim_text": "Model sharing between MBSE and MDE reuses early ADCS models for onboard software development and allows engineers to focus more on models than programming.", "evidence_confidence": "Weak", "observed_effect": "Qualitative/proposed: earlier ADCS models can be reused and programming duplication reduced; no measured effort saving.", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_path": "studies[37].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0079::claim-03", "study_id": "paper-0079"}</data>
    </edge>
