      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_physical_test_or_flight_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">The model is executable and simulation-based; no flat-sat, hardware test, environmental test, operational, or flight evidence is reported for the MBSE outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d9">EPS integration_test_readiness is not_reported in the completed extraction; the paper's results are Figures 14-19 simulations/trade studies rather than tests or flight operations.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[0].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[5]", "source_record_id": "paper-0001::limitation-06", "study_id": "paper-0001"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="limitationflag::no_quantitative_evaluation" id="e0003798">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_quantitative_evaluation</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper reports quantitative mission-performance simulations, but it does not quantitatively evaluate MBSE adoption benefits such as effort, defects, schedule, or cost savings.</data>
      <data key="d9">Completed extraction: outcome evidence metrics are on-board energy level and downloaded data; governance/ROI evidence is not_reported and no effort/defect/schedule/cost metric for MBSE value is present.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[0].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0001::limitation-03", "study_id": "paper-0001"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="limitationflag::prototype_or_future_work" id="e0003799">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">prototype_or_future_work</data>
      <data key="d8">The authors explicitly frame the model as a prototype and describe future availability/extension rather than a completed operational asset.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 1: 'intended as a prototype to prove out the applicability of MBSE... It is not intended to be an accurate model of the RAX satellite.' Conclusion: 'We are planning to make available the RAX CubeSat model and associated manual...'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[0].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0001::limitation-01", "study_id": "paper-0001"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="limitationflag::single_case_or_limited_scope" id="e0003800">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">single_case_or_limited_scope</data>
      <data key="d8">The demonstrated model is for one RAX CubeSat case and is limited to selected energy/data behavior.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4: 'The proof of concept is limited to modeling energy collection and management as well as data collection and management.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[0].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0001::limitation-02", "study_id": "paper-0001"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="limitationflag::tool_dependency_or_vendor_lockin" id="e0003801">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">tool_dependency_or_vendor_lockin</data>
      <data key="d8">The implementation depends on a named proprietary COTS stack; the paper does not discuss open alternatives or license impacts.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4 lists 'COTS modeling and simulation tools' including MagicDraw/CST, ModelCenter/MBSE Analyzer, STK, and MATLAB.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[0].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[7]", "source_record_id": "paper-0001::limitation-08", "study_id": "paper-0001"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="limitationflag::weak_claim_evidence_linkage" id="e0003802">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">weak_claim_evidence_linkage</data>
      <data key="d8">Concrete trade-study claims are supported, but broad claims about scalability, utility, consistency, and future reuse are not measured independently.</data>
      <data key="d9">Claim records C1 and C9 are rated Unsupported and C8 Weak; no scalability, reuse, or adoption-benefit metric is reported.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[0].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[10]", "source_record_id": "paper-0001::limitation-11", "study_id": "paper-0001"}</data>
    </edge>
