    <edge source="paper-0001" target="reusemechanism::high_level_abstraction" id="e0005520">
      <data key="d5">HAS_REUSE_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d6">mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">high-level abstraction</data>
      <data key="d8">The reusable contribution is a RAX-specific executable CubeSat model and workflow based on a prior CubeSat reference model. The paper supports high-level and non-detailed abstraction because non-critical subsystems are excluded/grouped and states are binary, while reuse is claimed as a starting point for other CubeSat teams. It does not support mission-agnostic architecture, interface-focused model, or open package: the demonstrated model remains RAX-specific and release is only planned.</data>
      <data key="d9">The first phase of the SSWG MBSE CubeSat project consisted of developing a SysML reference model of a CubeSat, and then applying the reference model to model RAX.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["high"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[0].extraction.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism", "studies[0].structured_code_summary.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0001::code-0044", "paper-0001::code-0164"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0001", "value_index": 4}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="reusemechanism::low_dynamics_non_detailed_behavior_model" id="e0005521">
      <data key="d5">HAS_REUSE_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d6">mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">low-dynamics / non-detailed-behavior model</data>
      <data key="d8">The reusable contribution is a RAX-specific executable CubeSat model and workflow based on a prior CubeSat reference model. The paper supports high-level and non-detailed abstraction because non-critical subsystems are excluded/grouped and states are binary, while reuse is claimed as a starting point for other CubeSat teams. It does not support mission-agnostic architecture, interface-focused model, or open package: the demonstrated model remains RAX-specific and release is only planned.</data>
      <data key="d9">The first phase of the SSWG MBSE CubeSat project consisted of developing a SysML reference model of a CubeSat, and then applying the reference model to model RAX.</data>
