    <edge source="paper-0002" target="reusemechanism::high_level_abstraction" id="e0005526">
      <data key="d5">HAS_REUSE_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d6">mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">high-level abstraction</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper presents a repeatable eight-step method tied to the CubeSat Reference Model and uses generic CubeSat mission-data requirements/use cases that teams can tailor to unique missions. High-level abstraction and mission-agnostic architecture are supported only at the generic CubeSat enterprise / mission-data functional-architecture level. Do not code interface-focused model because interfaces are future work; do not code low-dynamics / non-detailed-behavior model because limited behavior detail is a scope limitation, not a claimed reuse mechanism; do not code specific-mission model with reusable method only because the examples are generic/reference-model examples, not a named specific mission.</data>
      <data key="d9">This approach provides a repeatable, generalized method for CubeSat development teams to follow</data>
