    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::assumptions_or_data_quality_limits" id="e0003818">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">assumptions_or_data_quality_limits</data>
      <data key="d8">The SNR analysis assumes a single ground station; the behavior model is a simplified representation and useful simulation is described as iterative; some operational parameters can be unknown or not modeled early.</data>
      <data key="d9">In this example, we assume there is a single ground station. ... A model is a simplified representation of the actual system ... creating a model that allows for useful simulation and analysis is an iterative process. ... key operational parameters ... are often unknown or not modeled.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[6]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-07", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::figure_dependent_quantitative_evidence" id="e0003819">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">figure-dependent-quantitative-evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">Several numerical results and power-workflow variables are available mainly through figure descriptions/screenshots rather than text tables, limiting independent scrutiny from the markdown extraction.</data>
      <data key="d9">Figure 13 description reports p_dl=0.101 and r_dl=94,719.799; Figure 14 description reports power variables and violation metrics, but the text does not provide a complete numerical power-results table.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-16", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::incomplete_lifecycle_coverage" id="e0003820">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">incomplete_lifecycle_coverage</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper aspires to full lifecycle DWWYFW use but reports separate demonstrations; combined simulations, schedule verification, dynamic constraint solving, and real-data validation are future work.</data>
      <data key="d9">The various simulations in this paper currently execute individually. Future work will bring these simulations together ... The ability to verify optimal scheduling algorithms ... would be extremely useful ... Finally, comparing results ... to real data ...</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[11]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-12", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::interoperability_limitations" id="e0003821">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">interoperability_limitations</data>
      <data key="d8">Tool integration requires wrapper files and save/reopen cycles, debugging wrapped MATLAB/STK models is difficult, STK wrapping into ParaMagic is prototype-stage, and simulations are not yet unified.</data>
      <data key="d9">Setting up the simulation environment requires several steps, including creating wrapper files, wrapping models, saving, and re-opening models ... difficult to de-bug Matlab code and STK scenarios after they have been wrapped ... The various simulations in this paper currently execute individually.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[8]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-09", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::learning_curve_or_training_burden" id="e0003822">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">learning_curve_or_training_burden</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper reports that beginners could contribute but found SysML easier with prior CubeSat mission or tool experience, indicating a training/domain-knowledge dependency.</data>
      <data key="d9">Beginners found the learning curve reasonable ... Beginners found working with SysML easier if they had experience with the CubeSat mission itself or other tools that were incorporated into the framework (e.g. STK, Matlab).</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[9]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-10", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::lineage_or_duplicate_reference_model_overlap" id="e0003823">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">lineage_or_duplicate_reference_model_overlap</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper explicitly extends a 2012 IEEE Aerospace CubeSat MBSE paper and is part of the INCOSE Space Systems Challenge lineage; synthesis should avoid double-counting framework reuse as independent evidence.</data>
      <data key="d9">This paper extends the work reported in our 2012 IEEE Aerospace conference paper ... Our follow-on CubeSat project was initiated in April 2011 ... The INCOSE Space Systems Working Group (SSWG) established the Space Systems Challenge team.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[13]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-14", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::model_not_available" id="e0003824">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">model_not_available</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper describes plans for a CubeSat model development kit and many diagrams/workflows, but does not provide a public URL, repository, or release status for the SysML model, scripts, wrappers, or data.</data>
      <data key="d9">Absence-based: structured field quality_checklist.reproducibility_toolchain_reported is Insufficiently; the only reusable-package statement is an overall plan to develop a CubeSat model development kit.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[10]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-11", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::no_baseline_or_comparator" id="e0003825">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_baseline_or_comparator</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper conceptually contrasts against document-centric/manual approaches, but the RAX outcome claims are not quantitatively compared to a prior mission, previous process, manual analysis result, or alternative toolchain.</data>
      <data key="d9">Absence-based: structured field claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[].baseline_comparator includes conceptual manual/document-centric comparators but no measured baseline for SNR, power, schedule, operations, or adoption outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-04", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::no_independent_validation" id="e0003826">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_independent_validation</data>
      <data key="d8">No independent replication, external evaluator, stakeholder study, or third-party validation of model outputs is reported.</data>
      <data key="d9">Absence-based: the reported evidence is the authors' single RAX/MBSE Challenge demonstration; future work calls for comparing model results to real RAX operational data.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-05", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::no_physical_test_or_flight_evidence" id="e0003827">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_physical_test_or_flight_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">RAX flight context is described, but the paper does not report that model predictions were validated by hardware tests, flat-sat, environmental tests, or actual flight/operations data.</data>
      <data key="d9">Finally, comparing results from our simulation environment based on our modeling framework to real data from operational missions such as RAX will provide a means to verify, validate, and improve the models.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[5]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-06", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::no_quantitative_evaluation" id="e0003828">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_quantitative_evaluation</data>
      <data key="d8">Although technical SNR/power/data values are calculated, the paper does not quantitatively evaluate MBSE benefits such as effort, schedule, defect reduction, ROI, model reuse, or integration failures.</data>
      <data key="d9">Absence-based: claimed-outcome records contain technical metrics such as SNR and p_dl, but no quantitative process-benefit metric or measured MBSE value indicator beyond single-scenario calculations.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-03", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::no_unified_scheduling_verification_environment_yet" id="e0003829">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no-unified-scheduling-verification-environment-yet</data>
      <data key="d8">Operational schedule robustness is a major motivation, but the authors explicitly state that efficient unified verification of optimal scheduling algorithms is not yet available.</data>
      <data key="d9">The ability to verify optimal scheduling algorithms in the simulation environment would be extremely useful, as there is currently no unified environment where this can be done efficiently.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-17", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::post_launch_case_limits_evidence_for_pre_physical_development_verification" id="e0003830">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">post-launch-case-limits-evidence-for-pre-physical-development-verification</data>
      <data key="d8">The RAX point design was already launched and operating when the paper was written; pre-implementation verification is argued and illustrated, but not shown as historically used before RAX physical development.</data>
      <data key="d9">RAX-1 was launched in October of 2010 and RAX-2 was launched in November of 2011. At the time of writing (January 2013) RAX-2 is performing experiments and being operated on a daily basis.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-15", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::prototype_or_future_work" id="e0003831">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">prototype_or_future_work</data>
      <data key="d8">Several important capabilities are explicitly future work or prototype-stage, including ParaMagic execution of wrapped STK models, unified simulations, constraint-based dynamic solving, optimal schedule verification, combined power/communication optimization, and validation against real data.</data>
      <data key="d9">Wrapping STK models as parametric constraints and executing them using ParaMagic. This capability is in a prototype stage right now. ... The various simulations in this paper currently execute individually. ... comparing results ... to real data ... will provide a means to verify, validate, and improve the models.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-01", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::single_case_or_limited_scope" id="e0003832">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">single_case_or_limited_scope</data>
      <data key="d8">The demonstration uses RAX as a point design and includes simplified scenarios such as a single-ground-station SNR example and a logical-operations focus rather than complete physical spacecraft modeling.</data>
      <data key="d9">RAX satellite being the point design. ... In this example, we assume there is a single ground station. ... The focus of this paper is on the operations of the RAX system, thus we focus on the logical models.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-02", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="limitationflag::tool_dependency_or_vendor_lockin" id="e0003833">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">tool_dependency_or_vendor_lockin</data>
      <data key="d8">The toolchain is COTS-heavy and the authors explicitly identify license requirements and vendor support as challenges.</data>
      <data key="d9">Appropriate licenses are required for all simulation tools which can be challenging, and required vendor support.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[2].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[7]", "source_record_id": "paper-0003::limitation-08", "study_id": "paper-0003"}</data>
    </edge>
