    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::bibliographic_metadata_author_discrepancy" id="e0003835">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">bibliographic-metadata-author-discrepancy</data>
      <data key="d8">Prompt corpus metadata authors differ from the author names visible in the markdown header; extraction uses prompt metadata for citation while documenting the discrepancy.</data>
      <data key="d9">Prompt metadata authors: D. Kaslow, B. Ayres, Michael J. Chonoles, S. Gasster, L. Hart, Chris Massa, Rose Yntema, B. Shiotani.; Markdown header authors visible include David Kaslow, Louise Anderson, Curtis Iwata, Bungo Shiotani, Sharan Asundi, Bradley Ayres, Robert Thompson.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-17", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::incomplete_lifecycle_coverage" id="e0003836">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">incomplete_lifecycle_coverage</data>
      <data key="d8">Although all lifecycle stages are intended, the authors say the work so far covers nomenclature, stakeholders/MOEs, and logical subsystem architecture, with lifecycle definition and concept/development models still next steps.</data>
      <data key="d9">"The effort to date has been focused on establishing nomenclature; incorporating the stakeholders and their needs, objectives, and measures of effectiveness; and defining the architecture down to the logical subsystems."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[11]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-12", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::interim_architecture_not_validated_reference_release" id="e0003837">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">interim-architecture-not-validated-reference-release</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper presents interim architecture/nomenclature and future roll-out/validation rather than a completed, independently evaluated reference model.</data>
      <data key="d9">"Work has begun on the development and distribution..."; "The model will be validated..."; "will be rolled-out in a controlled fashion..."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-15", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::interoperability_limitations" id="e0003838">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">interoperability_limitations</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper claims interfaces between SysML and COTS modeling/simulation tools but does not provide the interoperability mechanism, data flow, or synchronization details.</data>
      <data key="d9">The paper states "it is possible to interface SysML with special purpose M&amp;S tools" and Figure 6 shows "Interface with COTS Modeling and Simulation Tools," but no API/plugin/import-export/co-simulation mechanism is reported.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[8]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-09", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::learning_curve_or_training_burden" id="e0003839">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">learning_curve_or_training_burden</data>
      <data key="d8">The authors explicitly note that a fully formed model may overwhelm teams new to MBSE/SysML and propose lifecycle phase models to ease adoption.</data>
      <data key="d9">"Providing a fully-formed CubeSat Reference Model and CubeSat Project Model could be a bit overwhelming for a mission specific CubeSat team, especially a team that is just becoming familiar with MBSE and SysML."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[9]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-10", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::lineage_or_duplicate_reference_model_overlap" id="e0003840">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">lineage_or_duplicate_reference_model_overlap</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper is part of a recurring SSWG CubeSat reference-model lineage spanning prior IEEE Aerospace papers; synthesis must avoid double-counting RAX/model evidence across lineage papers.</data>
      <data key="d9">Abstract summarizes first, second, and third SSWG CubeSat project phases and Section 2 references prior RAX and enterprise-model papers [6]-[9].</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[13]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-14", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::model_not_available" id="e0003841">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">model_not_available</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper describes future controlled roll-out rather than providing a public model package, repository, or downloadable assets.</data>
      <data key="d9">"The CubeSat Reference Model will be rolled-out in a controlled fashion... The first roll-out will be to an MBSE workshop." Absence-based: no model URL/package/repository is provided.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[10]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-11", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::no_baseline_or_comparator" id="e0003842">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_baseline_or_comparator</data>
      <data key="d8">No outcome claim is evaluated against document-centric practice, a previous mission, manual analysis, or an alternative toolchain.</data>
      <data key="d9">Absence-based from completed extraction: baseline_comparator is not_reported for the structured outcome summary and all claim records; the Phase 2 shortcoming is historical context rather than a quantified comparator.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-04", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::no_eps_specific_evidence" id="e0003843">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_eps_specific_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">Power elements and power/energy trade studies are mentioned, but no EPS-specific outcome evaluation or EPS-specific MBSE verification evidence is reported.</data>
      <data key="d9">Power evidence is limited to "Solar energy collection and subsystem power consumption..." and "solar panels, batteries, regulators, and wiring harnesses"; no EPS outcome metrics or EPS verification artifacts are reported.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[6]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-07", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::no_independent_validation" id="e0003844">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_independent_validation</data>
      <data key="d8">Validation is described as future work and dependent on a planned hypothetical mission application and workshop feedback.</data>
      <data key="d9">"The model will be validated by applying it to a hypothetical CirrusSat mission..."; "The first roll-out will be to an MBSE workshop. The model will then be updated based on the feedback..."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-05", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::no_physical_test_or_flight_evidence" id="e0003845">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_physical_test_or_flight_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">Although RAX is an operational CubeSat lineage, the paper states the RAX model was not intended as an accurate satellite model and does not provide physical integration/test, operational, or flight evidence for MBSE benefits.</data>
      <data key="d9">"It was not intended to be an accurate model of the RAX satellite." Absence-based: no integration/test/operational/flight evidence appears in the claim-evidence records.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[5]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-06", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::no_pre_physical_verification_model" id="e0003846">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_pre_physical_verification_model</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper does not identify any pre-hardware EPS verification procedure integrated into the model; V&amp;V is stated at system/reference-model level only.</data>
      <data key="d9">Absence-based from completed extraction: eps_verification_specific.pre_physical_development_verification_mechanism is not_reported and verification_validation_artifacts is uncertain for controlled V&amp;V artifacts.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[7]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-08", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::no_quantitative_evaluation" id="e0003847">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_quantitative_evaluation</data>
      <data key="d8">The completed extraction found trade-study examples, but no quantitative evaluation of MBSE outcomes such as saved time, reduced defects, reuse rate, integration failures, or cost/schedule effects.</data>
      <data key="d9">Absence-based from completed extraction: claimed outcome records have evidence types assertion/conceptual/single-case/trade-study but no quantitative MBSE outcome metric or effect size.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-03", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::prototype_or_future_work" id="e0003848">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">prototype_or_future_work</data>
      <data key="d8">The reference/project model is explicitly interim and not yet validated or fully defined across lifecycle stages.</data>
      <data key="d9">"The next step is to determine the level of model definition at each of the lifecycle stages and to create models for the concept and development phases."; "The model will be validated by applying it to a hypothetical CirrusSat mission..."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-01", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0004" target="limitationflag::single_case_or_limited_scope" id="e0003849">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">single_case_or_limited_scope</data>
      <data key="d8">Prior applied evidence is mainly the RAX CubeSat lineage, and the current validation is planned on a hypothetical CirrusSat mission rather than multiple completed projects.</data>
      <data key="d9">"The first phase consisted of developing a SysML reference model of a CubeSat and applying it to the Radio Aurora Explorer (RAX)."; "The model will be validated by applying it to a hypothetical CirrusSat mission..."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[3].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0004::limitation-02", "study_id": "paper-0004"}</data>
    </edge>
