    <edge source="paper-0005" target="paper-0005::claim-01" id="e0001987">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The CubeSat Reference Model logical elements can be reused as a starting point for mission-specific CubeSat logical and physical architectures and development.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Abstract: "The logical elements can be reused as a starting point for a mission-specific CubeSat logical architecture, followed by the physical architecture and the CubeSat development."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0005::claim-01", "source_claim_id": "C1_reference_model_reuse", "source_path": "studies[4].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0005::claim-01", "study_id": "paper-0005"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="paper-0005::claim-02" id="e0001988">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Putting requirements and design in the SysML model, with trace/refine/derive relationships, supports traceability and consistency across mission, segment, and subsystem levels.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Abstract: "Requirements and design are contained in the model rather than in a series of independent engineering artifacts." Section 4: "Space and ground subsystem requirements are derived from segment requirements and trace to segment use cases."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0005::claim-02", "source_claim_id": "C2_requirements_design_in_model_traceability", "source_path": "studies[4].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0005::claim-02", "study_id": "paper-0005"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="paper-0005::claim-03" id="e0001989">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">CRM and mission-specific model viewpoints can provide objective evidence for validation and verification of the CRM, mission-specific model, and CubeSat.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Section 6: "Figure 10 illustrates that viewpoints into the CRM will provide the objective evidence needed for validation. The CRM will be populated with a representative mission, and then the viewpoints will provide the objective evidence for verification."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0005::claim-03", "source_claim_id": "C3_viewpoints_vv_objective_evidence", "source_path": "studies[4].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0005::claim-03", "study_id": "paper-0005"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="paper-0005::claim-04" id="e0001990">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The CubeSat SysML model and modeling tool can be configured to execute mission scenarios and interface with COTS modeling tools for mission modeling/V&amp;V.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Section 6: "The CubeSat SysML model and the modeling tool can be configured to execute a mission scenario. This includes interfacing with commercial off-the-shelf (COTS) modeling tools [2]."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0005::claim-04", "source_claim_id": "C4_executable_mission_scenario_tool_integration", "source_path": "studies[4].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0005::claim-04", "study_id": "paper-0005"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="paper-0005::claim-05" id="e0001991">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">MBSE and a properly designed CRM promise reduced systems-engineering task burden for small CubeSat teams.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Conclusion: "MBSE holds the promise of reducing the burden of systems engineering tasks, which is beneficial to small CubeSat teams".</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0005::claim-05", "source_claim_id": "C5_reduced_systems_engineering_burden", "source_path": "studies[4].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0005::claim-05", "study_id": "paper-0005"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="paper-0005::claim-06" id="e0001992">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">A properly designed reference model can serve as a checklist and promote uniformity and consistency across future CubeSat models.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Conclusion: "a properly designed reference model can serve as a checklist to these teams and promote uniformity and consistency across future CubeSat models."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
