    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="limitationflag::cots_simulation_interface_evidence_is_inherited_cited_rather_than_reported_in_th" id="e0003853">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">cots-simulation-interface-evidence-is-inherited-cited-rather-than-reported-in-th</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper references prior work for COTS interfaces and trade studies, so current-paper evidence for executable simulation/tool integration is weak.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 1: "Previously, the SSWG demonstrated the ability to model behaviors, interface with commercial off-the-shelf (COTS) simulation tools, and carry out trade studies [2]."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": null, "source_path": "studies[4].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0005::limitation-16", "study_id": "paper-0005"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="limitationflag::external_regulatory_specification_model_links_are_partly_future_planned" id="e0003854">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">external-regulatory-specification-model-links-are-partly-future-planned</data>
      <data key="d8">NASA Spectrum Guidance and Cal Poly specification SysML model linking/productization are described as future or ongoing, limiting current reproducibility and compliance evidence.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 8: "They will be incorporating their Spectrum Guidance... into a SysML model" and "We will work with Cal Poly to make CubeSat Spec SysML model a Cal Poly product."</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": null, "source_path": "studies[4].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0005::limitation-17", "study_id": "paper-0005"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="limitationflag::incomplete_lifecycle_coverage" id="e0003855">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">incomplete_lifecycle_coverage</data>
      <data key="d8">Although the intended scope spans design, development, V&amp;V and operation, the current CRM is still being populated with needs, technical measures, requirements, and use cases.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 8: "The model elements for stakeholder needs, objectives, and technical measure are being added as well as for mission, segment, and subsystem use cases and requirements."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[4].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[12]", "source_record_id": "paper-0005::limitation-13", "study_id": "paper-0005"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="limitationflag::interoperability_limitations" id="e0003856">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">interoperability_limitations</data>
      <data key="d8">External SysML model links and COTS interfaces are described, but mechanisms such as APIs, exchange formats, plugins, synchronization rules, or co-simulation architecture are not reported.</data>
      <data key="d9">Completed extraction: interoperability_mechanisms status=not_reported despite statements about COTS interfaces and future external model linking.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[4].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[9]", "source_record_id": "paper-0005::limitation-10", "study_id": "paper-0005"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="limitationflag::learning_curve_or_training_burden" id="e0003857">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">learning_curve_or_training_burden</data>
      <data key="d8">The intended users need intermediate space/MBSE/SysML knowledge and SME guidance, implying a learning/training burden for novice CubeSat teams.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 2 states the intermediate-level understanding and SME-support assumption for team members.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[4].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[10]", "source_record_id": "paper-0005::limitation-11", "study_id": "paper-0005"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="limitationflag::lineage_or_duplicate_reference_model_overlap" id="e0003858">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">lineage_or_duplicate_reference_model_overlap</data>
      <data key="d8">This is an interim-status paper in a recurring INCOSE SSWG CubeSat Reference Model publication lineage, with potential overlap with prior and companion papers.</data>
      <data key="d9">Title: "Interim status #3"; references [3]-[6] are prior CRM interim/status papers and reference [7] is a related 2017 behavior-definition paper.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[4].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[14]", "source_record_id": "paper-0005::limitation-15", "study_id": "paper-0005"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="limitationflag::model_not_available" id="e0003859">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">model_not_available</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper does not provide a repository, model file, open package, or downloadable CRM; OMG specification adoption and external-model productization are future work.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 8: "A next step is... initiating the OMG process for adopting a CubeSat Reference Model as an OMG specification"; no model availability URL or file is reported.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[4].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[11]", "source_record_id": "paper-0005::limitation-12", "study_id": "paper-0005"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="limitationflag::no_baseline_or_comparator" id="e0003860">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_baseline_or_comparator</data>
      <data key="d8">Although a traditional pre-MBSE requirements-document approach is mentioned narratively, no evaluated baseline or counterfactual is used for the outcome claims.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 6 mentions: "A traditional pre-MBSE approach would be to negotiate a CRM requirements document..."; no measured comparison follows.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[4].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0005::limitation-04", "study_id": "paper-0005"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0005" target="limitationflag::no_eps_specific_evidence" id="e0003861">
