    <edge source="paper-0005" target="reusemechanism::high_level_abstraction" id="e0005545">
      <data key="d5">HAS_REUSE_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d6">mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">high-level abstraction</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper explicitly presents a reusable CubeSat Reference Model that serves as a starting point/foundation for mission-specific CubeSat logical and physical architectures. High-level abstraction is supported by the logical architecture and abstract logical components. Mission-agnostic architecture is supported because the CRM is not for one mission but for later mission-specific instantiation. Do not include low-dynamics / non-detailed-behavior model or interface-focused model: behavior and interfaces are mentioned, but the paper does not claim reuse is enabled by deliberately low behavioral detail or by an interface-focused modeling strategy.</data>
      <data key="d9">The CubeSat Reference Model provides the logical architecture. The logical elements can be reused as a starting point for a mission-specific CubeSat logical architecture, followed by the physical architecture and the CubeSat development.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["high"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[4].extraction.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism", "studies[4].structured_code_summary.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0005::code-0047", "paper-0005::code-0147"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0005", "value_index": 5}</data>
