    <edge source="paper-0008" target="paper-0008::claim-01" id="e0002000">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Integrating enterprise/cost concerns into the CubeSat SysML framework is intended to provide an up-to-date mission cost estimate and enable cost/performance/schedule/risk trades from conceptual design through the lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Abstract: 'A cost model in the form of parametric, cost estimating relationships (CERs) is described here and is planned to be integrated with the system model architecture to provide an "up to the minute" total project cost estimate, with emphasis on assessment at the conceptual design phase.' Section 3: 'it is critical to have cost estimation capabilities throughout the mission lifecycle allowing trades to be conducted between cost, system performance, schedule and risk.'</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0008::claim-01", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::claim-01", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="paper-0008::claim-02" id="e0002001">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The CubeSat architecture framework provides traceability from mission objectives and mission requirements to system components, interfaces, tasks, and operating modes.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Section 2: 'A CubeSat architecture framework ... can provide a traceability map for translating the mission objectives and mission requirements into basic building blocks of CubeSat system components, interfaces and tasks.' Section 2: 'The system requirements when flowed through this block get broken down into components, interfaces, and tasks as basic building blocks.'</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0008::claim-02", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::claim-02", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="paper-0008::claim-03" id="e0002002">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">An integrated SysML, analysis, and simulation toolchain enabled end-to-end mission-scenario simulation, trade studies, and requirements verification involving power/data interdependencies and battery/solar-panel parameters.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Section 4: 'This was executed by the Cameo Simulation Toolkit ... which enabled end-to-end simulation of realistic mission scenarios. This enabled requirements verification for mission scenarios and the ability to perform trades on parameters such as orbit latitude, ground network size and distribution, and solar panel and battery sizes.' Section 6: 'The integrated model enabled the execution of trade studies to evaluate mission performance and verify that mission requirements would be satisfied.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0008::claim-03", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::claim-03", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="paper-0008::claim-04" id="e0002003">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The CubeSat SysML framework/model and manual provide a reusable starting point and learning resource for other CubeSat teams.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Abstract: 'The framework developed is a SysML representation of common CubeSat elements that can be used as a library to build a domain-specific CubeSat.' Model Availability: 'Our RAX CubeSat model and its manual are being made available to the academic community' and intent includes 'A starting point for a CubeSat team to develop their own model.'</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0008::claim-04", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::claim-04", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="paper-0008::claim-05" id="e0002004">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">SLIM links SysML blocks to PLM parts/BOMs, enabling generation/synchronization of part structures and continuity from systems architecture to mechanical/electrical design.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Section 5: 'SLIM enables systems engineers to develop a high-level system model in SysML and connect it to domain-specific models, such as Bills of Materials (BOMs) and Computer Aided Design (CAD)... managed in various enterprise product lifecycle management systems.' Section 5 Use Case 1: 'the block structure is used to generate a part structure in a PLM system Windchill ... Connections are saved between the corresponding parts and blocks so that changes on either side can be synchronized as desired.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0008::claim-05", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::claim-05", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="paper-0008::claim-06" id="e0002005">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">A payload part structure from a previous mission can be reused from PLM to generate a SysML block structure for a new CubeSat design, replacing placeholders and supporting mass/cost calculations.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Section 5 Use Case 2: 'The payload for the mission may be reused from a previous mission enterprise that exists in a PLM system ... Generate a SysML block structure from the payload model in Windchill and use it in the context of a new CubeSat design.' Section 5: 'This may be a preliminary design, perhaps submitted for purposes of mass and/or cost calculation.'</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0008::claim-06", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::claim-06", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="paper-0008::claim-07" id="e0002006">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">MBSE/SysML and a top-down framework improve team communication and integration of components, interfaces, processes, and tasks into early CONOPS and design choices.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Introduction: 'MBSE and the use of standard languages such as Systems Modeling Language (SysML) and Unified Modeling Language (UML) allow for stronger more integrated communication between engineering teams.' Conclusion: 'an engineering team can more effectively communicate and integrate the system such as the component, interfaces, processes and tasks.'</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0008::claim-07", "source_claim_id": "C7", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[6]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::claim-07", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="paper-0008::claim-08" id="e0002007">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The modeling framework should lead to more robust and reusable CubeSat designs and address reliability/stakeholder concerns by combining top-down architecture with bottom-up component/interface/task overhead estimation.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Abstract/Section 6: 'a modeling framework that allows for analyzing and costing the technical design of the spacecraft throughout the lifecycle of the mission will allow for more robust and reusable designs.' Introduction/third phase: 'a bottom-up development process to address the reliability of CubeSats and stakeholder concerns.'</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0008::claim-08", "source_claim_id": "C8", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[7]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::claim-08", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="paper-0008::claim-09" id="e0002008">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The work is claimed to be the first known integration of a space-system SysML model with analytical models, simulation engines, and a special-purpose high-fidelity space-system model.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Section 6: 'To the best of our knowledge this is the first known integration of a space system SysML model with a set of analytical models, simulation engines, and special purpose high fidelity space system model.'</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0008::claim-09", "source_claim_id": "C9", "source_path": "studies[6].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[8]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::claim-09", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="developmentcontext::academic_student" id="e0002245">
      <data key="d5">HAS_DEVELOPMENT_CONTEXT</data>
