    <edge source="paper-0008" target="ivvintegrationlevel::simulation_in_the_loop" id="e0003757">
      <data key="d5">HAS_IVV_LEVEL</data>
      <data key="d6">eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level</data>
      <data key="d7">simulation-in-the-loop</data>
      <data key="d8">The highest supported IVV integration level is simulation-in-the-loop: SysML is connected with analytical/simulation tools and executed for mission-scenario requirements verification, including battery capacity/margin and solar-panel/battery trades. The paper does not support SIL/HIL, physical integration/test, or model-contained EPS test procedures.</data>
      <data key="d9">This was executed by the Cameo Simulation Toolkit ... which enabled end-to-end simulation of realistic mission scenarios. This enabled requirements verification for mission scenarios</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["high"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[6].extraction.eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level", "studies[6].structured_code_summary.eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0008::code-0095", "paper-0008::code-0260"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0008", "value_index": 1}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::assumptions_or_data_quality_limits" id="e0003885">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">assumptions_or_data_quality_limits</data>
      <data key="d8">CubeSat cost modeling depends on difficult-to-measure labor, dynamic requirements, lack of standards, small-mass cost databases, and proprietary/unknown launch cost data.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 3: 'generally no accurate labor cost can be tracked'; 'system requirements and architecture are often undefined and dynamic'; 'Lack of standards during development, Integration &amp; Test, and operation makes it difficult to apply detailed parametric cost models'; 'There is an inherent inability to utilize traditional massbased cost databases'. Section Launch Cost: 'The detailed nature of these costs is proprietary and not disclosed'.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[7]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-08", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::cost_model_integration_not_completed_in_this_paper" id="e0003886">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">cost-model-integration-not-completed-in-this-paper</data>
      <data key="d8">The abstract says CER cost modeling is planned to integrate with the system model, while Section 3 describes the approach and rationale rather than reporting implemented results.</data>
      <data key="d9">'A cost model ... is described here and is planned to be integrated with the system model architecture...'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": null, "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-14", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::detailed_numerical_trade_study_outputs_omitted" id="e0003887">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">detailed-numerical-trade-study-outputs-omitted</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper identifies parameters varied in energy/data trade studies but does not include the resulting plots/tables or requirement margins.</data>
      <data key="d9">'Energy state trade studies varied the solar panel area and battery capacity. Data collection trade studies varied the orbital altitude and ground station network.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": null, "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-16", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::incomplete_lifecycle_coverage" id="e0003888">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">incomplete_lifecycle_coverage</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper aspires to full lifecycle coverage but provides strongest detail for conceptual/early design, simulation trades, and PLM handoff; physical I&amp;T and operations evidence are not reported.</data>
      <data key="d9">Lifecycle continuity is asserted ('throughout the lifecycle'), but integration/test readiness and operational validation fields are not reported in the completed extraction.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[10]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-11", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::interoperability_limitations" id="e0003889">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">interoperability_limitations</data>
      <data key="d8">Cross-repository comparison/synchronization is described as maturing/future rather than complete.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 5: 'Capabilities to compare and synchronize the structures ... using SLIM are maturing now and will be demonstrated in the next iteration of this work.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[9]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-10", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::lineage_or_duplicate_reference_model_overlap" id="e0003890">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">lineage_or_duplicate_reference_model_overlap</data>
      <data key="d8">This paper builds directly on prior INCOSE SSWG/RAX CubeSat MBSE Challenge papers and reuses the same framework/model lineage, creating potential overlap with other corpus papers.</data>
      <data key="d9">References [4], [5], and [6] are prior CubeSat/RAX MBSE papers; Section 4 states 'The initial CubeSat framework developed in [4] has been extended...' and the first/second phases cite [4] and [5].</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[12]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-13", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::model_access_conditions_unclear" id="e0003891">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">model-access-conditions-unclear</data>
      <data key="d8">The model/manual are said to be available or being made available to the academic/CubeSat community, but no URL, license, or access procedure is given in the paper.</data>
      <data key="d9">'Our RAX CubeSat model and its manual are being made available to the academic community.'</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": null, "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-15", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::no_baseline_or_comparator" id="e0003892">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_baseline_or_comparator</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper does not compare MBSE outcomes against a document-centric, manual, alternative-toolchain, or previous-mission baseline.</data>
      <data key="d9">structured_code_summary['claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[].baseline_comparator'] is status=not_reported; previous-mission payload reuse is a source for a structure, not an evaluated comparator.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-04", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::no_eps_specific_evidence" id="e0003893">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_eps_specific_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">EPS/power is modeled within a system-level framework, but the paper does not present a dedicated EPS model evaluation or EPS-specific reliability/reproducibility outcome.</data>
      <data key="d9">The paper reports 'power collection, power management' and trades on 'solar panel area and battery capacity', but claimed outcomes are framed for the CubeSat system/framework rather than an EPS-specific verification model.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[6]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-07", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::no_independent_validation" id="e0003894">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_independent_validation</data>
      <data key="d8">No independent stakeholder/user/expert evaluation or external validation of the framework's claimed benefits is reported.</data>
      <data key="d9">The model is being released to solicit suggestions, but the extraction found no reported feedback results: Model Availability includes 'A mechanism for soliciting suggestions for improvements to the model'.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-05", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::no_physical_test_or_flight_evidence" id="e0003895">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_physical_test_or_flight_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">Although RAX is a real CubeSat mission, the paper does not connect the MBSE/enterprise model to hardware test, environmental test, integration-test, operational, or flight outcome evidence.</data>
      <data key="d9">eps_verification_specific.integration_test_readiness is status=not_reported; reported evidence is simulation/trade-study and PLM use-case based.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[5]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-06", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::no_quantitative_evaluation" id="e0003896">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_quantitative_evaluation</data>
      <data key="d8">No numeric outcome metrics are reported for MBSE value claims such as speed, cost savings, reuse, reliability, defect reduction, or integration success.</data>
      <data key="d9">Claim extraction found qualitative statements such as 'enabled the execution of trade studies' and 'will allow for more robust and reusable designs', but no effect sizes, before/after metrics, or measured ROI.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-03", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::prototype_or_future_work" id="e0003897">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">prototype_or_future_work</data>
      <data key="d8">Several capabilities are explicitly planned or maturing rather than fully demonstrated in this paper, including cost-model integration, ground-system SysML transformation, and SLIM synchronization.</data>
      <data key="d9">Abstract: cost model 'is planned to be integrated with the system model architecture'. Section 5: 'Capabilities to compare and synchronize the structures ... are maturing now and will be demonstrated in the next iteration of this work.' Section 2: 'Current work is focused transforming the functional flow diagram ... into the SysML model'.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-01", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::single_case_or_limited_scope" id="e0003898">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">single_case_or_limited_scope</data>
      <data key="d8">The applied evidence centers on the RAX CubeSat/framework lineage and illustrative SLIM use cases; generalization beyond this context is asserted but not independently demonstrated.</data>
      <data key="d9">The paper states the first phase applied the SysML framework 'to model RAX' and Section 5 says 'we exercised the following use cases with SLIM'; no multi-project outcome evaluation is reported in the completed extraction.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-02", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::tool_dependency_or_vendor_lockin" id="e0003899">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">tool_dependency_or_vendor_lockin</data>
      <data key="d8">The reported executable/reproducible workflow depends on multiple named COTS/proprietary tools, which may limit independent reuse even though the authors also express interest in a proprietary-free/open framework.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 6: 'The COTS modeling and simulation tools included MagicDraw and Cameo Simulation Tool Kit ... ModelCenter ... STK ... and MATLAB.' Section 5 uses Windchill/Teamcenter through SLIM.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[8]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-09", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0008" target="limitationflag::weak_claim_evidence_linkage" id="e0003900">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">weak_claim_evidence_linkage</data>
      <data key="d8">Some broader claims such as robust/reliable designs, improved communication, ROI, and quicker analysis are not supported by quantified or independently validated evidence.</data>
      <data key="d9">Claim records C7 and C8 have evidence_confidence_rating Unsupported; quality_checklist.evidence_for_outcomes is scored Insufficiently.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[6].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[11]", "source_record_id": "paper-0008::limitation-12", "study_id": "paper-0008"}</data>
    </edge>
