    <edge source="paper-0011" target="ivvintegrationlevel::model_contained_verification_artifacts" id="e0003759">
      <data key="d5">HAS_IVV_LEVEL</data>
      <data key="d6">eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level</data>
      <data key="d7">model-contained verification artifacts</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper shows system-level, not EPS-specific, V&amp;V artifacts contained in the CSRM model through Validation/Verification packages, activity elements, tables, element properties, diagrams, and Word-document artifacts. Trace links from verification activities to requirements are also shown. There is no evidence of executable checks, simulation-in-the-loop, SIL/HIL, or physical integration/test as the IVV integration level.</data>
      <data key="d9">The CSRM provides for defining these elements; and for tracing requirements from stakeholders, behaviors, and technical measures down to subsystems and components and then to validation and verification activities.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["high"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[8].extraction.eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level", "studies[8].structured_code_summary.eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0011::code-0063", "paper-0011::code-0176"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0011", "value_index": 1}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0011" target="limitationflag::incomplete_lifecycle_coverage" id="e0003917">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">incomplete_lifecycle_coverage</data>
      <data key="d8">Coverage emphasizes early logical architecture, requirements, behaviors, technical measures, and V&amp;V planning; implementation, integration/test execution, and operations are not evidenced.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 3/Architecture states logical architecture is followed by physical architecture and development; completed extraction has lifecycle_stage_addressed coded only as concept/pre-Phase A and Phase A/B.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[8].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[10]", "source_record_id": "paper-0011::limitation-11", "study_id": "paper-0011"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0011" target="limitationflag::interoperability_limitations" id="e0003918">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">interoperability_limitations</data>
      <data key="d8">The authors explicitly state that specification dissemination/control/update processes and available formats are unresolved; detailed current CSRM exchange mechanisms are not reported.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4/OMG Specification Efforts: 'Processes for dissemination and control of the CSRM once it becomes an OMG specification, maintaining updates to it, and what formats will be available have yet to be worked out.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[8].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[8]", "source_record_id": "paper-0011::limitation-09", "study_id": "paper-0011"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0011" target="limitationflag::lineage_or_duplicate_reference_model_overlap" id="e0003919">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">lineage_or_duplicate_reference_model_overlap</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper is part of a long INCOSE SSWG CubeSat/RAX MBSE reference-model lineage, so synthesis should avoid treating all cited phase outputs as independent evidence.</data>
      <data key="d9">Background/Project History: CSRM development has been underway since 2012 and prior phases included a CubeSat model applied to RAX, power/downlink behavior expansion, and integrated simulation trade studies.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[8].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[12]", "source_record_id": "paper-0011::limitation-13", "study_id": "paper-0011"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0011" target="limitationflag::methodology_agnostic_model_leaves_tailoring_burden_to_teams" id="e0003920">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">methodology-agnostic-model-leaves-tailoring-burden-to-teams</data>
      <data key="d8">Flexibility is a strength, but the paper also states teams determine which elements/relationships to use and may modify the containment tree, which can limit uniform adoption without additional guidance.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 3: 'The CSRM provides a library of model elements but does not dictate what model elements and relationships to use. This is determined by the development team.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[8].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0011::limitation-15", "study_id": "paper-0011"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0011" target="limitationflag::model_based_specification_governance_unresolved" id="e0003921">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">model-based-specification-governance-unresolved</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper proposes a model-based OMG specification precedent but states dissemination, control, update, and format details are not yet decided.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4/OMG Specification Efforts: 'what formats will be available have yet to be worked out.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[8].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0011::limitation-16", "study_id": "paper-0011"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0011" target="limitationflag::model_not_available" id="e0003922">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">model_not_available</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper reports submission to OMG and university use, but provides no downloadable model, repository, license, or specification format for reproduction.</data>
      <data key="d9">Completed extraction: reproducibility_toolchain_reported=Insufficiently; the paper states future formats have not been worked out and does not include a model URL or repository.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[8].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[9]", "source_record_id": "paper-0011::limitation-10", "study_id": "paper-0011"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0011" target="limitationflag::no_baseline_or_comparator" id="e0003923">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_baseline_or_comparator</data>
      <data key="d8">Except for the document-based OMG specification context, outcome claims have no controlled comparison against previous document-centric processes, prior missions, or alternative toolchains.</data>
      <data key="d9">The paper states 'In the past, OMG specifications have all been documentbased' but does not compare CSRM outcomes quantitatively or empirically against that or any mission-development baseline.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[8].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0011::limitation-04", "study_id": "paper-0011"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0011" target="limitationflag::no_eps_specific_evidence" id="e0003924">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_eps_specific_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">EPS/power evidence is limited to a generic Power Subsystem block and brief historical power trade-study mentions; no EPS requirements, behavior model, verification procedure, or result is presented for the CSRM.</data>
      <data key="d9">Figure 11 lists 'Power Subsystem'; Background mentions 'power usage behaviors' and solar/battery trade studies, but no current EPS model artifacts or EPS V&amp;V results are shown.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[8].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[6]", "source_record_id": "paper-0011::limitation-07", "study_id": "paper-0011"}</data>
