    <edge source="paper-0012" target="ivvintegrationlevel::executable_model_based_checks" id="e0003760">
      <data key="d5">HAS_IVV_LEVEL</data>
      <data key="d6">eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level</data>
      <data key="d7">executable/model-based checks</data>
      <data key="d8">The highest supported IVV integration level is executable/model-based feasibility or constraint checking inside the mission-design model. This should not be upgraded to trace-linked verification artifacts, simulation-in-the-loop, SIL/HIL, or formal EPS V&amp;V. The evidence is model-executed parametric checks for feasibility, power sizing, and constraints before physical development.</data>
      <data key="d9">The process begins with the input of power requirements... Total power demand... Battery capacity required... Solar panel area required... Design is feasible... Select min. cost feasible design.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["medium"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[9].extraction.eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level", "studies[9].structured_code_summary.eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0012::code-0058", "paper-0012::code-0151"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0012", "value_index": 1}</data>
    </edge>
