    <edge source="paper-0012" target="reusemechanism::high_level_abstraction" id="e0005577">
      <data key="d5">HAS_REUSE_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d6">mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">high-level abstraction</data>
      <data key="d8">The reusable contribution is a baseline CubeSat mission-design architecture/workflow and guidance, not a fully mission-agnostic or interface-focused model. The paper explicitly says the architecture cannot be completely generalized but can be maintained as a baseline with modified inputs/requirements. Its generality also depends on high-level analytical abstractions and deliberate avoidance of detailed/numerical dynamic behavior. The current 'specific-mission model with reusable method only' is overstated because the paper demonstrates two generic use cases rather than one specific mission model.</data>
      <data key="d9">Since each space mission is unique, the model architecture introduced here cannot be completely generalized, however a baseline structure can be maintained with modifications of the inputs and requirements made for each use case.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["high"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[9].extraction.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism", "studies[9].structured_code_summary.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0012::code-0036", "paper-0012::code-0128"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0012", "value_index": 4}</data>
    </edge>
