    <edge source="paper-0014" target="ivvintegrationlevel::trace_linked_verification_artifacts" id="e0003762">
      <data key="d5">HAS_IVV_LEVEL</data>
      <data key="d6">eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level</data>
      <data key="d7">trace-linked verification artifacts</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper supports trace-linked V&amp;V artifacts at the generic CSRM/system-reference-model level through requirement and technical-measure links to validation/verification activities. It does not show EPS-specific verification, executable/model-based checks, simulation-in-the-loop, SIL/HIL, or physical integration/test evidence. Do not upgrade beyond trace-linked verification artifacts.</data>
      <data key="d9">The CSRM provides for defining and tracing requirements from stakeholders, to behaviors, with technical measures assigned to subsystems and components to be certified through validation and verification activities.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["medium"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[11].extraction.eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level", "studies[11].structured_code_summary.eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0014::code-0059", "paper-0014::code-0153"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0014", "value_index": 1}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::incomplete_lifecycle_coverage" id="e0003961">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">incomplete_lifecycle_coverage</data>
      <data key="d8">Mission Engineering support, including V&amp;V, is not yet evaluated and implementation evaluations are planned for future stages.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4, line 222: '...the current CSRM provides support for verification and validation activities. The level to which that supports Mission Engineering activities would have to be evaluated.' Section 6, lines 276-280: Stage 1 is outreach in 2021, Stage 2 reports methodologies/evaluation strategies and down-selects, and Stage 3 carries out implementation evaluations; 'Updating the OMG CSRM specification and files requires OMG and INCOSE approval.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[8]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-09", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::interoperability_limitations" id="e0003962">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">interoperability_limitations</data>
      <data key="d8">The authors state that descriptive SysML products do not enable detailed performance analysis, require external mission models, and that Mission Engineering/SoS extensions need further research and tool/process improvements.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4, line 216: 'While these products enable a complete description of a mission from multiple perspectives, they do not enable detailed analysis of the performance of that mission...Proper analysis requires definition and analysis of external mission models.' Section 4, line 218: '...extending it beyond that point to incorporate a dynamic, analytical capability to assess overall mission performance would be challenging and an area that would require much further research.' Section 4, line 220: '...incorporating MBSE into SoSE practice is shown to be a necessary, albeit challenging, step... it will require improvements and extensions of MBSE concepts, processes and tools...'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[7]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-08", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::lineage_or_duplicate_reference_model_overlap" id="e0003963">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">lineage_or_duplicate_reference_model_overlap</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper belongs to a recurring CSRM lineage from 2014-2020 and cites prior behavior, V&amp;V, technical-measure, and development/application CSRM papers.</data>
      <data key="d9">Introduction, line 91: 'The International Council on Systems Engineering (INCOSE) Space Systems Working Group (SSWG) has been focused on the design and development of the CubeSat System Reference Model (CSRM) since 2014. [1] - [6] That effort was successfully completed in 2020.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[10]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-11", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::mission_specific_population_burden" id="e0003964">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">mission-specific-population-burden</data>
      <data key="d8">The CSRM is deliberately not pre-populated with mission-specific stakeholders, technical measures, behaviors, or requirements; teams must supply these elements.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 2, line 115: 'The CSRM is a repository for systems engineering artifacts. However, it is not pre-populated with specific stakeholders, technical measures, behaviors, and requirements. That is the job of the CubeSat mission development team, specific to their needs and objectives.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-13", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::mission_utility_metrics_not_yet_defined" id="e0003965">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">mission-utility-metrics-not-yet-defined</data>
      <data key="d8">The authors identify creation of metrics for alternatives and mission utility as future work needed to model the mission in its entirety.</data>
      <data key="d9">Summary, line 301: 'While the CSRM has tremendous utility in the development of a system, more work needs to be done in properly modelling the mission in its entirety (e.g., creation of metrics that allow for the evaluation of alternatives, mission utility, etc.).'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-15", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::no_baseline_or_comparator" id="e0003966">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_baseline_or_comparator</data>
      <data key="d8">No claim is compared against a document-centric process, manual analysis, alternative toolchain, or previous mission.</data>
      <data key="d9">Completed extraction: structured_code_summary['claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[].baseline_comparator'] is not_reported; all claim records list baseline_comparator='not reported'.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-04", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::no_eps_specific_evidence" id="e0003967">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_eps_specific_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">Power and energy are mentioned as mission trade factors, but no EPS architecture, EPS requirements, EPS components, or EPS verification procedure is modeled in detail.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4, lines 226-228: '...the transformation from Logical Architecture to Physical Design in the model starts at the enterprise level and expands down into the space segment, ground segments, subsystems, and subsystem components. Drivers... include ... how much power is available to support these operations.' Section 4, line 230: 'The trade studies are based on the modeling of collecting mission observations, storage, downlink, energy collection, and energy consumption. Such factors are used early in the mission process by stakeholders and mission engineers to define and negotiate a trade space.' Completed extraction: eps_relevance is EPS-adjacent, not EPS-specific.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[6]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-07", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::no_independent_validation" id="e0003968">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_independent_validation</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper states professional vetting and favorable community introduction, but provides no independent validation protocol, evaluator details, results, or replication evidence.</data>
      <data key="d9">Abstract, line 61: 'The CSRM has been vetted by System Engineering professionals and has been introduced to the CubeSat mission development team community with favorable results.' Completed extraction: evidence type is weak/undetailed stakeholder-user-expert evaluation, not independent validation.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-05", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::no_physical_test_or_flight_evidence" id="e0003969">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_physical_test_or_flight_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper describes reference-model and V&amp;V support only; no flat-sat, hardware/software integration, environmental test, operational, or flight results are reported.</data>
      <data key="d9">Completed extraction: eps_verification_specific.integration_test_readiness is not_reported and claimed outcomes use conceptual/assertion evidence rather than physical/flight evidence.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[5]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-06", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::no_quantitative_evaluation" id="e0003970">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_quantitative_evaluation</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper does not report quantitative outcome metrics for MBSE adoption; it states that mission-utility/evaluation metrics still need to be created.</data>
      <data key="d9">Summary, line 301: 'While the CSRM has tremendous utility in the development of a system, more work needs to be done in properly modelling the mission in its entirety (e.g., creation of metrics that allow for the evaluation of alternatives, mission utility, etc.).' Completed extraction: claim records contain no numerical effect size, cost/schedule/effort/defect metric, or requirements/test coverage metric.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-03", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::prototype_or_future_work" id="e0003971">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">prototype_or_future_work</data>
      <data key="d8">The Mission Engineering extension is explicitly an early-stage study with proposed future methodology selection and implementation evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d9">Summary, line 301: 'The SSWG is in the early stages of a study that will explore the feasibility of extending the CSRM into the realm of Mission Engineering.' Section 6, lines 276-280: Stage 1 is outreach in 2021, Stage 2 reports methodologies/evaluation strategies and down-selects, and Stage 3 carries out implementation evaluations; 'Updating the OMG CSRM specification and files requires OMG and INCOSE approval.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-01", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::single_case_or_limited_scope" id="e0003972">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">single_case_or_limited_scope</data>
      <data key="d8">The completed asset is one CSRM reference model focused on CubeSat space/ground logical architecture; extension to full mission and SoS is only preliminarily assessed.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 2, line 109: 'The CSRM provides a CubeSat logical space-ground architecture. The logical components are abstractions of the physical components that perform the system functionality without imposing implementation constraints.' Section 4, line 224: 'The above analysis is just a very preliminary assessment... feasible to extend the CSRM to capture a descriptive model of the mission. Addressing areas such as interoperability analysis and capturing the implementation of a mission-oriented SoS will require much further research...'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-02", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::sys_ml_capability_modeling_gap" id="e0003973">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">sys-ml-capability-modeling-gap</data>
      <data key="d8">Mission capability analysis requires a capability concept not native to SysML, so the CSRM would need stereotype/profile extension.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4, line 202: 'There is no model element defined in SysML for a capability. However, SysML can be extended through the use of stereotypes. The CSRM had created unique stereotypes for other model elements.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-12", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::unnamed_modeling_tool_and_exchange_format" id="e0003974">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">unnamed-modeling-tool-and-exchange-format</data>
      <data key="d8">Reproducibility/toolchain synthesis is limited because the paper names SysML and a generic graphical modeling tool but not the tool, model version, exchange format, API, or repository URL.</data>
      <data key="d9">Abstract, line 61: 'The CSRM is based on Model-Based System Engineering (MBSE) principles, is System Modeling Language (SysML) compliant, is hosted in a graphical modeling tool, and is intended to foster completeness and economies of scale associated with reusability.' Section 2, line 117: 'A mission-specific CubeSat team downloads the CSRM specification and files from OMG for import it into their own graphical modeling tool. The mission team identifies the systems engineering methodology to be followed and populates the model, elements, relationships, and diagrams as needed.'</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-14", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0014" target="limitationflag::weak_claim_evidence_linkage" id="e0003975">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">weak_claim_evidence_linkage</data>
      <data key="d8">Although claims are linked to CSRM mechanisms, most evidence is conceptual, cited from prior work, or asserted without in-paper results.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4, line 204: 'It has been demonstrated that the CSRM can be used to define and analyze mission activities such as those involved with the tasking, collection, and distribution of mission data [1].' Section 4, line 206: '...it has been demonstrated that the CSRM can be used to perform a similar analysis utilizing technical measures and parametrics [3].' Completed extraction: strongest claim evidence types are assertion only, illustrative/conceptual argument, and undetailed stakeholder/user/expert evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[11].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[9]", "source_record_id": "paper-0014::limitation-10", "study_id": "paper-0014"}</data>
    </edge>
