    <edge source="paper-0014" target="reusemechanism::high_level_abstraction" id="e0005591">
      <data key="d5">HAS_REUSE_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d6">mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">high-level abstraction</data>
      <data key="d8">The CSRM is a reusable CubeSat reference/logical architecture intended as a starting point for mission teams, not a single mission-specific model. It is mission-agnostic because teams populate mission-specific stakeholders, requirements, behaviors, and measures. It uses high-level logical abstractions and does not impose physical implementation constraints. The paper also supports a non-detailed/descriptive behavior interpretation because the model is not pre-populated with behaviors and the authors state that dynamic/performance analysis requires external mission models and further research. Do not add interface-focused model or specific-mission model with reusable method only.</data>
      <data key="d9">The International Council on Systems Engineering (INCOSE) Space System Working Group (SSWG) has created the CubeSat System Reference Model (CSRM), a representation of the logical architecture of a CubeSat system, intended to be used by system architects and engineers as a starting point as they develop the physical architecture of the Space and Ground segments of the CubeSat mission of interest to them.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["high"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[11].extraction.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism", "studies[11].structured_code_summary.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0014::code-0041", "paper-0014::code-0133"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0014", "value_index": 6}</data>
    </edge>
