      <data key="d8">Outcome claims are not accompanied by numeric measures for effort, cost, schedule, reliability, trace coverage, test coverage, or integration outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d9">Absence-based from completed extraction: claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence records have metric_or_value_indicator empty or qualitative except trace links/model reuse; no quantitative results table or effect size appears in the paper.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[12].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0015::limitation-03", "study_id": "paper-0015"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0015" target="limitationflag::planned_standardization_not_current_approval" id="e0003987">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">planned-standardization-not-current-approval</data>
      <data key="d8">OMG specification status is an intended validation/governance route, but the paper does not report that the CRM has already been approved as a specification.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4: OMG review and approval of the CRM will validate that the CRM is qualified to be a specification.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": null, "source_path": "studies[12].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0015::limitation-15", "study_id": "paper-0015"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0015" target="limitationflag::prototype_or_future_work" id="e0003988">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">prototype_or_future_work</data>
      <data key="d8">The CRM and V&amp;V augmentation are presented as ongoing work with future advances expected.</data>
      <data key="d9">Abstract: Further research is needed into how best to augment with other models to facilitate CubeSat test and evaluation. Conclusion: This activity is expected to continue into the foreseeable future resulting in further advances in MBSE.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[12].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0015::limitation-01", "study_id": "paper-0015"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0015" target="limitationflag::single_case_or_limited_scope" id="e0003989">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">single_case_or_limited_scope</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper is limited to a high-abstraction CubeSat reference model rather than a physically instantiated mission or multiple applied cases.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 1: Even though it is at least three levels of abstraction away from any physical instantiation, it still provides valuable assistance to the Mission-specific CubeSat development teams.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[12].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0015::limitation-02", "study_id": "paper-0015"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0015" target="limitationflag::viewpoints_as_evidence_not_operationalized" id="e0003990">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">viewpoints-as-evidence-not-operationalized</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper repeatedly states that viewpoints provide objective evidence, but does not define viewpoint acceptance criteria, measures, or completed viewpoint examples with results.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4: viewpoints into the CRM will provide the objective evidence needed for validation. Absence-based: viewpoint content, pass/fail criteria, and resulting evidence are not shown.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": null, "source_path": "studies[12].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0015::limitation-16", "study_id": "paper-0015"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0015" target="limitationflag::weak_claim_evidence_linkage" id="e0003991">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">weak_claim_evidence_linkage</data>
      <data key="d8">Some outcomes are tied to MBSE artifacts, but key value claims such as productivity and no negative impacts are asserted without supporting evidence.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 1: ...providing them a standard Reference Model for their development will boost the efficiency and productivity of less experienced teams without any negative impacts. Absence-based: no productivity or negative-impact evidence is reported.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[12].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[12]", "source_record_id": "paper-0015::limitation-13", "study_id": "paper-0015"}</data>
