    <edge source="paper-0022" target="approachclass::extended_mbse" id="e0001660">
      <data key="d5">HAS_APPROACH_CLASS</data>
      <data key="d6">implementation_pathway_tailoring.approach_classification</data>
      <data key="d7">Extended MBSE</data>
      <data key="d8">The approach centers on SysML/OOSEM but explicitly connects the system model to external simulations, trade studies, requirements/V&amp;V context, reusable libraries, and multiple lifecycle stages; downstream hardware/software integration is not demonstrated, so it is not coded as Integrated MBSE/digital engineering.</data>
      <data key="d9">Abstract: 'The system model also integrates other discipline specific engineering models and simulations.'</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["medium"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[14].extraction.implementation_pathway_tailoring.approach_classification", "studies[14].structured_code_summary.implementation_pathway_tailoring.approach_classification"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0022::code-0053", "paper-0022::code-0170"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0022", "value_index": 1}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0022" target="paper-0022::claim-01" id="e0002062">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">A SysML system model provides a single source for architecture development and interface management and integrates discipline-specific models/simulations.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Abstract: 'MBSE involves creating a system model that is a single source for system engineering such as architecture development and interface management. The system model also integrates other discipline specific engineering models and simulations.' Figure 5: 'Model updates are automatically populated into the system views.'</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0022::claim-01", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_path": "studies[14].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0022::claim-01", "study_id": "paper-0022"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0022" target="paper-0022::claim-02" id="e0002063">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The CubeSat Reference Model can serve as a reusable starting point/logical architecture for mission-specific CubeSat models.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Goal: 'Provide a CubeSat Reference Model that CubeSat teams can use as starting point for their mission-specific CubeSat model.' Section III.A: 'provide a logical architecture... the building blocks for any kind of CubeSat mission.'</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0022::claim-02", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_path": "studies[14].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0022::claim-02", "study_id": "paper-0022"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0022" target="paper-0022::claim-03" id="e0002064">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Concept lifecycle trade studies can be structured by decomposing MOEs to MOPs/TPMs, identifying model elements/parameters, and interfacing the mission model with STK to quantify performance.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Section III.C: 'First, the MOEs are decomposed into measures of performances (MOPs) and technical performance measures (TPMs).' 'The interface supports the input (driving parameters) into the space system model and the output (quantifying parameters) from the space system model.'</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0022::claim-03", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_path": "studies[14].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0022::claim-03", "study_id": "paper-0022"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0022" target="paper-0022::claim-04" id="e0002065">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Power/data/communications concept trades can evaluate whether candidate subsystem models provide sufficient power to collect and downlink mission data.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Section III: 'The following two trade studies were demonstrated: 1) On board energy level as a function of solar panel area and maximum battery capacity, and 2) quantity of data downloaded...' Section III.C: 'The model is used to establish and evaluate a second-order trade space that provides sufficient power for collect and downlink mission data...'</data>
