    <edge source="paper-0023" target="limitationflag::figure_table_driven_evidence_without_accessible_model_files" id="e0004023">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">figure-table-driven-evidence-without-accessible-model-files</data>
      <data key="d8">Many details are available only as figures/tables in the article; the SysML model itself is not provided, limiting replication and detailed checking of trace links.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 5.1: "requirements tables were generated ... These tables describe the requirements and their relationship to other SysML design elements to facilitate requirements traceability, satisfaction, and verification." Completed extraction: the paper has a future-work paragraph but no formal limitations, threats-to-validity, quantitative evaluation, baseline comparison, independent validation, model repository, integration-test result, or flight/operations result was found in the markdown.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[15].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0023::limitation-13", "study_id": "paper-0023"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0023" target="limitationflag::incomplete_lifecycle_coverage" id="e0004024">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">incomplete_lifecycle_coverage</data>
      <data key="d8">The framework covers all lifecycle phases conceptually, while the demonstrated MASAT1 application is mainly mission analysis and PBS; external analysis/executable behavior remains future work.</data>
      <data key="d9">Abstract: "This paper aims to contribute to research efforts to improve the success of university nanosatellite missions using Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE) to facilitate the initial project management and design phases." Section 5: "MBSE approach can be used to create a PBS model repository that can be used by university teams designing nanosatellite projects, for requirements, design, analysis verification, and validation activities." Conclusion: "The next step of this work is to improve the viability and practicality of the product breakdown structure model by integrating external analysis and simulation tools such as MATLAB and STK. The aim is to develop an executable SysML model with a graphical user interface to provide insight into how nanosatellites work."</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[15].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[10]", "source_record_id": "paper-0023::limitation-11", "study_id": "paper-0023"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0023" target="limitationflag::interoperability_limitations" id="e0004025">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">interoperability_limitations</data>
      <data key="d8">External analysis and simulation tool integration is explicitly left to the next step, indicating current interoperability is incomplete.</data>
      <data key="d9">Conclusion: "The next step of this work is to improve the viability and practicality of the product breakdown structure model by integrating external analysis and simulation tools such as MATLAB and STK. The aim is to develop an executable SysML model with a graphical user interface to provide insight into how nanosatellites work."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[15].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[7]", "source_record_id": "paper-0023::limitation-08", "study_id": "paper-0023"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0023" target="limitationflag::model_not_available" id="e0004026">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">model_not_available</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper describes diagrams and packages but does not provide a model repository, files, reusable package, or data availability statement.</data>
      <data key="d9">Absence-based from completed extraction: reproducibility_toolchain_reported is Insufficiently; Completed extraction: the paper has a future-work paragraph but no formal limitations, threats-to-validity, quantitative evaluation, baseline comparison, independent validation, model repository, integration-test result, or flight/operations result was found in the markdown.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[15].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[9]", "source_record_id": "paper-0023::limitation-10", "study_id": "paper-0023"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0023" target="limitationflag::no_baseline_or_comparator" id="e0004027">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_baseline_or_comparator</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper contrasts MBSE with DBSE/ad hoc practices conceptually but does not measure against a document-centric or prior-mission baseline.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 1: "the early failure rate of these missions is around 40%" and "One reason for such low reliability can be the traditional project management and design procedures following the approach of Document-Based Systems Engineering (DBSE) ... usually over-specified for nanosatellite projects." Conclusion: "To improve communication, planning, management, and development, we implemented this approach, replacing ad hoc procedures in the work organization with process flow and model based on the different views of the system architecture." Absence-based: no quantitative comparator was reported.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[15].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0023::limitation-04", "study_id": "paper-0023"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0023" target="limitationflag::no_eps_specific_evidence" id="e0004028">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_eps_specific_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">Power subsystem requirements and architecture are modeled, but outcome evidence remains artifact-level and does not quantify EPS reliability, reproducibility, or integrability improvements.</data>
      <data key="d9">Fig. 18 description: Power System BDD contains Solar Panel [1..5], Battery [1..2] with DOD/capacity/voltage, Power Control Unit with Power Converter/Conditioner/Distribution, Kill Switch, RBF pin, and Power Management SW with power-point tracking, housekeeping, battery protection, and command/data interface. Absence-based: EPS-related claim C6 has only a model verification example, not EPS outcome metrics.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[15].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[6]", "source_record_id": "paper-0023::limitation-07", "study_id": "paper-0023"}</data>
    </edge>
