    <edge source="paper-0023" target="limitationflag::single_case_or_limited_scope" id="e0004034">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">single_case_or_limited_scope</data>
      <data key="d8">The approach is derived from and applied to the MASAT1 university nanosatellite and mainly details the mission-analysis/PBS phase.</data>
      <data key="d9">Abstract: "The proposed model-based approach is the result of experience gained from the MASAT1 project, a Moroccan university nanosatellite, and it is based on an architectural framework that allows the system to be described via a set of views." Section 4.1: "MASAT1 is a nanosatellite project initiated at the University of Sidi Mohamed Ben Abdellah, Fez, Morocco" to build "a resilient, ready-to-fly CubeSat system, with efficient power management and low-cost mission control ground station"; payload is "an FPGA-based reconfigurable secondary onboard computer."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[15].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0023::limitation-02", "study_id": "paper-0023"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0023" target="limitationflag::tool_dependency_or_vendor_lockin" id="e0004035">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">tool_dependency_or_vendor_lockin</data>
      <data key="d8">The implemented model uses No Magic MagicDraw/Cameo Simulation Toolkit, and no export/open model alternative is reported; this creates tool dependency for reproduction.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 2: "Implementation of MBSE is enabled by ... A SysML modeling toolset" and "We used No Magic MagicDraw modeler with SysML and Cameo Simulation toolkit plugin." Absence-based: no model repository, export mechanism, or open-source implementation is reported.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[15].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[8]", "source_record_id": "paper-0023::limitation-09", "study_id": "paper-0023"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0023" target="limitationflag::weak_claim_evidence_linkage" id="e0004036">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">weak_claim_evidence_linkage</data>
      <data key="d8">Some broad claims about reliability, quality, efficiency, and cost-effectiveness are linked to MBSE only by conceptual argument and single-case artifacts without outcome measurement.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 1: "The combination of Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE) and Systems Modeling Language (SysML) emerged as an alternative management and design approach that improves mission reliability ... Typical advantages of MBSE are that it provides better traceability, design consistency, quality improvement, and reduced document management overhead." Conclusion: the approach "synthesizes the basic concepts and processes that allow supervising teachers to carry out project management and design activities easily and efficiently." Absence-based: no measured outcome effects are reported.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[15].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[11]", "source_record_id": "paper-0023::limitation-12", "study_id": "paper-0023"}</data>
    </edge>
