      <data key="d7">no_baseline_or_comparator</data>
      <data key="d8">No quantitative baseline or comparator is used to evaluate the workflow against document-centric engineering, manual analysis, proprietary toolchains, or previous missions.</data>
      <data key="d9">Completed extraction: claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[].baseline_comparator is coded only as previous document-centric process/none/not reported; no measured comparator is reported.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[19].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0029::limitation-04", "study_id": "paper-0029"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0029" target="limitationflag::no_independent_validation" id="e0004085">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_independent_validation</data>
      <data key="d8">The validation is a self-contained proof of concept; no independent reproduction, stakeholder/user evaluation, or external expert validation is reported.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4 calls the case a "preliminary validation"; no independent validation evidence appears in the extraction.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[19].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0029::limitation-05", "study_id": "paper-0029"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0029" target="limitationflag::no_physical_test_or_flight_evidence" id="e0004086">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_physical_test_or_flight_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">The work is limited to preliminary design modeling/simulation and does not report hardware integration, testing, operations, or flight evidence.</data>
      <data key="d9">Completed extraction: eps_verification_specific.integration_test_readiness is not_reported and lifecycle stage is limited to concept/pre-Phase A and Phase A/B.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[19].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[5]", "source_record_id": "paper-0029::limitation-06", "study_id": "paper-0029"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0029" target="limitationflag::no_pre_physical_verification_model" id="e0004087">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_pre_physical_verification_model</data>
      <data key="d8">Although pre-physical analyses are generated, no formal verification procedure, matrix, acceptance criteria linkage, or executable verification checks are integrated into the EPS/system model.</data>
      <data key="d9">Completed extraction: eps_verification_specific.verification_validation_artifacts and pre_physical_development_verification_mechanism are not_reported.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[19].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[6]", "source_record_id": "paper-0029::limitation-07", "study_id": "paper-0029"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0029" target="limitationflag::no_quantitative_evaluation" id="e0004088">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_quantitative_evaluation</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper provides quantitative design/budget outputs, but no quantitative evaluation of MBSE process outcomes such as effort, cost, schedule, errors, traceability coverage, or integration failures.</data>
      <data key="d9">Completed extraction: Figure 7 gives battery/TC/TM quantities, but quality_checklist.evidence_for_outcomes and ROI fields found no quantitative process-benefit evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[19].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0029::limitation-03", "study_id": "paper-0029"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0029" target="limitationflag::nominal_operating_mode_abstraction_excludes_eop_off_nominal_behavior" id="e0004089">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">nominal-operating-mode-abstraction-excludes-eop-off-nominal-behavior</data>
      <data key="d8">The OM generalization intentionally omits detumbling, calibration, safe-mode, EOP, and other off-nominal scenarios, limiting applicability to mission assurance or fault-management analysis.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 3.1.2: early orbit/off-nominal OMs "are not considered for the current analysis"; Section 5 says EOP/off-nominal OMs were not fully incorporated.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[19].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0029::limitation-14", "study_id": "paper-0029"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0029" target="limitationflag::nss_eccentricity_approximation_in_twc_case" id="e0004090">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">nss-eccentricity-approximation-in-twc-case</data>
      <data key="d8">The TWC mission is described as using Molniya-like high elliptical orbits, but Table 9 states eccentricity was treated as null due to simulation-tool limitations, which may affect fidelity of the proof of concept.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4: TWC uses "two high elliptical Molniya-like orbits"; Table 9 note: "Because of limitations within the simulation tools used, the ECC has been considered null."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[19].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0029::limitation-13", "study_id": "paper-0029"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0029" target="limitationflag::prototype_or_future_work" id="e0004091">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">prototype_or_future_work</data>
      <data key="d8">The TWC application is framed as an illustration/proof of concept and several extensions are left to future work.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 6: "A proof of concept is presented with the SysML model of the TWC mission..."; "Future works... could address approximations by the NSS tools and limitations of the OM generalization".</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[19].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0029::limitation-01", "study_id": "paper-0029"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0029" target="limitationflag::single_case_or_limited_scope" id="e0004092">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">single_case_or_limited_scope</data>
      <data key="d8">The empirical application is one theoretical academic TWC case, and the OM generalization is scoped to common LEO CubeSat nominal operations.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section 4: TWC is "a theoretical academic concept"; Section 5: "Another limitation is the focus on low Earth orbit (LEO) missions".</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[19].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0029::limitation-02", "study_id": "paper-0029"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0029" target="limitationflag::tool_dependency_or_vendor_lockin" id="e0004093">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
