      <data key="d7">requirements-modeling-language-rml</data>
      <data key="d8">Open extraction observation not fully represented by the controlled vocabulary.</data>
      <data key="d9">Section III, Requirements Modeling Language: Requirements Modeling Language (RML) is a collection of diagrams used to model software from the business analysis or product management perspective [12]. RML is concerned with a project's goals and objectives, instead of complex system design models (which is the focus of UML and SySML) [13].</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"category": null, "description": "Visual requirements modeling language used from a business-analysis/product-management perspective rather than a SysML system architecture method.", "original_label": "Requirements Modeling Language (RML)", "source_path": "studies[22].emergent_codes[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0034::emergent-01", "study_id": "paper-0034"}</data>
    </edge>
