    <edge source="paper-0034" target="ivvintegrationlevel::trace_linked_verification_artifacts" id="e0003772">
      <data key="d5">HAS_IVV_LEVEL</data>
      <data key="d6">eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level</data>
      <data key="d7">trace-linked verification artifacts</data>
      <data key="d8">The RMM explicitly maps and traces requirements to code and test cases, so the best-supported level is trace-linked verification artifacts. It should not be upgraded to executable/model-based checks, simulation-in-the-loop, or SIL/HIL; no EPS-specific IVV model is reported.</data>
      <data key="d9">It works as a high-level documentation, which maps and traces user requirements with the corresponding test cases.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["high"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[22].extraction.eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level", "studies[22].structured_code_summary.eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0034::code-0049", "paper-0034::code-0128"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0034", "value_index": 1}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0034" target="limitationflag::automated_testing_not_operationalized" id="e0004125">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">automated-testing-not-operationalized</data>
      <data key="d8">Despite the title's automated-testing framing, the paper reports only a generic possibility of automated missing-link checking and illustrative test-case tables, not an implemented automated test execution pipeline.</data>
      <data key="d9">A Requirements Mapping Matrix (RMM) is best used by a requirement management model tool which can automate the process of checking for missing links [12].</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": null, "source_path": "studies[22].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0034::limitation-12", "study_id": "paper-0034"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0034" target="limitationflag::incomplete_lifecycle_coverage" id="e0004126">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">incomplete_lifecycle_coverage</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper focuses on requirements mapping and software test cases; no lifecycle gates, operations, downstream hardware integration, or full project lifecycle execution is demonstrated.</data>
      <data key="d9">In this paper, the importance of implementing RML into a project lifecycle of an engineering system (such as a CubeSat system) is described. A case study of using requirements mapping matrix (RMM) for requirements validation and verification of a typical CubeSat system is provided.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[22].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[9]", "source_record_id": "paper-0034::limitation-10", "study_id": "paper-0034"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0034" target="limitationflag::model_not_available" id="e0004127">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">model_not_available</data>
      <data key="d8">No model file, RMM spreadsheet, tool configuration, repository, scripts, or downloadable package is reported.</data>
      <data key="d9">Completed extraction found descriptive figures/tables only; availability or reproducibility assets are not reported.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[22].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[8]", "source_record_id": "paper-0034::limitation-09", "study_id": "paper-0034"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0034" target="limitationflag::no_baseline_or_comparator" id="e0004128">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_baseline_or_comparator</data>
      <data key="d8">Although RML is conceptually contrasted with UML/SysML, the paper does not compare outcomes against a previous document-centric process, manual testing, another toolchain, or prior mission.</data>
      <data key="d9">Requirements Modeling Language (RML) is a collection of diagrams used to model software from the business analysis or product management perspective [12]. RML is concerned with a project's goals and objectives, instead of complex system design models (which is the focus of UML and SySML) [13].</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[22].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0034::limitation-04", "study_id": "paper-0034"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0034" target="limitationflag::no_eps_specific_evidence" id="e0004129">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_eps_specific_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">EPS is only mentioned as a subsystem connected through the OBC; no EPS requirements, architecture, power budgets, components, or EPS verification evidence are modeled.</data>
      <data key="d9">OBC is the central component of the CubeSat system. It is connecting all subsystem components, so it can control subsystems by allowing subsystems to connect with the communication &amp; Data handling with the Electrical Power System (EPS).</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[22].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[6]", "source_record_id": "paper-0034::limitation-07", "study_id": "paper-0034"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0034" target="limitationflag::no_independent_validation" id="e0004130">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_independent_validation</data>
      <data key="d8">No stakeholder, user, expert, external, or independent validation is reported; actual-project testing is planned as future work.</data>
      <data key="d9">Future work will include verifying and characterizing the efficacy of the proposed approach, testing it in an actual project and updating it based on this experience.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
