    <edge source="paper-0034" target="reusemechanism::high_level_abstraction" id="e0005666">
      <data key="d5">HAS_REUSE_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d6">mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">high-level abstraction</data>
      <data key="d8">RML/RMM is presented as a reusable requirements-modeling method and matrix structure, and RMM is explicitly described as high-level documentation. However, the actual CubeSat artifact is an NDSAT/example radio-camera-OBC case, not a reusable mission-agnostic architecture. Do not retain low-dynamics / non-detailed-behavior model because the paper does not frame low behavioral detail itself as the reuse mechanism.</data>
      <data key="d9">RMM contains multiple levels of mapping that map process flow steps to requirements, requirements to business rules, business objectives to features, features to requirements, requirements to code, and requirements to test cases, as illustrated in Fig. 1.</data>
