    <edge source="paper-0039" target="paper-0039::claim-01" id="e0002125">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">A CSRM-derived standardized MBSE template can make CubeSat design cycles more efficient and reduce future design/development time by preventing repeated trade studies on well-understood subsystems/components.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The aim of this model is to aid in the education of undergraduate engineering students in their capstone design course as well as to reduce design and development times for future CubeSat systems.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0039::claim-01", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_path": "studies[24].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0039::claim-01", "study_id": "paper-0039"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0039" target="paper-0039::claim-02" id="e0002126">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The baseline model defines PSAT1U subsystems/components/interfaces while leaving payload and mission modules undefined, helping users understand the payload design space and create mission-specific instances.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The baseline model is unique in that it defines all of the important subsystems, components, and interfaces of the PSAT1U, but leaves the payload and mission specific modules undefined.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0039::claim-02", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_path": "studies[24].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0039::claim-02", "study_id": "paper-0039"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0039" target="paper-0039::claim-03" id="e0002127">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Model relationships automatically propagate a Watchdog Timer specification change from ADCS to the Power subsystem and other related elements, avoiding manual propagation and improving consistency/traceability.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">As a result, any changes made to the Watchdog Timer specification are automatically propagated to the Power subsystem and to any other subsystems or components with a relationship to the Watchdog Timer. The user does not need to manually propagate this change.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0039::claim-03", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_path": "studies[24].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0039::claim-03", "study_id": "paper-0039"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0039" target="paper-0039::claim-04" id="e0002128">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Storing critical PSAT1U design information inside model documentation tabs makes it viewable/editable by practitioners and supports shared understanding.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The model stores design specifics of the PSAT1U as text data within the documentation tab of the appropriate subsystem or component specification. In this way, critical design information is stored in the model and can be viewed or edited as needed by practitioners.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0039::claim-04", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_path": "studies[24].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0039::claim-04", "study_id": "paper-0039"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0039" target="paper-0039::claim-05" id="e0002129">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The faculty-prepared template lets students and discipline experts benefit from MBSE tools without becoming MBSE experts, allowing them to focus on analysis, testing, and mission-critical decisions.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">This approach... will also allow subject matter experts in aerospace engineering and other specific disciplines to gain the benefit of these powerful systems engineering tools without becoming expert MBSE users.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0039::claim-05", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_path": "studies[24].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0039::claim-05", "study_id": "paper-0039"}</data>
    </edge>
