    <edge source="paper-0039" target="reusemechanism::high_level_abstraction" id="e0005675">
      <data key="d5">HAS_REUSE_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d6">mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">high-level abstraction</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper supports reuse through a CSRM-derived CubeSat template/reference model, existing diagram templates and component library, and a repeatable process for tailoring the model with mission-specific requirements and payload details. The PSAT1U baseline itself is reusable because mission and payload modules are deliberately left undefined within a design envelope, and interfaces/components are central to the model. Do not code 'specific-mission model with reusable method only' because the model itself is claimed as a reusable template. Do not code 'low-dynamics / non-detailed-behavior model' because the paper does not directly frame limited behavior/dynamics modeling as the reuse mechanism.</data>
      <data key="d9">the CubeSat System Reference Model (CSRM) ... was chosen as a CubeSat specific template providing the "logical elements [which] can be reused as a starting point for a mission-specific CubeSat logical architecture."</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["high"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[24].extraction.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism", "studies[24].structured_code_summary.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0039::code-0039", "paper-0039::code-0135"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0039", "value_index": 6}</data>
