    <edge source="paper-0043" target="paper-0043::claim-01" id="e0002136">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">MOSAiC connects ARCADIA-based MBSE models with open-source multi-domain simulations to improve traceability, reusability, and lifecycle fidelity.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">This paper presents the first version of the unified Modeling and Simulation (M&amp;S) framework MOSAiC ... which connects MBSE with open source, multi-domain simulation environments, with the goal of improving traceability, reusability, and fidelity in the system lifecycle.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0043::claim-01", "source_claim_id": "C1_traceable_reusable_simulation_framework", "source_path": "studies[26].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0043::claim-01", "study_id": "paper-0043"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0043" target="paper-0043::claim-02" id="e0002137">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Model-to-simulation extraction improves consistency between system models, operational modes, and simulation artifacts.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The extracted dataset includes subsystem-level parameters such as mass, volume, and power consumption—both static and mode-dependent—as well as functional and component exchanges, OMs definitions, and their associated transition conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0043::claim-02", "source_claim_id": "C2_consistency_model_simulation_artifacts", "source_path": "studies[26].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0043::claim-02", "study_id": "paper-0043"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0043" target="paper-0043::claim-03" id="e0002138">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Simulation integrated with the MBSE model enables early validation of design choices, trade-off exploration, and data-driven architectural refinement.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Overall, this early feedback loop enabled more informed and data-driven design decisions, provided justification for architectural refinements, and strengthened the confidence in the system's capacity to meet mission-level constraints, while moving onto the Physical Architecture layer.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0043::claim-03", "source_claim_id": "C3_early_validation_tradeoffs", "source_path": "studies[26].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0043::claim-03", "study_id": "paper-0043"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0043" target="paper-0043::claim-04" id="e0002139">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The EPS/power simulation can verify battery capacity and power balance across operational modes and eclipse/contact periods before hardware implementation.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">during eclipse periods, the simulation would verify whether battery capacity was sufficient to sustain system operation until sunlight was available for recharging.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0043::claim-04", "source_claim_id": "C4_eps_power_feasibility", "source_path": "studies[26].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0043::claim-04", "study_id": "paper-0043"}</data>
    </edge>
