    <edge source="paper-0043" target="reusemechanism::high_level_abstraction" id="e0005688">
      <data key="d5">HAS_REUSE_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d6">mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">high-level abstraction</data>
      <data key="d8">MOSAiC is presented as a reusable framework/workflow rather than only the FIRE-EYE mission model. The paper explicitly claims applicability beyond a specific space application, uses layered abstraction from stakeholder needs to components, emphasizes interfaces/data exchanges between MBSE and simulations, and makes models/code publicly available. Do not code low-dynamics / non-detailed-behavior model because dynamic, time-dependent simulations are central; do not code specific-mission model with reusable method only because the framework itself is claimed adaptable beyond the case.</data>
      <data key="d9">This paper presents the first version of the unified Modeling and Simulation (M&amp;S) framework MOSAiC ... which connects MBSE with open source, multi-domain simulation environments, with the goal of improving traceability, reusability, and fidelity in the system lifecycle.</data>
