    <edge source="paper-0046" target="limitationflag::sapph_ire_terminology_confusion" id="e0004211">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">sapph-ire-terminology-confusion</data>
      <data key="d8">Users had difficulty with element names such as Organ and Physical Phenomena, suggesting semantic usability limits not fully captured by general learning-curve coding.</data>
      <data key="d9">The Organ in particular could be renamed to better reflect its purpose, such as 'Physical Parameters'. The 'Physical Phenomena' also created initial confusion</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": null, "source_path": "studies[27].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0046::limitation-15", "study_id": "paper-0046"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0046" target="limitationflag::single_case_or_limited_scope" id="e0004212">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">single_case_or_limited_scope</data>
      <data key="d8">The model and tool are based on one UPEI SpudNik-1 CubeSat case and tested with 15 UPEI engineering students.</data>
      <data key="d9">All work for this survey took place at the University of Prince Edward Island (UPEI) using the CubeSat 'SpudNik-1' as a case study.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[27].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0046::limitation-02", "study_id": "paper-0046"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0046" target="limitationflag::student_task_environment_may_not_reflect_industrial_collaborative_use" id="e0004213">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">student-task-environment-may-not-reflect-industrial-collaborative-use</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper acknowledges student-team context and notes that industry settings may require different explicit behavior documentation.</data>
      <data key="d9">This is one of the limitations with conducting a survey using engineering students. In an industry setting, where the database may need to be accessed and understood by external personnel, the Physical Phenomena may prove to be more relevant.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
