    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0053" target="paper-0053::claim-01" id="e0002149">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The concurrent-engineering toolchain produces an adaptable and interoperable model in which mission or satellite-configuration changes can be studied quickly/easily.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The main added value of this process is that it allows to define an adaptable and interoperable model. For instance, any change on the mission can be studied almost instantly by regenerating the corresponding ephemeris data.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0053::claim-01", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_path": "studies[28].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0053::claim-01", "study_id": "paper-0053"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0053" target="paper-0053::claim-02" id="e0002150">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The simulation workflow enables EPS sizing and stable energy-budget assessment under worst-case mission and environmental conditions.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">One last thing to mention is that the minimum SOC (State Of Charge) reached during the simulation is 85%</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0053::claim-02", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_path": "studies[28].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0053::claim-02", "study_id": "paper-0053"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0053" target="paper-0053::claim-03" id="e0002151">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The workflow enables trade studies of observation plans, technologies, regulator types, bus voltages, solar-cell placement, thermal sensitivity, and battery configurations.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">This step is also an opportunity to carry out various trade-offs between technologies and architecture principles (type of battery/solar cell, power bus topologies, control principles, etc.).</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0053::claim-03", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_path": "studies[28].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0053::claim-03", "study_id": "paper-0053"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0053" target="paper-0053::claim-04" id="e0002152">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Standardized files and interoperable tools enable subsystem experts to exchange data, communicate through engineering models, and keep dedicated specialized tools compatible.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">It allows everyone to use their own dedicated and specialized tools by still ensuring compatibility with inputs/outputs of other tools, leading to a smooth workflow.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0053::claim-04", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_path": "studies[28].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0053::claim-04", "study_id": "paper-0053"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0053" target="paper-0053::claim-05" id="e0002153">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The preliminary-phase workflow could be extended to phases A/B/C/D by adding the satellite manufacturer/provider if file standards are respected.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">it could also be implemented for phases A/B/C/D by adding a satellite manufacturer/provider in the loop as long as the files standard is still respected</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0053::claim-05", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_path": "studies[28].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0053::claim-05", "study_id": "paper-0053"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0053" target="developmentcontext::academic_student" id="e0002305">
      <data key="d5">HAS_DEVELOPMENT_CONTEXT</data>
      <data key="d6">study_context_population.development_context</data>
      <data key="d7">academic/student</data>
      <data key="d8">The use case involves LESIA laboratory and CNES agency in a concurrent engineering process for a 16U nanosatellite with volume/power constraints; the paper explicitly describes mission agility and concurrent design.</data>
      <data key="d9">This mission concept has been carried out by the French laboratory LESIA (Laboratory for Space Studiers and Astrophysics Instrumentation) with the help of CNES which is in charge of evaluating its feasibility.</data>
