      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">exchange-standard-details-underspecified</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper emphasizes standardized and CCSDS-like files but does not specify schemas, semantic mappings, or version/configuration control needed for independent reproduction.</data>
      <data key="d9">CCSDS-like standard files generated by Simu-CIC</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": null, "source_path": "studies[28].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0053::limitation-13", "study_id": "paper-0053"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0053" target="limitationflag::formal_requirements_and_v_v_traceability_not_shown" id="e0004216">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">formal-requirements-and-v-v-traceability-not-shown</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper validates energy feasibility through simulation but does not show formal requirements objects, verification matrices, or test-case traceability.</data>
      <data key="d9">In that case, a satisfactory equilibrium for the aforementioned power subsystem would thus be defined as a battery cycling between 75% and a bit less than 100% of state of charge, meaning that the energy production is sufficient to power the satellite as well as charging the battery during low illumination time windows, while still ensuring a sufficient margin in the eventuality of a satellite malfunction.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": null, "source_path": "studies[28].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0053::limitation-12", "study_id": "paper-0053"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0053" target="limitationflag::incomplete_lifecycle_coverage" id="e0004217">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">incomplete_lifecycle_coverage</data>
      <data key="d8">The demonstrated scope is preliminary phases; later A/B/C/D coverage is only proposed as possible.</data>
      <data key="d9">The presented use case describes the process for preliminary phases</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
