    <edge source="paper-0059" target="reusemechanism::method_guidance" id="e0005709">
      <data key="d5">HAS_REUSE_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d6">mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">method guidance</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper presents RFLP-in-PLM as a transferable workflow/method and demonstrates it on one CubeSat electrical-power viewpoint. It discusses abstraction and interfaces, but does not provide or demonstrate a reusable mission-agnostic architecture, template, library, open package, or interface-focused reusable model asset.</data>
      <data key="d9">The RFLP approach consists of four methodological stages, represented by its acronym: requirement specification, functional, logical, and physical. These stages are followed sequentially</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["medium"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[30].extraction.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism", "studies[30].structured_code_summary.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0059::code-0041", "paper-0059::code-0148"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0059", "value_index": 2}</data>
