    <edge source="paper-0061" target="paper-0061::claim-01" id="e0002166">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The CE-MBSE/concurrent model-based approach shortens the BOSS feasibility analysis relative to the traditional methodology.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Using the CE-MBSE methodology, the feasibility study was completed in one month, compared to the three months required when using the traditional approach.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0061::claim-01", "source_claim_id": "C1_schedule_reduction", "source_path": "studies[31].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0061::claim-01", "study_id": "paper-0061"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0061" target="paper-0061::claim-02" id="e0002167">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The CE-MBSE approach reduces the estimated mission cost for the BOSS feasibility study compared with a traditional methodology.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The CE-MBSE approach projected a total mission cost of 15 million euros, which is significantly lower than the 22 million euros estimated through the traditional approach.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0061::claim-02", "source_claim_id": "C2_cost_reduction", "source_path": "studies[31].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0061::claim-02", "study_id": "paper-0061"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0061" target="paper-0061::claim-03" id="e0002168">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The CE-MBSE workflow produced different/lower mass and other feasibility figures of merit, interpreted as evidence of integrated iterative design effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The CE-MBSE methodology resulted in a spacecraft mass of 22.59 kg, which is approximately 15% lower than the 26.6 kg calculated using the traditional methodology.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0061::claim-03", "source_claim_id": "C3_design_performance_figures_of_merit", "source_path": "studies[31].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0061::claim-03", "study_id": "paper-0061"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0061" target="paper-0061::claim-04" id="e0002169">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The Central Data Exchange System improves cross-discipline consistency, validation, and error reduction by sharing up-to-date data and checking common inputs.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">It allows automated data transfer from the other spreadsheets of the S3D Tool and enables faster validation of the sizing, budgets and design, reducing manual effort and minimizing errors.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0061::claim-04", "source_claim_id": "C4_consistency_error_reduction", "source_path": "studies[31].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0061::claim-04", "study_id": "paper-0061"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0061" target="paper-0061::claim-05" id="e0002170">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Concurrent sessions and shared tools improve collaboration, communication, and cross-disciplinary alignment.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">the team continuously communicates, discusses, and takes decisions by consensus</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0061::claim-05", "source_claim_id": "C5_communication_alignment", "source_path": "studies[31].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0061::claim-05", "study_id": "paper-0061"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0061" target="paper-0061::claim-06" id="e0002171">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">CUTE-DB supports component selection and decision making by linking available CubeSat technology specifications and performance data to preliminary design.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The CUTE-DB provides immediate access to specifications and performance data of commercially available components, supporting not only the component selection during the design process but also ensuring that CubeSat projects are based on current technological realities.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0061::claim-06", "source_claim_id": "C6_component_selection_decision_support", "source_path": "studies[31].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "source_record_id": "paper-0061::claim-06", "study_id": "paper-0061"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0061" target="paper-0061::claim-07" id="e0002172">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The Concurrent Model-Based approach and tools are reusable across multiple CubeSat/small-satellite mission case studies.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">the Concurrent Model-Based approach and the related tools (both S3D Tool and CUTE-DB) have been implemented and tested in several case studies, including the Bennu Observer Small Satellites (BOSS) mission, the Geo-Profundo mission [13], and the Cislunar mission [15].</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0061::claim-07", "source_claim_id": "C7_reuse_across_case_studies", "source_path": "studies[31].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[6]", "source_record_id": "paper-0061::claim-07", "study_id": "paper-0061"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0061" target="paper-0061::claim-08" id="e0002173">
