    <edge source="paper-0063" target="reusemechanism::interface_focused_model" id="e0005717">
      <data key="d5">HAS_REUSE_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d6">mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">interface-focused model</data>
      <data key="d8">The EIRSAT-1 model is specific to one mission and the demonstrated exemplar is the communications subsystem, not a mission-agnostic architecture. Reuse is supported at the workflow/method level: OOSEM/SysML/CATIA Magic are used to construct verification models from test plans, interface them with scripts/hardware, and reuse/apply a similar approach in comparable verification scenarios and remaining subsystems. The interface-focused label is supported by the model-to-script/test-setup exchange and ground-segment interface modeling. Do not add high-level abstraction, mission-agnostic architecture, or low-dynamics / non-detailed-behavior model.</data>
      <data key="d9">As a starting point, we have adopted INCOSE OOSEM.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["high"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[32].extraction.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism", "studies[32].structured_code_summary.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0063::code-0038", "paper-0063::code-0141"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0063", "value_index": 3}</data>
    </edge>
