    <edge source="paper-0068" target="paper-0068::claim-01" id="e0002180">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">DSM/DMM can represent CubeSat subsystems, interfaces, objects, processes, and states in one concise representation.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">A practical utility of Figure 5 is the ability to represent the CubeSat subsystems and their interfaces including objects/processes/states in one DSM/DMM representation.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0068::claim-01", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_path": "studies[33].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0068::claim-01", "study_id": "paper-0068"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0068" target="paper-0068::claim-02" id="e0002181">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The approach facilitates a digital information flow or digital thread from MBSE conceptual design to PLM/detailed design.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Based on the data that is encoded in DSM/DMM in Figure 5 we could trace the flow of data that was created during the conceptual design phase to the next phase of the design process.</data>
