      <data key="d7">risk-metric-validity-not-evaluated</data>
      <data key="d8">RPI thresholds and color categories are specified, but the paper does not validate that the thresholds improve prioritization quality or risk outcomes for student teams.</data>
      <data key="d9">Risk Precedence Index [RPI]: Risk Precedence Index for this proposal is defined as the product of the severity index number and the likelihood index number.; Risk Precedence Index [RPI]: A risk with an RPI of 15 or higher is classified as high-level risk, a risk with RPI greater than 5 and lesser than 15 is classified as mid-level risk and risks with RPI lower than or equal to 5 are classified as low-level risks.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
