    <edge source="paper-0077" target="paper-0077::claim-01" id="e0002191">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Using CSRM as the basis for a mission-specific CubeSat model enables reuse of logical components and sharing/reuse across design activities.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The CSRM logical components are intended to be reused as a starting point for a mission-specific CubeSat logical architecture followed by the development of physical architecture during CubeSat development.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0077::claim-01", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_path": "studies[35].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0077::claim-01", "study_id": "paper-0077"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0077" target="paper-0077::claim-02" id="e0002192">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The MSM can serve as the single central design baseline throughout development and operations, replacing dispersed document-centric artifacts.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The MSM is maintained throughout all phases of development and operations as the single and central design baseline.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0077::claim-02", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_path": "studies[35].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0077::claim-02", "study_id": "paper-0077"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0077" target="paper-0077::claim-03" id="e0002193">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Explicit relationships among stakeholders, concerns, requirements, use cases, and technical measures support traceability, completeness, and stakeholder alignment.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The CSRM has model elements for stakeholders, concerns, mission needs, mission objectives, mission constraints and mission requirements. These model elements and their relationships are mission and engineering methodology specific.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0077::claim-03", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_path": "studies[35].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0077::claim-03", "study_id": "paper-0077"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0077" target="paper-0077::claim-04" id="e0002194">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Verification and validation activities linked to requirements, technical measures, mission objectives, and stakeholders support mission assurance and requirements satisfaction evidence.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The verify relationship is a relationship between a requirement and a test case or other model element that is used to verify the requirement is satisfied.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0077::claim-04", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_path": "studies[35].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0077::claim-04", "study_id": "paper-0077"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0077" target="paper-0077::claim-05" id="e0002195">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Web-published CSRM, XMI files, and exportable tables improve model access, interoperability, and reviewability for mission teams and external reviewers.</data>
