    <edge source="paper-0077" target="ivvintegrationlevel::model_contained_verification_artifacts" id="e0003784">
      <data key="d5">HAS_IVV_LEVEL</data>
      <data key="d6">eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level</data>
      <data key="d7">model-contained verification artifacts</data>
      <data key="d8">The highest supported IVV level is model-contained verification artifacts at generic MSM/system level: Verification/Validation Activity elements, properties, diagrams, tables, and hyperlinks are represented in or linked from the model and are trace-linked to requirements/technical measures. This is not EPS-specific and not executable, simulation-in-the-loop, or SIL/HIL.</data>
      <data key="d9">The Verification Activity element describes the process for verifying an element, e.g. a requirement. For example, the process could include verification plans, procedures, execution, results, and status. The process can be captured in a 1) Verification Activity element properties, or 2) Verification Activity Diagram, or 3) Verification Activity Word document.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["high"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[35].extraction.eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level", "studies[35].structured_code_summary.eps_verification_specific.ivv_integration_level"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0077::code-0062", "paper-0077::code-0164"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0077", "value_index": 1}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0077" target="limitationflag::incomplete_lifecycle_coverage" id="e0004313">
