    <edge source="paper-0077" target="limitationflag::no_baseline_or_comparator" id="e0004316">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_baseline_or_comparator</data>
      <data key="d8">Except for a generic contrast with document-centric artifacts, outcome claims do not report measured comparison against prior missions, manual analysis, alternative tools, or a baseline process.</data>
      <data key="d9">In MBSE, requirements and design are captured in the model rather than the traditional document centric series of independent engineering artifacts.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[35].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0077::limitation-04", "study_id": "paper-0077"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0077" target="limitationflag::no_eps_specific_evidence" id="e0004317">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_eps_specific_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">Power subsystem, solar array, battery, and power properties are only examples within a broader CubeSat system reference model; no EPS-specific MBSE outcomes, verification results, or power-subsystem model evidence are reported.</data>
      <data key="d9">For example: processor, memory, antenna solar array, battery, and GPS receiver.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[35].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[6]", "source_record_id": "paper-0077::limitation-07", "study_id": "paper-0077"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0077" target="limitationflag::no_independent_validation" id="e0004318">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_independent_validation</data>
      <data key="d8">The authors state that initial validation-requirement satisfaction is based on the CSRM development team's judgment, and that mission-team evaluation is the preferred next step rather than reported evidence.</data>
      <data key="d9">Initially satisfaction of these validation requirements is based on the judgment of the CSRM development team. However, the satisfaction of these validation requirements is best evaluated by several Mission-specific CubeSat teams</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[35].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0077::limitation-05", "study_id": "paper-0077"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0077" target="limitationflag::no_physical_test_or_flight_evidence" id="e0004319">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_physical_test_or_flight_evidence</data>
      <data key="d8">The extraction found conceptual V&amp;V activity modeling but no hardware integration, flat-sat, environmental-test, operational, or flight results.</data>
      <data key="d9">Figures 17 and 18 are illustrations of the types of relationships that can be established between Validation Activities, Verification Activities, Stakeholders, Technical Measures, and Requirements.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[35].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[5]", "source_record_id": "paper-0077::limitation-06", "study_id": "paper-0077"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0077" target="limitationflag::no_quantitative_evaluation" id="e0004320">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">no_quantitative_evaluation</data>
      <data key="d8">Completed extraction found no quantitative outcome metrics for time, effort, defects, integration failures, test coverage, cost, schedule, reliability, or reuse. The validation evidence described is judgment-based and prospective.</data>
      <data key="d9">Initially satisfaction of these validation requirements is based on the judgment of the CSRM development team.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "extractor_identified", "source_path": "studies[35].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0077::limitation-03", "study_id": "paper-0077"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0077" target="limitationflag::power_weight_cost_parametrics_deliberately_omitted" id="e0004321">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">power-weight-cost-parametrics-deliberately-omitted</data>
      <data key="d8">The model does not yet include power/weight/cost parametrics, limiting evidence for quantitative power or cost analysis at the reference-model level.</data>
      <data key="d9">The Next Steps section of Reference [5] mentioned adding parametrics for power, weight, and cost. They have not been added since they are more appropriate for a physical model.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[35].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0077::limitation-13", "study_id": "paper-0077"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0077" target="limitationflag::prototype_or_future_work" id="e0004322">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">prototype_or_future_work</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper presents an interim status/reference model that is mature for validation but still pending validation and OMG candidate specification submission.</data>
      <data key="d9">The CSRM is sufficiently mature for validation to be accomplished followed by submission to OMG for candidate normative specification.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[35].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0077::limitation-01", "study_id": "paper-0077"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0077" target="limitationflag::single_case_or_limited_scope" id="e0004323">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[]</data>
      <data key="d7">single_case_or_limited_scope</data>
      <data key="d8">The CSRM is a sandbox/reference model, not a fully populated mission model; mission-specific stakeholders, measures, use cases, requirements, and tailoring are left to each team.</data>
      <data key="d9">The CSRM is a repository for systems engineering artifacts. However, it is not pre-populated with specific stakeholders, technical measures, use cases, and requirements. That is the job of the mission-specific CubeSat team.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "limitation_present", "limitation_type": "controlled_flag", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[35].structured_limitations.limitation_assessments[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0077::limitation-02", "study_id": "paper-0077"}</data>
    </edge>
