      <data key="d8">The method explicitly covers early Phase A/B requirement/model iterations, later onboard/flight software development, HIL/FM testing, and an operational target for generated software; operations are a downstream target, not operational evidence.</data>
      <data key="d9">In this step, detailed technical requirements are developed, and integrated system models including requirement model and ADCS models are built ... early development phase, i.e. Phase-A or B ... For each iteration, verification using SysM or executable SysML driven simulations shall be performed.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["medium"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[37].extraction.study_context_population.lifecycle_stage_addressed", "studies[37].structured_code_summary.study_context_population.lifecycle_stage_addressed"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0079::code-0013", "paper-0079::code-0128"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0079", "value_index": 1}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0079" target="approachclass::integrated_mbse_digital_engineering" id="e0001683">
      <data key="d5">HAS_APPROACH_CLASS</data>
      <data key="d6">implementation_pathway_tailoring.approach_classification</data>
      <data key="d7">Integrated MBSE/digital engineering</data>
      <data key="d8">The described environment links SysML requirements, executable simulation, MATLAB/Simulink, generated C code, code verification, HIL/FM integration, and testing.</data>
      <data key="d9">A collaborative MBSE workspace/environment is provided. This workspace integrates discipline-specific models capable of performing all aspects of the system definition. With proper construction of Simulink models and wrap-up of engineering model and flight model of onboard software, this workspace even allows a seamless integration of requirement development, model verification, code automatic generation and verification with high efficiency and quality.</data>
      <data key="d10">medium</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["medium"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[37].extraction.implementation_pathway_tailoring.approach_classification", "studies[37].structured_code_summary.implementation_pathway_tailoring.approach_classification"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0079::code-0048", "paper-0079::code-0163"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0079", "value_index": 1}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0079" target="paper-0079::claim-01" id="e0002204">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">SysML supports more structured and transparent nanosatellite requirements development and verification, with improved traceability and consistency.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">System requirements are derived by means of the following sequence of suggested activities ... Derive system requirements from mission requirements, Use Cases, system context diagram mission phases diagram and functional analysis ... Model 'derived', 'trace', or 'Refine' relations when applicable in new requirements diagrams.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0079::claim-01", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_path": "studies[37].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0079::claim-01", "study_id": "paper-0079"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0079" target="paper-0079::claim-02" id="e0002205">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Executable SysML connected to MATLAB/Simulink can automatically verify an ADCS design requirement before hardware by running simulations and updating requirement status.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">ADCSF.34 is connected to a constraint block by means of 'refine' relationship. This is the way SysML adopts indicate that a requirement can be analyzed executi parametric models.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0079::claim-02", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_path": "studies[37].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0079::claim-02", "study_id": "paper-0079"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0079" target="paper-0079::claim-03" id="e0002206">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Model sharing between MBSE and MDE reuses early ADCS models for onboard software development and allows engineers to focus more on models than programming.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">From the case study of DelFFi, it can be observed that the key of both MBSE and MDE-based onboard software development is the model. Therefore a bridge between MBSE and onboard software development can be built up through model sharing.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0079::claim-03", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_path": "studies[37].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0079::claim-03", "study_id": "paper-0079"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0079" target="paper-0079::claim-04" id="e0002207">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Automatic generation from executable Simulink solutions and consistency between simulation models and onboard software should improve code/product quality and reliability.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">If the Simulink Solution works well and the AOCS/GNC algorithms have been executed so far with desirable results in simulation, the C code be generated directly from an executable Simulink Solution. On this basis, the Onboard Software is ready for testing and after some necessary items will be the exact software running in operation.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0079::claim-04", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_path": "studies[37].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0079::claim-04", "study_id": "paper-0079"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0079" target="paper-0079::claim-05" id="e0002208">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Reusable Simulink model libraries and flexible configurations enable quick response to changing requirements and reduce design time.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">This is basically a set of libraries which collect the MATLAB/Simulink models, including the spacecraft hardware (sensors/actuators), kinematics dynamics, the space environment, as well as some generic functions and algorithms.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0079::claim-05", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_path": "studies[37].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0079::claim-05", "study_id": "paper-0079"}</data>
    </edge>
