    <edge source="paper-0079" target="limitationflag::ad_hoc_simulation_wrapper_needed" id="e0004339">
      <data key="d5">HAS_LIMITATION</data>
      <data key="d6">structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[]</data>
      <data key="d7">ad-hoc-simulation-wrapper-needed</data>
      <data key="d8">Many simulation variables could not be cleanly assigned to existing model elements, so an ad-hoc ADCS4simulation block was created.</data>
      <data key="d9">Since many different variables were found to be influencing the outcome the simulation, and since it was not possible to directly associate all these quantities to a unique model element, an ad-hoc block was created. This block's name is 'ADCS4simulation', and it wraps all simulation variables and parameters.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[37].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0079::limitation-17", "study_id": "paper-0079"}</data>
    </edge>
