      <data key="d7">ambiguous-requirement-relation-semantics</data>
      <data key="d8">The authors observed ambiguity between containment, derive, and trace relations.</data>
      <data key="d9">The reported work flow aims at being a general recipe indeed, but the way a relation is modeled, strongly depends upon the specific case ... little difference was found between the use of ... a containment relationship, instead of a derive relationship. The trace relationship also appeared be suitable in some cases ... This ambiguity did not represent a problem though.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"assessment": "emergent_limitation", "limitation_type": "emergent_limitation", "source": "author_stated", "source_path": "studies[37].structured_limitations.emergent_limitations[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0079::limitation-14", "study_id": "paper-0079"}</data>
