    <edge source="paper-0080" target="paper-0080::claim-01" id="e0002210">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">MBSE/SysML improves consistency, traceability, V&amp;V, and change-impact assessment compared with document/tool-spread traditional SE.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">MBSE provides a consistent and automatically traceable system design, which enhances the quality of traceability and change impact assessment.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0080::claim-01", "source_claim_id": "C1", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[0]", "source_record_id": "paper-0080::claim-01", "study_id": "paper-0080"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0080" target="paper-0080::claim-02" id="e0002211">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">SysML parametric constraints linked to requirements verify NSS-1 mass and power budget margins before physical development.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">After connecting the parameter ports to respective inputs and outputs, we validated the model using ParaMagic.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0080::claim-02", "source_claim_id": "C2", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[1]", "source_record_id": "paper-0080::claim-02", "study_id": "paper-0080"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0080" target="paper-0080::claim-03" id="e0002212">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Connecting SysML to Excel and MATLAB/Simulink enables interoperability and on-the-fly parameter tuning using existing SE tools.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">Seamless interface of existing system-level design tools (Satellite Tool Kit [STK], matrix laboratory [MATLAB]/ Simulink, and Microsoft Excel) with the SysML satellite model to assist on-the-fly parameter tuning</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0080::claim-03", "source_claim_id": "C3", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[2]", "source_record_id": "paper-0080::claim-03", "study_id": "paper-0080"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0080" target="paper-0080::claim-04" id="e0002213">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">The NSS-1 model repository supports reuse, generic nanosatellite patterns, and knowledge transfer to future missions such as NSS-2.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">We reused some model elements from the FireSat SysML model</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0080::claim-04", "source_claim_id": "C4", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[3]", "source_record_id": "paper-0080::claim-04", "study_id": "paper-0080"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0080" target="paper-0080::claim-05" id="e0002214">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Automatic report/table/code generation from SysML supports automated systems engineering and downstream simulation/software implementation.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">from SysML models, an allocation table, a requirement table, and coverage analysis are generated automatically from the model repository</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0080::claim-05", "source_claim_id": "C5", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[4]", "source_record_id": "paper-0080::claim-05", "study_id": "paper-0080"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0080" target="paper-0080::claim-06" id="e0002215">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Extensible SysML structures reduced model development time and are expected to reduce future cost to change designs.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">We have also adopted design techniques for creating extensible system structures. This practice reduced the model development time. In the future, this will also reduce the cost to change the design</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0080::claim-06", "source_claim_id": "C6", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[5]", "source_record_id": "paper-0080::claim-06", "study_id": "paper-0080"}</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0080" target="paper-0080::claim-07" id="e0002216">
      <data key="d5">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d6">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d7">Overall MBSE approach is promising for reduced development risk, improved quality, and increased productivity.</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d9">The model-based approach is found to be promising for a reduced development risk, improved quality, and increased productivity.</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11">{"claim_id": "paper-0080::claim-07", "source_claim_id": "C7", "source_path": "studies[38].extraction.claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[6]", "source_record_id": "paper-0080::claim-07", "study_id": "paper-0080"}</data>
    </edge>
