    <edge source="paper-0081" target="reusemechanism::high_level_abstraction" id="e0005752">
      <data key="d5">HAS_REUSE_MECHANISM</data>
      <data key="d6">mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism</data>
      <data key="d7">high-level abstraction</data>
      <data key="d8">The paper supports cross-mission reuse through reusable baselines/templates, reference/model patterns, functional libraries, and an automated Capella/Python4Capella workflow. The reusable architecture is high-level and mission-agnostic enough to be imported and extended for mission-specific elements, and interfaces/exchanges are a central organizing mechanism. Do not retain low-dynamics / non-detailed-behavior model: the paper uses functional abstraction, but does not explicitly make low-dynamics or non-detailed behavior a reuse mechanism.</data>
      <data key="d9">An automated framework was developed to support fast, consistent deployment of satellite digital models across missions, leveraging standard solutions and use cases.</data>
      <data key="d10">high</data>
      <data key="d11">{"confidences": ["high"], "source_path": null, "source_paths": ["studies[39].extraction.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism", "studies[39].structured_code_summary.mbse_objective_scope_artifacts.generality_reuse_mechanism"], "source_record_id": null, "source_record_ids": ["paper-0081::code-0039", "paper-0081::code-0148"], "source_sections": ["extraction", "structured_code_summary"], "status": "coded", "statuses": ["coded"], "study_id": "paper-0081", "value_index": 7}</data>
